ph/src/locate/membership.rs`:\n  - Removed the `hybrid_root` short-circuit → the hybrid-root test failed as expected.\n  - Made the empty-globset case fall through to admit-all → both tests failed as expected.\n  - Restored the original code (verified `git diff` on membership.rs was empty afterward).\n- Full `callisto-graph` lib suite: 289 passed, 0 failed. `cargo fmt` and `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings` both clean.\n- Committed as `98cb1e2`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"TASK-17\",\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"confirmed prior 12 commits present and tree clean\",\n    \"read AC-10b acceptance criterion text directly from spec file on disk\",\n    \"identified plan fixture omitted spec's hybrid-root exemption clause and added a second test to cover it\",\n    \"wrote both tests (red-step check: passed immediately, consistent with prior regression-proof tasks in this range)\",\n    \"adversarially verified non-vacuousness by breaking hybrid_root short-circuit and empty-globset behavior in membership.rs, confirming each test failed appropriately, then restored original code\",\n    \"ran full callisto-graph lib test suite (289 passed)\",\n    \"ran cargo fmt -p callisto-graph and cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings (clean)\",\n    \"committed\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"98cb1e2\",\n  \"criteria_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-10b\",\n      \"test_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 817,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 230\n    }\n  ],\n  \"concerns\": \"No genuine red step occurred (consistent with TASK-07 through TASK-16 in this plan); non-vacuousness was verified via adversarial mutation instead, per the task's own instructions. The plan's original fixture only covered the zero-npm-entries half of AC-10b; I added a second test (ac10b_pnpm_empty_packages_list_still_admits_hybrid_root, line 842) to cover the hybrid-root exemption clause explicitly named in the spec's criterion text, which the plan's fixture omitted.\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Spec AC-10b text explicitly carves out an AC-17-style hybrid-root exemption from its zero-entries claim. The plan's single fixture (no root package.json) never exercises that carve-out, so a literal reading of the plan alone would under-prove the criterion. Added a second fixture with a root package.json declaring 'name' to prove the exemption holds. Verified both tests are meaningful via targeted mutation of NpmMembership::admits before committing.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>85136</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>23</tool_uses><duration_ms>505568</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"4a8a8b40-e3bd-4925-8006-b45559511a4b","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:51:08.035Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.232","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
