{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T02:59:07.797Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a21d31ea63cdb4b30</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/5e79b5c6-5688-4728-8d81-ff2c106a0e2e/tasks/a21d31ea63cdb4b30.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement TASK-27 (AC-11 regression test)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Summary\n\n**TASK-27** (AC-11: malformed pnpm YAML, no package.json workspaces field present) — completed.\n\nConfirmed all 22 prior commits (0971005..24740e2) present and tree clean before starting.\n\n**Spec vs plan discrepancy found and corrected**: The plan's fixture omitted a root `package.json` entirely, but AC-11's exact spec text (read from `.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK3A-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP.json`) specifies \"a root package.json with no 'workspaces' field\" — i.e., the file must exist but lack the field. I verified in `membership.rs` that file-absent and field-absent are behaviorally equivalent (both fall through to `None` via `?`-chains), but wrote the test to match the spec's literal scenario rather than the plan's looser one, adding `std::fs::write(root.join(\"package.json\"), r#\"{\"name\":\"root\"}\"#)`.\n\nAs predicted by the \"regression-proof\" pattern (matching TASK-07 through TASK-26), the test passed immediately with no implementation change needed — behavior already existed. Per the established adversarial-verification precedent, I temporarily broke `read_pnpm_packages` in `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs` (made malformed YAML return `Some(Vec::new())` instead of falling through to `None`), confirmed the test failed with a clear assertion panic, then restored the original code (verified via `git diff --stat` showing zero diff on membership.rs).\n\nRan `cargo fmt -p callisto-graph`, full `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib` (307 passed), and `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings` (clean) before committing.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"TASK-27\",\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"verified 22 prior commits present and tree clean\",\n    \"read AC-11 exact criterion text from spec file on disk\",\n    \"found and fixed plan fixture gap (missing root package.json without workspaces field)\",\n    \"wrote test, ran it, confirmed pass (no red step, as expected for regression-proof)\",\n    \"adversarially broke membership.rs read_pnpm_packages, confirmed test fails\",\n    \"restored membership.rs to original (zero diff)\",\n    \"confirmed test green again\",\n    \"ran cargo fmt, full test suite (307 passed), clippy -D warnings (clean)\",\n    \"committed\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"f93e5aa\",\n  \"criteria_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-11\",\n      \"test_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 1013,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 255\n    }\n  ],\n  \"concerns\": \"Plan's failing_test fixture for TASK-27 omitted the root package.json file that AC-11's spec text explicitly requires (file present, workspaces field absent, as distinct from file entirely absent). Corrected in the committed test; no functional bug found (file-absent and field-absent are both handled by the same ?-chain fallback in read_package_json_workspaces), but the fixture now matches the spec's literal scenario rather than a behaviorally-equivalent-but-textually-different one.\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"No implementation change required; existing fallback logic in read_npm_membership/read_pnpm_packages already implements AC-11 correctly, confirmed via mutation-style break/restore rather than assumption.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>60039</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>22</tool_uses><duration_ms>414564</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
