{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:46:59.093Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af27e814ddc2e2bb4</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/af27e814ddc2e2bb4.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Draft SPEC-TRACK1 fixed-group cascade spec\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I drafted the spec@1 and wrote it to `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track1-draft.json` for reference. This is the drafter's output only — it has not gone through verify/audit/gate, and per the canon orchestration contract I did not write it into `.claude/specs/` or set `spec_file_path` (that happens only after exit-gate passes).\n\nHere is the complete spec@1 JSON object:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Wire three already-implemented but currently disconnected/broken pieces of callisto's fixed-group version engine into the real command call paths: (1) make fixed-group siblings converge on a single shared group-aligned target version instead of each bumping independently from its own base, by having cascade.rs's raise()/bump_target use the existing fixed_group_target function; (2) call the existing, fully-implemented pre_mutation_checks divergence/napi-drift detector from callisto-graph's real version-command orchestration path, before mutation, and actually consume its result (merge diagnostics, abort on divergence error); (3) add cross-group conflict detection to GroupTable::resolve so that two differently-spelled group members that resolve to the same PackageId across two different groups produce GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership instead of silently overwriting one group's claim with the other's.\",\n  \"scope\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs (CascadeInput struct, raise(), bump_target call site); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (plan_version's internal orchestration: TagIndex/NapiTargetsIndex bindings, pre_mutation_checks call, diagnostics merge, CascadeInput construction at line 70); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs (CascadeInput construction at line 53, mechanical update only); crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs (GroupTable::resolve, private fn at line 135). Both real CascadeInput construction sites in the codebase are covered; no other command constructs CascadeInput.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"Track 2 (platform-manifest / optionalDependencies writes) — separate track, depends on this one, not addressed here.\",\n    \"Track 9 (cascade_action peer-escalation severity bug, dependency-spec rewrite key bug) — separate, scoped track sharing cascade.rs, sequenced immediately after this one, not part of this spec.\",\n    \"Any change to fixed_group_target's or pre_mutation_checks's own internal logic/signature beyond what's needed to call them from real code — both are already correct; this track is about wiring, not redesigning them. (Note: unlike pre_mutation_checks, fixed_group_target has no pre-existing dedicated unit test as of this spec — see reasoning. This spec does not add one as a separate task; the real-call-path tests required by AC-002 and AC-004 exercise fixed_group_target indirectly, which is the coverage this spec commits to. Adding an isolated unit test for fixed_group_target directly is out of scope, not because it's undesirable, but because this spec's contract is about the real call path being fixed and tested, not about backfilling unit-test coverage for a helper that was already correct.)\",\n    \"GroupTable::resolve's other existing responsibilities and error paths beyond the new ConflictingGroupMembership detection — do not refactor unrelated parts of resolve() as a side effect.\",\n    \"Calling pre_mutation_checks from commands/snapshot.rs's plan_snapshot. Reason: plan_snapshot assigns the identical synthetic `0.0.0-&lt;tag&gt;-&lt;sha&gt;` version to every package in the workspace unconditionally (snapshot.rs, `snapshot_versions.insert(pkg.id.clone(), snapshot_ver.clone())` runs for every package regardless of severity or group membership) — there is no divergence between real, distinct release targets for pre_mutation_checks to catch in snapshot mode, since no package ever gets a distinct real target version during a snapshot run. Wiring pre_mutation_checks into snapshot.rs would be a no-op check against synthetic data, not a meaningful protection. This exclusion is a stated design decision (see AC-006), not a silent omission.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"CascadeInput.tags\",\n      \"signature\": \"pub tags: &amp;'a TagIndex\",\n      \"description\": \"New field added to the CascadeInput struct (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, currently 8 fields: graph, groups, cfg, seed, reasons, named_by, base, pre — none named tags). Required so that raise()'s per-sibling fixed-group loop can call fixed_group_target(sib, tags, ...) instead of calling bump_target independently on each sibling. Both real construction sites must supply it: commands/version.rs:70 (plan_version) and commands/snapshot.rs:53 (plan_snapshot). TagIndex is defined in crates/callisto-graph/src/tags.rs and exposes last_tag(&amp;self, id: &amp;PackageId) -&gt; Option&lt;&amp;LastTag&gt; and an empty() constructor for tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"cascade::raise (internal, per-sibling fixed-group loop)\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn raise&lt;D: DependencyResolver&gt;(input: &amp;CascadeInput&lt;D&gt;, ...) -&gt; ... (signature unchanged; internal logic changes only)\",\n      \"description\": \"The fixed-group loop at lines 464-478 currently computes each sibling's target by calling bump_target(sib, sev, input) directly against that sibling's own base version. This spec changes that loop to compute the shared group-aligned target once (via crate::groups::fixed_group_target, using input.tags) and assign that same target to every sibling in the group, instead of bumping each sibling independently. raise() is shared by both run_cascade call paths (version.rs and snapshot.rs via solve_cascade), so this fix applies to both commands mechanically — see AC-004/AC-005.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"commands::version::plan_version (internal orchestration change; external signature unchanged)\",\n      \"signature\": \"pub fn plan_version(...) -&gt; Result&lt;VersionPlan, GraphError&gt;\",\n      \"description\": \"External signature and return type are unchanged. Internally, plan_version gains: (a) a local `tags` binding capturing the TagIndex currently only produced inline as an unbound argument to aggregate() at line 43 (e.g. `let tags = ws.tags()?;`); (b) a newly-constructed NapiTargetsIndex, which does not exist anywhere in plan_version today (e.g. `NapiTargetsIndex::load(&amp;ws.config.groups, ws.root)?`); (c) a call to crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks(...) using base_versions (already bound at line 27), ws.config.groups (already in scope), the new tags binding, and the new NapiTargetsIndex, executed before run_cascade; (d) merging of the returned GroupCheckOutcome.diagnostics into the existing `diagnostics` collection (bound at line 203, passed through escalate() at line 219) so they appear in the final VersionPlan.diagnostics; (e) propagating pre_mutation_checks's Err(GraphError::FixedGroupDivergent | GraphError::GroupGrammarMismatch) as plan_version's own Err result, aborting before run_cascade executes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"config::groups::GroupTable::resolve\",\n      \"signature\": \"pub(crate) fn resolve(raw: &amp;RawGroupTable, index: &amp;IdentityIndex) -&gt; Result&lt;GroupTable, GraphError&gt;\",\n      \"description\": \"Signature unchanged. Internal logic gains cross-group conflict detection: while building the fixed_of/linked_of maps (currently populated via unchecked .insert() calls that silently overwrite an existing entry), if a PackageId being inserted for group G2 already has an entry recorded for a different group G1, resolve() returns Err(GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership { package, groups }) where `package` is the shared resolved PackageId and `groups` lists the conflicting group names (at least G1 and G2), instead of completing the insert and returning Ok.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-001\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a Fixed group with two Package members — one already released with a prior tag at version 2.0.0, one never-released at version 0.1.0 — and a cascade run where both siblings are assigned a Minor severity bump, both siblings' computed target version (as observed in the resulting VersionPlan/cascade output) are the identical group-aligned version derived from the released sibling's tag-based version via fixed_group_target, not two independently-bumped versions computed from each sibling's own base version.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-002\",\n      \"criterion\": \"The behavior in AC-001 is observable through the real, live call path crate::cascade::run_cascade -&gt; raise() -&gt; the per-sibling fixed-group loop -&gt; the shared-target computation, exercised end-to-end by a test that invokes run_cascade (or commands::version::plan_version, which calls it) rather than a test that calls fixed_group_target directly in isolation.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-003\",\n      \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-graph builds successfully after CascadeInput gains a `tags: &amp;TagIndex` field, with both real construction sites updated to supply it: commands/version.rs's plan_version (line 70's CascadeInput construction) and commands/snapshot.rs's plan_snapshot (line 53's CascadeInput construction). `cargo build -p callisto-graph` (or the workspace equivalent via `just ci` / `moon run :test`) completes with no compilation errors referencing either file.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-004\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given the same Fixed-group two-sibling scenario as AC-001, running it through commands::snapshot::plan_snapshot's call path (run_cascade -&gt; raise(), the same shared code as version.rs's path) also produces the identical shared group-aligned target for both siblings at the cascade-computation stage, confirming the fix in raise()/bump_target is not duplicated or version.rs-only, since raise() is one shared function used by both commands.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-005\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a workspace with Fixed-group members, running plan_snapshot before and after this fix produces the identical snapshot_versions output: every package in the workspace is assigned the same synthetic `0.0.0-&lt;tag&gt;-&lt;sha&gt;` version string, unconditional on severity or fixed-group membership. This fix does not change plan_snapshot's observable version output for any package — it only changes the internal cascade-stage target computation exercised by AC-004, which snapshot.rs's synthetic versioning step subsequently overrides for every package uniformly.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-006\",\n      \"criterion\": \"commands::version::plan_version does not call crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks anywhere in its call path — that wiring is scoped to commands/version.rs's real orchestration only, per this spec's non_goals, with the stated reason that snapshot mode never produces distinct real target versions for pre_mutation_checks to evaluate.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-007\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a base_versions/TagIndex/NapiTargetsIndex combination for which crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks's existing logic returns Err(GraphError::FixedGroupDivergent) or Err(GraphError::GroupGrammarMismatch) (using the same input conditions that already trigger these outcomes in pre_mutation_checks's existing unit test), running the real `callisto version` command (commands::version::plan_version) returns that same GraphError variant as its own Err result, and run_cascade never executes (no VersionPlan with a cascade-computed target is produced) — the divergence check aborts the command rather than being silently discarded.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-008\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a base_versions/TagIndex/NapiTargetsIndex combination for which pre_mutation_checks succeeds and returns a GroupCheckOutcome with one or more non-empty diagnostics, running commands::version::plan_version produces a VersionPlan whose `diagnostics` field contains those same diagnostic entries (in addition to any diagnostics plan_version already produces, e.g. EmptyChangeset), confirming the diagnostics are merged into the real output rather than discarded.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-009\",\n      \"criterion\": \"commands::version::plan_version constructs a TagIndex (via a newly-bound local variable, distinct from the existing inline, unbound `ws.tags()?` call passed directly as an argument to aggregate()) and a NapiTargetsIndex (via NapiTargetsIndex::load or equivalent — no such construction exists in plan_version prior to this fix), and passes both to pre_mutation_checks and, for the tags value, to CascadeInput's new `tags` field.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-010\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given two group definitions in a workspace's raw TOML group config where a member is spelled differently in each (e.g. group A lists \\\"my-lib\\\", group B lists \\\"cargo:my-lib\\\") but both spellings resolve, via the IdentityIndex, to the same real PackageId, GroupTable::resolve returns Err(GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership { package, groups }) where `package` equals that shared resolved PackageId and `groups` contains the names of both conflicting groups (A and B).\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-011\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a workspace group config where a single PackageId legitimately belongs to exactly one group (the ordinary, allowed case — no other group claims the same resolved id), GroupTable::resolve returns Ok(..) for that config and GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership is not constructed anywhere during that resolve() call.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-012\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a workspace config with no group spelling conflicts (the pre-existing, unmodified test fixtures used by GroupTable::resolve's current test suite), GroupTable::resolve's output is unchanged from its pre-fix behavior — all existing group-resolution tests pass unmodified after this fix, with no test assertions altered to accommodate the new conflict-detection logic.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-013\",\n      \"criterion\": \"The test suite added for this spec includes at least one test per bug that exercises the real call path rather than only the pre-existing helper function in isolation: bug 1 via a test invoking crate::cascade::run_cascade (or a command that calls it, e.g. plan_version or plan_snapshot) and asserting on its output, not merely a direct unit-test call to fixed_group_target; bug 2 via a test invoking commands::version::plan_version and asserting on its Err/diagnostics output, not merely a direct unit-test call to pre_mutation_checks; bug 3 via a test invoking GroupTable::resolve with a full RawGroupTable/IdentityIndex pair reflecting realistic TOML-parsed config, not a synthetic direct construction of internal maps that bypasses resolve()'s own entry point.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Incorporated all ten verified corrections: (1) fixed_group_target has zero pre-existing unit tests, contrary to the requirement's blanket claim that both helpers 'already have their own isolated unit tests today' — I scoped that claim in non_goals to pre_mutation_checks only and explicitly noted the test gap for fixed_group_target rather than repeating the requirement's inaccurate claim; AC-002 and AC-013 make clear that real-call-path testing is what closes this gap, not a new isolated unit test (kept out of scope deliberately, stated with reason). (2) pre_mutation_checks's exact signature is reflected in AC-007/AC-008/AC-009 and the api_surface entry for plan_version. (3) GroupTable::resolve's confirmed silent-overwrite-on-insert behavior is the exact mechanism AC-010/AC-011/AC-012 target. (4) CascadeInput's confirmed 8-field shape (no tags field) grounds the api_surface entry and AC-003; I avoided inventing types for cfg/seed/reasons/named_by/pre since those weren't verified and aren't touched by this spec. (5) Confirmed construction sites at version.rs:70 and snapshot.rs:53, and confirmed apply.rs constructs neither — matches AC-003 exactly, and I did not add any apply.rs-related criterion. (6) raise()'s shared-code-path nature (used by both run_cascade callers) grounds AC-004 and AC-005 — I treated the snapshot.rs mechanical fix and its lack of observable-output change as two separate, both-necessary criteria rather than collapsing them, since a developer needs both the compile-fix confirmation and the no-behavior-change confirmation to know they haven't accidentally changed snapshot output. (7) version.rs's real diagnostics collection/escalate() path grounds AC-008. (8) The snapshot.rs pre_mutation_checks exclusion is stated as both a non_goal (with the synthetic-version reason spelled out) and a positive, testable AC-006 confirming the exclusion is real and intentional rather than an accidental gap — I chose to state it in both places since the instructions asked for it to be explicit and testable, not silently absent, and a non_goal alone isn't independently verifiable by a tester without a corresponding criterion. (9) GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership's exact field shape (package: PackageId, groups: Vec&lt;GroupName&gt; — singular package, not 'both groups and the shared id' as separate items) is reflected precisely in AC-010's wording. (10) TagIndex's type and location grounds the api_surface entry for CascadeInput.tags. Judgment call: I did not include a criterion demanding a *new* isolated unit test for fixed_group_target, since the out_of_scope item 'any change to fixed_group_target's...internal logic/signature beyond what's needed to call it from real code' reads as covering test-scaffolding-only additions as optional-but-not-required; I made this explicit in non_goals rather than leaving it ambiguous, since the corrections flagged it as a point that must not be silently glossed. Judgment call: AC-013 is a meta-criterion about test methodology rather than pure system behavior; I kept it because the requirement's done_when explicitly demands it and a tester CAN confirm it by reading the test suite and observing which entry points each test calls — it remains an externally-confirmable proposition about the artifact (the test suite), not an internal implementation-assumption criterion.\"\n}\n```\n\nThis is a first-draft `spec@1` — it has not yet passed through canon's verify/audit/exit-gate pipeline, so `spec_file_path` is intentionally unset. The reference copy lives at `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track1-draft.json`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>43015</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>3</tool_uses><duration_ms>161225</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:46:59.122Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af27e814ddc2e2bb4</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/af27e814ddc2e2bb4.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Draft SPEC-TRACK1 fixed-group cascade spec\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I drafted the spec@1 and wrote it to `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track1-draft.json` for reference. This is the drafter's output only — it has not gone through verify/audit/gate, and per the canon orchestration contract I did not write it into `.claude/specs/` or set `spec_file_path` (that happens only after exit-gate passes).\n\nHere is the complete spec@1 JSON object:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Wire three already-implemented but currently disconnected/broken pieces of callisto's fixed-group version engine into the real command call paths: (1) make fixed-group siblings converge on a single shared group-aligned target version instead of each bumping independently from its own base, by having cascade.rs's raise()/bump_target use the existing fixed_group_target function; (2) call the existing, fully-implemented pre_mutation_checks divergence/napi-drift detector from callisto-graph's real version-command orchestration path, before mutation, and actually consume its result (merge diagnostics, abort on divergence error); (3) add cross-group conflict detection to GroupTable::resolve so that two differently-spelled group members that resolve to the same PackageId across two different groups produce GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership instead of silently overwriting one group's claim with the other's.\",\n  \"scope\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs (CascadeInput struct, raise(), bump_target call site); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (plan_version's internal orchestration: TagIndex/NapiTargetsIndex bindings, pre_mutation_checks call, diagnostics merge, CascadeInput construction at line 70); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs (CascadeInput construction at line 53, mechanical update only); crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs (GroupTable::resolve, private fn at line 135). Both real CascadeInput construction sites in the codebase are covered; no other command constructs CascadeInput.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"Track 2 (platform-manifest / optionalDependencies writes) — separate track, depends on this one, not addressed here.\",\n    \"Track 9 (cascade_action peer-escalation severity bug, dependency-spec rewrite key bug) — separate, scoped track sharing cascade.rs, sequenced immediately after this one, not part of this spec.\",\n    \"Any change to fixed_group_target's or pre_mutation_checks's own internal logic/signature beyond what's needed to call them from real code — both are already correct; this track is about wiring, not redesigning them. (Note: unlike pre_mutation_checks, fixed_group_target has no pre-existing dedicated unit test as of this spec — see reasoning. This spec does not add one as a separate task; the real-call-path tests required by AC-002 and AC-004 exercise fixed_group_target indirectly, which is the coverage this spec commits to. Adding an isolated unit test for fixed_group_target directly is out of scope, not because it's undesirable, but because this spec's contract is about the real call path being fixed and tested, not about backfilling unit-test coverage for a helper that was already correct.)\",\n    \"GroupTable::resolve's other existing responsibilities and error paths beyond the new ConflictingGroupMembership detection — do not refactor unrelated parts of resolve() as a side effect.\",\n    \"Calling pre_mutation_checks from commands/snapshot.rs's plan_snapshot. Reason: plan_snapshot assigns the identical synthetic `0.0.0-&lt;tag&gt;-&lt;sha&gt;` version to every package in the workspace unconditionally (snapshot.rs, `snapshot_versions.insert(pkg.id.clone(), snapshot_ver.clone())` runs for every package regardless of severity or group membership) — there is no divergence between real, distinct release targets for pre_mutation_checks to catch in snapshot mode, since no package ever gets a distinct real target version during a snapshot run. Wiring pre_mutation_checks into snapshot.rs would be a no-op check against synthetic data, not a meaningful protection. This exclusion is a stated design decision (see AC-006), not a silent omission.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"CascadeInput.tags\",\n      \"signature\": \"pub tags: &amp;'a TagIndex\",\n      \"description\": \"New field added to the CascadeInput struct (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, currently 8 fields: graph, groups, cfg, seed, reasons, named_by, base, pre — none named tags). Required so that raise()'s per-sibling fixed-group loop can call fixed_group_target(sib, tags, ...) instead of calling bump_target independently on each sibling. Both real construction sites must supply it: commands/version.rs:70 (plan_version) and commands/snapshot.rs:53 (plan_snapshot). TagIndex is defined in crates/callisto-graph/src/tags.rs and exposes last_tag(&amp;self, id: &amp;PackageId) -&gt; Option&lt;&amp;LastTag&gt; and an empty() constructor for tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"cascade::raise (internal, per-sibling fixed-group loop)\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn raise&lt;D: DependencyResolver&gt;(input: &amp;CascadeInput&lt;D&gt;, ...) -&gt; ... (signature unchanged; internal logic changes only)\",\n      \"description\": \"The fixed-group loop at lines 464-478 currently computes each sibling's target by calling bump_target(sib, sev, input) directly against that sibling's own base version. This spec changes that loop to compute the shared group-aligned target once (via crate::groups::fixed_group_target, using input.tags) and assign that same target to every sibling in the group, instead of bumping each sibling independently. raise() is shared by both run_cascade call paths (version.rs and snapshot.rs via solve_cascade), so this fix applies to both commands mechanically — see AC-004/AC-005.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"commands::version::plan_version (internal orchestration change; external signature unchanged)\",\n      \"signature\": \"pub fn plan_version(...) -&gt; Result&lt;VersionPlan, GraphError&gt;\",\n      \"description\": \"External signature and return type are unchanged. Internally, plan_version gains: (a) a local `tags` binding capturing the TagIndex currently only produced inline as an unbound argument to aggregate() at line 43 (e.g. `let tags = ws.tags()?;`); (b) a newly-constructed NapiTargetsIndex, which does not exist anywhere in plan_version today (e.g. `NapiTargetsIndex::load(&amp;ws.config.groups, ws.root)?`); (c) a call to crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks(...) using base_versions (already bound at line 27), ws.config.groups (already in scope), the new tags binding, and the new NapiTargetsIndex, executed before run_cascade; (d) merging of the returned GroupCheckOutcome.diagnostics into the existing `diagnostics` collection (bound at line 203, passed through escalate() at line 219) so they appear in the final VersionPlan.diagnostics; (e) propagating pre_mutation_checks's Err(GraphError::FixedGroupDivergent | GraphError::GroupGrammarMismatch) as plan_version's own Err result, aborting before run_cascade executes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"config::groups::GroupTable::resolve\",\n      \"signature\": \"pub(crate) fn resolve(raw: &amp;RawGroupTable, index: &amp;IdentityIndex) -&gt; Result&lt;GroupTable, GraphError&gt;\",\n      \"description\": \"Signature unchanged. Internal logic gains cross-group conflict detection: while building the fixed_of/linked_of maps (currently populated via unchecked .insert() calls that silently overwrite an existing entry), if a PackageId being inserted for group G2 already has an entry recorded for a different group G1, resolve() returns Err(GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership { package, groups }) where `package` is the shared resolved PackageId and `groups` lists the conflicting group names (at least G1 and G2), instead of completing the insert and returning Ok.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-001\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a Fixed group with two Package members — one already released with a prior tag at version 2.0.0, one never-released at version 0.1.0 — and a cascade run where both siblings are assigned a Minor severity bump, both siblings' computed target version (as observed in the resulting VersionPlan/cascade output) are the identical group-aligned version derived from the released sibling's tag-based version via fixed_group_target, not two independently-bumped versions computed from each sibling's own base version.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-002\",\n      \"criterion\": \"The behavior in AC-001 is observable through the real, live call path crate::cascade::run_cascade -&gt; raise() -&gt; the per-sibling fixed-group loop -&gt; the shared-target computation, exercised end-to-end by a test that invokes run_cascade (or commands::version::plan_version, which calls it) rather than a test that calls fixed_group_target directly in isolation.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-003\",\n      \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-graph builds successfully after CascadeInput gains a `tags: &amp;TagIndex` field, with both real construction sites updated to supply it: commands/version.rs's plan_version (line 70's CascadeInput construction) and commands/snapshot.rs's plan_snapshot (line 53's CascadeInput construction). `cargo build -p callisto-graph` (or the workspace equivalent via `just ci` / `moon run :test`) completes with no compilation errors referencing either file.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-004\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given the same Fixed-group two-sibling scenario as AC-001, running it through commands::snapshot::plan_snapshot's call path (run_cascade -&gt; raise(), the same shared code as version.rs's path) also produces the identical shared group-aligned target for both siblings at the cascade-computation stage, confirming the fix in raise()/bump_target is not duplicated or version.rs-only, since raise() is one shared function used by both commands.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-005\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a workspace with Fixed-group members, running plan_snapshot before and after this fix produces the identical snapshot_versions output: every package in the workspace is assigned the same synthetic `0.0.0-&lt;tag&gt;-&lt;sha&gt;` version string, unconditional on severity or fixed-group membership. This fix does not change plan_snapshot's observable version output for any package — it only changes the internal cascade-stage target computation exercised by AC-004, which snapshot.rs's synthetic versioning step subsequently overrides for every package uniformly.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-006\",\n      \"criterion\": \"commands::version::plan_version does not call crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks anywhere in its call path — that wiring is scoped to commands/version.rs's real orchestration only, per this spec's non_goals, with the stated reason that snapshot mode never produces distinct real target versions for pre_mutation_checks to evaluate.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-007\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a base_versions/TagIndex/NapiTargetsIndex combination for which crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks's existing logic returns Err(GraphError::FixedGroupDivergent) or Err(GraphError::GroupGrammarMismatch) (using the same input conditions that already trigger these outcomes in pre_mutation_checks's existing unit test), running the real `callisto version` command (commands::version::plan_version) returns that same GraphError variant as its own Err result, and run_cascade never executes (no VersionPlan with a cascade-computed target is produced) — the divergence check aborts the command rather than being silently discarded.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-008\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a base_versions/TagIndex/NapiTargetsIndex combination for which pre_mutation_checks succeeds and returns a GroupCheckOutcome with one or more non-empty diagnostics, running commands::version::plan_version produces a VersionPlan whose `diagnostics` field contains those same diagnostic entries (in addition to any diagnostics plan_version already produces, e.g. EmptyChangeset), confirming the diagnostics are merged into the real output rather than discarded.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-009\",\n      \"criterion\": \"commands::version::plan_version constructs a TagIndex (via a newly-bound local variable, distinct from the existing inline, unbound `ws.tags()?` call passed directly as an argument to aggregate()) and a NapiTargetsIndex (via NapiTargetsIndex::load or equivalent — no such construction exists in plan_version prior to this fix), and passes both to pre_mutation_checks and, for the tags value, to CascadeInput's new `tags` field.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-010\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given two group definitions in a workspace's raw TOML group config where a member is spelled differently in each (e.g. group A lists \\\"my-lib\\\", group B lists \\\"cargo:my-lib\\\") but both spellings resolve, via the IdentityIndex, to the same real PackageId, GroupTable::resolve returns Err(GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership { package, groups }) where `package` equals that shared resolved PackageId and `groups` contains the names of both conflicting groups (A and B).\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-011\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a workspace group config where a single PackageId legitimately belongs to exactly one group (the ordinary, allowed case — no other group claims the same resolved id), GroupTable::resolve returns Ok(..) for that config and GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership is not constructed anywhere during that resolve() call.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-012\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a workspace config with no group spelling conflicts (the pre-existing, unmodified test fixtures used by GroupTable::resolve's current test suite), GroupTable::resolve's output is unchanged from its pre-fix behavior — all existing group-resolution tests pass unmodified after this fix, with no test assertions altered to accommodate the new conflict-detection logic.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-013\",\n      \"criterion\": \"The test suite added for this spec includes at least one test per bug that exercises the real call path rather than only the pre-existing helper function in isolation: bug 1 via a test invoking crate::cascade::run_cascade (or a command that calls it, e.g. plan_version or plan_snapshot) and asserting on its output, not merely a direct unit-test call to fixed_group_target; bug 2 via a test invoking commands::version::plan_version and asserting on its Err/diagnostics output, not merely a direct unit-test call to pre_mutation_checks; bug 3 via a test invoking GroupTable::resolve with a full RawGroupTable/IdentityIndex pair reflecting realistic TOML-parsed config, not a synthetic direct construction of internal maps that bypasses resolve()'s own entry point.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Incorporated all ten verified corrections: (1) fixed_group_target has zero pre-existing unit tests, contrary to the requirement's blanket claim that both helpers 'already have their own isolated unit tests today' — I scoped that claim in non_goals to pre_mutation_checks only and explicitly noted the test gap for fixed_group_target rather than repeating the requirement's inaccurate claim; AC-002 and AC-013 make clear that real-call-path testing is what closes this gap, not a new isolated unit test (kept out of scope deliberately, stated with reason). (2) pre_mutation_checks's exact signature is reflected in AC-007/AC-008/AC-009 and the api_surface entry for plan_version. (3) GroupTable::resolve's confirmed silent-overwrite-on-insert behavior is the exact mechanism AC-010/AC-011/AC-012 target. (4) CascadeInput's confirmed 8-field shape (no tags field) grounds the api_surface entry and AC-003; I avoided inventing types for cfg/seed/reasons/named_by/pre since those weren't verified and aren't touched by this spec. (5) Confirmed construction sites at version.rs:70 and snapshot.rs:53, and confirmed apply.rs constructs neither — matches AC-003 exactly, and I did not add any apply.rs-related criterion. (6) raise()'s shared-code-path nature (used by both run_cascade callers) grounds AC-004 and AC-005 — I treated the snapshot.rs mechanical fix and its lack of observable-output change as two separate, both-necessary criteria rather than collapsing them, since a developer needs both the compile-fix confirmation and the no-behavior-change confirmation to know they haven't accidentally changed snapshot output. (7) version.rs's real diagnostics collection/escalate() path grounds AC-008. (8) The snapshot.rs pre_mutation_checks exclusion is stated as both a non_goal (with the synthetic-version reason spelled out) and a positive, testable AC-006 confirming the exclusion is real and intentional rather than an accidental gap — I chose to state it in both places since the instructions asked for it to be explicit and testable, not silently absent, and a non_goal alone isn't independently verifiable by a tester without a corresponding criterion. (9) GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership's exact field shape (package: PackageId, groups: Vec&lt;GroupName&gt; — singular package, not 'both groups and the shared id' as separate items) is reflected precisely in AC-010's wording. (10) TagIndex's type and location grounds the api_surface entry for CascadeInput.tags. Judgment call: I did not include a criterion demanding a *new* isolated unit test for fixed_group_target, since the out_of_scope item 'any change to fixed_group_target's...internal logic/signature beyond what's needed to call it from real code' reads as covering test-scaffolding-only additions as optional-but-not-required; I made this explicit in non_goals rather than leaving it ambiguous, since the corrections flagged it as a point that must not be silently glossed. Judgment call: AC-013 is a meta-criterion about test methodology rather than pure system behavior; I kept it because the requirement's done_when explicitly demands it and a tester CAN confirm it by reading the test suite and observing which entry points each test calls — it remains an externally-confirmable proposition about the artifact (the test suite), not an internal implementation-assumption criterion.\"\n}\n```\n\nThis is a first-draft `spec@1` — it has not yet passed through canon's verify/audit/exit-gate pipeline, so `spec_file_path` is intentionally unset. The reference copy lives at `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track1-draft.json`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>43015</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>3</tool_uses><duration_ms>161225</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
