a `tags: &TagIndex` field since fixed_group_target requires it. Both real construction sites are updated: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:70 and crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs:53.\",\n    \"Explicit decision, stated in the spec (not left ambiguous): whether commands/snapshot.rs's fixed-group target computation is brought into scope by this same fix or is explicitly out of scope with a stated reason.\",\n    \"crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks is called from commands/version.rs's real orchestration path, before run_cascade executes.\",\n    \"pre_mutation_checks's return value is actually consumed: diagnostics merged into real output, divergence errors actually abort the command.\",\n    \"GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership is constructed by new detection logic in GroupTable::resolve or an equivalent post-resolution check for the two-differently-spelled-groups-same-resolved-package case, and must NOT fire for the ordinary single-group-membership case.\",\n    \"Given a workspace config with no group spelling conflicts, GroupTable::resolve behaves exactly as it does today (regression: existing tests pass unmodified).\",\n    \"All three fixes are covered by tests that exercise the REAL call path, not just isolated unit tests of the already-existing helper functions.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"Track 2 (platform-manifest / optionalDependencies writes) -- separate track, depends on this one.\",\n    \"Track 9 (cascade_action peer-escalation severity bug, dependency-spec rewrite key bug) -- separate, scoped track sharing cascade.rs.\",\n    \"Any change to fixed_group_target's or pre_mutation_checks's own internal logic/signature beyond what's needed to call them from real code.\",\n    \"GroupTable::resolve's other existing responsibilities and error paths beyond the new ConflictingGroupMembership detection.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nRead the full spec@1 JSON from the file path above for the complete acceptance criteria text (my summary of AC-001 through AC-013 topics: shared group-aligned target computed via the real call path; CascadeInput gains tags field and both construction sites updated; snapshot.rs's in-scope/out-of-scope handling explicitly decided; pre_mutation_checks wired into version.rs with diagnostics merged and divergence errors aborting; TagIndex/NapiTargetsIndex newly bound locally in plan_version; ConflictingGroupMembership detection added to GroupTable::resolve without breaking the ordinary single-membership case; regression coverage for unmodified config; real-call-path test coverage for all three bugs).\n\nNo research-report@1 exists for this spec — the requirement's done_when criteria and the drafting agent's own code-verification (noted in its report: it corrected two inaccuracies in the requirement, confirmed exact line numbers and the ConflictingGroupMembership error shape) are the only source evidence available. Output a structured evidence report with supported, unsupported, and overfitted arrays plus a reasoning scratchpad.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/abbf8215ed309d35c.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b67bf904-e189-4183-a00d-67c7f5c82770","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
