{"parentUuid":"831b5de7-5d29-4866-adf0-2445d1612981","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8dFVq78oYn1L3mFNySw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017n4Ka7zygCmTP7oU8j3AuA","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Re-audit Track 1 spec after redraft","subagent_type":"canon:auditor","prompt":"Adversarially audit the revised spec@1 at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track1-draft.json (id SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS, callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto). Read the full spec fresh from disk, including its `revision_note` field which documents a substantial redraft after a prior canon-exit-gate FAIL (7 blockers, most critically that bug 1's fix was rescoped from raise()'s sibling loop to a new Fixed-group convergence block inside solve_cascade, mirroring an existing Linked-group block at cascade.rs:314-379).\n\nA canon-verifier pass just ran on this redraft and flagged something you need to weigh explicitly as part of your own judgment (not just re-check mechanically): three criteria — AC-004, AC-007b, AC-010c — trace their origin to gaps found during a PRIOR audit/exit-gate cycle rather than to the original source requirement's done_when list. In particular, AC-010c (requiring GroupTable::resolve to deduplicate a group's members when the same PackageId is reachable under two different spellings within one group) was flagged as potentially conflicting with the requirement's own out_of_scope item: \"GroupTable::resolve's other existing responsibilities and error paths beyond the new ConflictingGroupMembership detection.\" The spec's revision_note states this was intentionally addressed by both adding the dedup behavior to the GroupTable::resolve api_surface entry AND amending non_goals item 4 to carve out an explicit exception -- so the spec claims to be internally self-consistent now, but you should independently judge: is this dedup requirement a legitimate, necessary correctness precondition for the OTHER criteria in this same spec (AC-001/AC-002's fixed_group_target computation and AC-007's divergence detection both iterate a group's members via g.members(...) -- would an undeduplicated double-counted member corrupt those computations?), or is it real scope creep that should instead be split into a separate, explicitly-deferred follow-up item? Read groups.rs's fixed_group_target and pre_mutation_checks bodies yourself to make this judgment on real evidence, not assumption.\n\nCheck the standard five dimensions: untestable/vague acceptance criteria, ambiguous phrasing, missing error cases, scope overlap with other workspace specs (.claude/specs/ directory), and TBDs/incomplete sections. Pay special attention to whether the redrafted AC-001/AC-002 (now describing a NEW Fixed-group convergence block inside solve_cascade rather than a change to raise()) are internally consistent with the rest of the spec's scope/non_goals/api_surface sections, since this was the site of the most significant rewrite. For every issue found, produce a specific rewritten suggested_fix, not generic guidance. Output the standard JSON object with issues array and overall pass/fail verdict."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4324,"cache_read_input_tokens":391409,"output_tokens":4289,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2897},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4324,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4289,"cache_read_input_tokens":391409,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4324,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4324},"type":"message"}],"speed":