agIndex.\\\", \\\"is_error_case\\\": true}.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-008\",\n      \"type\": \"incomplete\",\n      \"description\": \"GroupCheckOutcome has two fields: new_members and diagnostics (crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:12-16). pre_mutation_checks populates new_members with each Fixed group's not-yet-released ('fresh') members whenever that list is non-empty (groups.rs:84-86). Grepping the workspace confirms new_members is never read anywhere in the codebase today. This spec's plan_version api_surface entry (d) wires up only `.diagnostics` ('merging of the returned GroupCheckOutcome.diagnostics into the existing diagnostics collection'); it says nothing about new_members. After this spec lands, new_members remains permanently write-only — populated by a real, now-reachable call site, but never consumed by anything. The spec neither states this is intentional (no non_goals entry) nor gives it a criterion, leaving a reader unable to tell whether the omission is a deliberate scope boundary or a missed requirement.\",\n      \"suggested_fix\": \"Add a new non_goals item: 'GroupCheckOutcome.new_members (the list of a Fixed group's not-yet-released members) is populated by pre_mutation_checks but intentionally not consumed by this spec's plan_version wiring — only GroupCheckOutcome.diagnostics is merged into VersionPlan.diagnostics. Surfacing new_members (e.g. as a diagnostic or changelog annotation marking a Fixed-group sibling's first release) is a distinct, additive behavior with no basis in REQ-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS's done_when list and is deferred to a follow-up track. This spec's wiring leaves new_members write-only by design, not by oversight.' If new_members surfacing was in fact intended, instead add: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"AC-015\\\", \\\"criterion\\\": \\\"Given a pre_mutation_checks call whose returned GroupCheckOutcome.new_members is non-empty for some group, running commands::version::plan_version produces a VersionPlan whose diagnostics field includes one Diagnostic per group listed in new_members, with &lt;exact DiagnosticCode and message format to be specified&gt;.\\\", \\\"is_error_case\\\": false} — but this alternative requires a concrete DiagnosticCode/message contract the auditor cannot supply without additional domain input, so if this path is chosen it must be authored by the spec owner, not guessed.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overall\": \"fail\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Verified every line number, signature, and error-variant claim in the spec against live source (groups.rs, config/groups.rs, cascade.rs, napi.rs, version.rs, snapshot.rs, error.rs, report.rs) rather than trusting the document's paraphrase; all checked out. The AC-001/AC-002 redraft is internally consistent with the new Fixed-group-convergence-block framing and correctly reflects the code (BTreeSet worklist, equality-gated insert, released[0] alignment base). The one issue the task specifically asked me to weigh — AC-010c's grounding — I resolved by tracing the actual dependent computations rather than accepting the spec's self-declared consistency: the dedup requirement is not load-bearing for any other criterion in this spec and should be split out. Three further concrete gaps surfaced during the standard five-dimension pass: an AC-003 compile-check loophole that would pass while breaking cascade.rs's own test module, an undocumented new fallible path introduced into plan_snapshot, and a newly-reachable-but-never-consumed GroupCheckOutcome field. No untestable/vague language, no unresolved TBDs, and no overlap with other workspace specs (Track3A/B and Track G touch disjoint files) were found.\"\n}\n```\n\nFiles read for this audit (all absolute paths):\n- `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track1-draft.json`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/s