{"parentUuid":"c925c577-58d4-4a48-b20b-aa69d9c3e4d6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1c3ca052-fa32-436c-9e66-711297eb18a9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Z49fdbAdCTiHpyKD4LNCn","type":"tool_result","content":"=== non_goals ===\n0 : Track 2 (platform-manifest / optionalDependencies writes) — separate track, depends on this one, not addressed here.\n1 : Track 9 (cascade_action peer-escalation severity bug, dependency-spec rewrite key bug) — separate, scoped track sharing cascade.rs, sequenced immediat\n2 : Any change to fixed_group_target's or pre_mutation_checks's own internal logic/signature beyond what's needed to call them from real code — both are a\n3 : GroupTable::resolve's other existing responsibilities and error paths beyond the new ConflictingGroupMembership detection — do not refactor unrelated \n4 : Calling pre_mutation_checks from commands/snapshot.rs's plan_snapshot. Reason: plan_snapshot assigns the identical synthetic `0.0.0-<tag>-<sha>` versi\n5 : fixed_group_target hardcodes callisto_format::SemVerVersioning unconditionally (groups.rs:137), unlike bump_target, which dispatches on base.grammar()\n6 : raise()'s pre-existing per-sibling fixed-group loop (cascade.rs:464-478), which independently calls bump_target for each sibling when a cascade-trigge\n=== AC-003 ===\ncrates/callisto-graph builds successfully after CascadeInput gains a `tags: &TagIndex` field, with both real construction sites updated to supply it: commands/version.rs's plan_version (line 70's CascadeInput construction) and commands/snapshot.rs's plan_snapshot (line 53's CascadeInput construction). `cargo build -p callisto-graph` (or the workspace equivalent via `just ci` / `moon run :test`) completes with no compilation errors referencing either file.\n=== AC-010c ===\nGiven a single Fixed (or single Linked) group definition in a workspace's raw TOML config that lists the same real PackageId twice under two different spellings within that one group (e.g. group A lists both \"my-lib\" and \"cargo:my-lib\", with no other group referencing that package), GroupTable::resolve returns Ok(..) -- a duplicate spelling within one group's own membership list is not a ConflictingGroupMembership error. group.members for that group contains the resolved PackageId's GroupMember::Package entry exactly once (not twice), because resolve() calls `members.dedup()` immediately after the existing `members.sort()` for that group's member list, removing the now-adjacent duplicate produced by two spellings resolving to the same PackageId.\n=== scope ===\n\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs (CascadeInput struct gains a `tags` field; solve_cascade gains a new Fixed-group convergence block added within the existing `while changed` fixpoint loop, positioned alongside the pre-existing Linked-group block at lines 314-379 and iterating input.groups.fixed.values() instead of input.groups.linked.values(); raise()'s existing per-sibling fixed-group loop at lines 464-478 is NOT modified by this spec \\u2014 see non_goals); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (plan_version's internal orchestration: TagIndex/NapiTargetsIndex bindings, pre_mutation_checks call with its real six-argument signature, diagnostics merge, CascadeInput construction at line 70); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs (CascadeInput construction at line 53, mechanical update only); crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs (GroupTable::resolve, private fn at line 135, gains cross-group conflict detection plus `.dedup()` calls after the existing `.sort()` calls at lines 164 and 195). Both real CascadeInput construction sites in the codebase are covered; no other command constructs CascadeInput.\"","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5487db7e-5a34-4829-a9cc-a90ee5d8932b","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:39:07.742Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== non_goals ===\n0 : Track 2 (platform-manifest / optionalDependencies writes) — separate track, depends on this one, not addressed here.\n1 : Track 9 (cascade_action peer-escalation severity bug, dependency-spec rewrite key bug) — separate, scoped track sharing cascade.rs, sequenced immediat\n2 : Any change to fixed_group_target's or pre_mutation_checks's own internal logic/signature beyond what's needed to call them from real code — both are a\n3 : GroupTable::resolve's other existing responsibilities and error paths beyond the new ConflictingGroupMembership detection — do not refactor unrelated \n4 : Calling pre_mutation_checks from commands/snapshot.rs's plan_snapshot. Reason: plan_snapshot assigns the identical synthetic `0.0.0-<tag>-<sha>` versi\n5 : fixed_group_target hardcodes callisto_format::SemVerVersioning unconditionally (groups.rs:137), unlike bump_target, which dispatches on base.grammar()\n6 : raise()'s pre-existing per-sibling fixed-group loop (cascade.rs:464-478), which independently calls bump_target for each sibling when a cascade-trigge\n=== AC-003 ===\ncrates/callisto-graph builds successfully after CascadeInput gains a `tags: &TagIndex` field, with both real construction sites updated to supply it: commands/version.rs's plan_version (line 70's CascadeInput construction) and commands/snapshot.rs's plan_snapshot (line 53's CascadeInput construction). `cargo build -p callisto-graph` (or the workspace equivalent via `just ci` / `moon run :test`) completes with no compilation errors referencing either file.\n=== AC-010c ===\nGiven a single Fixed (or single Linked) group definition in a workspace's raw TOML config that lists the same real PackageId twice under two different spellings within that one group (e.g. group A lists both \"my-lib\" and \"cargo:my-lib\", with no other group referencing that package), GroupTable::resolve returns Ok(..) -- a duplicate spelling within one group's own membership list is not a ConflictingGroupMembership error. group.members for that group contains the resolved PackageId's GroupMember::Package entry exactly once (not twice), because resolve() calls `members.dedup()` immediately after the existing `members.sort()` for that group's member list, removing the now-adjacent duplicate produced by two spellings resolving to the same PackageId.\n=== scope ===\n\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs (CascadeInput struct gains a `tags` field; solve_cascade gains a new Fixed-group convergence block added within the existing `while changed` fixpoint loop, positioned alongside the pre-existing Linked-group block at lines 314-379 and iterating input.groups.fixed.values() instead of input.groups.linked.values(); raise()'s existing per-sibling fixed-group loop at lines 464-478 is NOT modified by this spec \\u2014 see non_goals); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (plan_version's internal orchestration: TagIndex/NapiTargetsIndex bindings, pre_mutation_checks call with its real six-argument signature, diagnostics merge, CascadeInput construction at line 70); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs (CascadeInput construction at line 53, mechanical update only); crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs (GroupTable::resolve, private fn at line 135, gains cross-group conflict detection plus `.dedup()` calls after the existing `.sort()` calls at lines 164 and 195). Both real CascadeInput construction sites in the codebase are covered; no other command constructs CascadeInput.\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c925c577-58d4-4a48-b20b-aa69d9c3e4d6","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
