{"parentUuid":"8204e9ca-b6ab-4407-a6a5-c1de9e38382b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1c3ca052-fa32-436c-9e66-711297eb18a9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FUciSs4bXkeLbngKw4Zo9Q","type":"tool_result","content":"=== non_goals[3] full ===\nGroupTable::resolve's other existing responsibilities and error paths beyond the new ConflictingGroupMembership detection — do not refactor unrelated parts of resolve() as a side effect. EXCEPTION, carved out explicitly: the `.dedup()` calls added immediately after the existing `.sort()` calls at lines 164 and 195 (see AC-010c) are in scope and required — they are the mechanism that makes a duplicate spelling within one group's own membership list resolve to a single member instead of two, which is necessary for AC-010c to hold and is not itself a refactor of any other part of resolve().\n\n=== api_surface entries ===\n--- CascadeInput.tags ---\nNew field added to the CascadeInput struct (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, currently 8 fields: graph, groups, cfg, seed, reasons, named_by, base, pre — none named tags). Required so that the new Fixed-group convergence block in solve_cascade (see the api_surface entry below) can call crate::groups::fixed_group_target(g, input.base, &out.severities, input.tags, input.pre) instead of computing each Fixed-group member's target independently via bump_target. Both real construction sites must supply it: commands/version.rs:70 (plan_version) and commands/snapshot.rs:53 (plan_snapshot). TagIndex is defined in crates/callisto-graph/src/tags.rs and exposes last_tag(&self, id: &PackageId) -> Option<&LastTag> and an empty() constructor for tests.\n\n--- cascade::solve_cascade (new Fixed-group convergence block) ---\nFor each `g` in `input.groups.fixed.values()`: collect that group's Package member ids the same way the Linked-group block does (via `g.members(crate::config::GroupMemberKind::Package)` filtered to `GroupMember::Package`). Compute `max_sev` as the maximum of `out.severities.get(id)` over those member ids (defaulting absent entries to `Severity::None`), and for any member whose current severity in `out.severities` is below `max_sev`, raise it to `max_sev` (mirroring the Linked-group block's severity-union step) so severities stay consistent with the shared target about to be computed. If `max_sev > Severity::None`, call `crate::groups::fixed_group_target(g, input.base, &out.severities, input.tags, input.pre)` — the real five-argument signature (`g: &GroupDef, base: &BTreeMap<PackageId, Version>, severities: &BTreeMap<PackageId, Severity>, tags: &TagIndex, _pre: Option<&callisto_format::PreState>`) — exactly once per group per outer-loop iteration, propagating its `Result<Version, GraphError>` with `?`. For every member whose current `out.targets` entry differs from the returned `winner` version, insert `winner` into `out.targets`, set `out.reasons` to `BumpReason::FixedGroupUnion { group: g.name.clone() }`, insert the member id into `worklist`, and set the outer loop's `changed = true` (identical convergence-signaling pattern to the Linked-group block, lines 366-378). This block runs on every seed-triggered pass (AC-001/AC-002's scenario, where both siblings arrive via `input.seed` and are visible in `out.severities` before `raise()` is ever invoked) as well as on any pass where `raise()` has raised a member's severity via a dependent edge, since it re-reads `out.severities` fresh each outer iteration.\n\n--- commands::version::plan_version (internal orchestration change; external signature unchanged) ---\nExternal signature and return type are unchanged. Internally, plan_version gains: (a) a local `tags` binding capturing the TagIndex currently only produced inline as an unbound argument to aggregate() at line 43 (e.g. `let tags = ws.tags()?;` — `ws.tags()` already returns `Result<&TagIndex, GraphError>`, a borrowed reference, so `tags` is itself `&TagIndex` and must be passed as `tags`, not `&tags`, everywhere it's used, including CascadeInput's new `tags` field); (b) a newly-constructed NapiTargetsIndex, which does not exist anywhere in plan_version today (e.g. `NapiTargetsIndex::load(&ws.config.groups, ws.root)?`); (c) a call to `crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks(&ws.graph, &ws.config.groups, &base_versions, tags, &napi, ws.root)` — the real six-argument signature (`_graph: &D, groups: &GroupTable, base: &BTreeMap<PackageId, Version>, tags: &TagIndex, napi: &NapiTargetsIndex, root: &Path`), sourcing `&ws.graph` for `_graph` and `ws.root` for `root` in addition to the previously-listed `base_versions`, `ws.config.groups`, `tags`, and `napi` — executed before run_cascade; (d) merging of the returned GroupCheckOutcome.diagnostics into the existing `diagnostics` collection (bound at line 203, passed through escalate() at line 219) so they appear in the final VersionPlan.diagnostics; (e) propagating pre_mutation_checks's Err(GraphError::FixedGroupDivergent | GraphError::GroupGrammarMismatch) as plan_version's own Err result, aborting before run_cascade executes.\n\n--- config::groups::GroupTable::resolve ---\nSignature unchanged. Internal logic gains two changes: (1) cross-group conflict detection: while building the fixed_of/linked_of maps (currently populated via unchecked .insert() calls at lines 149 and 180 that silently overwrite an existing entry), if a PackageId being inserted for group G2 already has an entry recorded for a different group G1, resolve() returns Err(GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership { package, groups }) where `package` is the shared resolved PackageId and `groups` lists the conflicting group names (at least G1 and G2), instead of completing the insert and returning Ok. Conflict detection is unified across group kinds: a single resolved PackageId may appear in at most one group total (Fixed or Linked), not one-per-kind. The check compares against a single combined view of both fixed_of and linked_of when performing the insert, not two independently-scoped maps. (2) within-group dedup: immediately after the existing `members.sort()` calls (line 164 for the fixed loop, line 195 for the linked loop), add `members.dedup()` so that a PackageId reachable under two different spellings within that one group's own raw member list (e.g. \"my-lib\" and \"cargo:my-lib\" both resolving to the same PackageId) appears exactly once in the resulting GroupDef.members, since `Vec::dedup()` only removes *consecutive* duplicates and the preceding `.sort()` (which sorts GroupMember by its derived Ord, placing equal resolved-PackageId Package members adjacent to each other) guarantees any such duplicate is consecutive before dedup runs. A duplicate spelling of the same PackageId within one group's own membership list is not a cross-group conflict (see AC-010c) — it is handled entirely by this within-group dedup step, which runs before the cross-group conflict check would ever see the second occurrence.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"38d4c5b1-397b-480e-be8f-cc6492fed9c7","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:39:18.538Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== non_goals[3] full ===\nGroupTable::resolve's other existing responsibilities and error paths beyond the new ConflictingGroupMembership detection — do not refactor unrelated parts of resolve() as a side effect. EXCEPTION, carved out explicitly: the `.dedup()` calls added immediately after the existing `.sort()` calls at lines 164 and 195 (see AC-010c) are in scope and required — they are the mechanism that makes a duplicate spelling within one group's own membership list resolve to a single member instead of two, which is necessary for AC-010c to hold and is not itself a refactor of any other part of resolve().\n\n=== api_surface entries ===\n--- CascadeInput.tags ---\nNew field added to the CascadeInput struct (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, currently 8 fields: graph, groups, cfg, seed, reasons, named_by, base, pre — none named tags). Required so that the new Fixed-group convergence block in solve_cascade (see the api_surface entry below) can call crate::groups::fixed_group_target(g, input.base, &out.severities, input.tags, input.pre) instead of computing each Fixed-group member's target independently via bump_target. Both real construction sites must supply it: commands/version.rs:70 (plan_version) and commands/snapshot.rs:53 (plan_snapshot). TagIndex is defined in crates/callisto-graph/src/tags.rs and exposes last_tag(&self, id: &PackageId) -> Option<&LastTag> and an empty() constructor for tests.\n\n--- cascade::solve_cascade (new Fixed-group convergence block) ---\nFor each `g` in `input.groups.fixed.values()`: collect that group's Package member ids the same way the Linked-group block does (via `g.members(crate::config::GroupMemberKind::Package)` filtered to `GroupMember::Package`). Compute `max_sev` as the maximum of `out.severities.get(id)` over those member ids (defaulting absent entries to `Severity::None`), and for any member whose current severity in `out.severities` is below `max_sev`, raise it to `max_sev` (mirroring the Linked-group block's severity-union step) so severities stay consistent with the shared target about to be computed. If `max_sev > Severity::None`, call `crate::groups::fixed_group_target(g, input.base, &out.severities, input.tags, input.pre)` — the real five-argument signature (`g: &GroupDef, base: &BTreeMap<PackageId, Version>, severities: &BTreeMap<PackageId, Severity>, tags: &TagIndex, _pre: Option<&callisto_format::PreState>`) — exactly once per group per outer-loop iteration, propagating its `Result<Version, GraphError>` with `?`. For every member whose current `out.targets` entry differs from the returned `winner` version, insert `winner` into `out.targets`, set `out.reasons` to `BumpReason::FixedGroupUnion { group: g.name.clone() }`, insert the member id into `worklist`, and set the outer loop's `changed = true` (identical convergence-signaling pattern to the Linked-group block, lines 366-378). This block