{"parentUuid":"35514d8e-47f4-4ee6-9d86-dabea60969aa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8fFC2GXJCJ6vPhJcZNW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AuuuRUxzYRKYDwaLZg2x97","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\npython3 << 'PYEOF'\nimport json\n\npath = '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track1-draft.json'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    d = json.load(f)\n\n# Fix 1: purpose clause (3) -- remove dedup trailing clause\nd['purpose'] = d['purpose'].replace(\n    \" instead of silently overwriting one group's claim with the other's, and deduplicate \"\n    \"same-group duplicate spellings so a PackageId reachable under two spellings within one \"\n    \"group appears exactly once in that group's resolved members.\",\n    \" instead of silently overwriting one group's claim with the other's.\"\n)\n\n# Fix 2: revision_note -- append a note about the second audit round's fixes, correcting the\n# stale BLK-03 description\nd['revision_note'] += (\n    \" SECOND AUDIT ROUND (after retry-1 passed then a fresh audit found 4 more issues): the \"\n    \"BLK-03 fix described above (adding `.dedup()` to GroupTable::resolve, carving out a \"\n    \"non_goals exception) has been RETRACTED. A second audit traced fixed_group_target's \"\n    \"released[0]-only alignment-base lookup, its idempotent max_sev computation, \"\n    \"pre_mutation_checks's idempotent divergence comparison, and solve_cascade's \"\n    \"equality-gated/BTreeSet-backed convergence writes, and confirmed an undeduplicated \"\n    \"duplicate spelling cannot corrupt any of AC-001/AC-002/AC-004/AC-007 -- the dedup \"\n    \"requirement was not load-bearing and has been removed as scope creep: AC-010c deleted, \"\n    \"the GroupTable::resolve api_surface entry's dedup clause removed, non_goals item 4 \"\n    \"restored to its unqualified original form, and a new non_goals item added explicitly \"\n    \"deferring within-group dedup with the traced justification. Three further issues from \"\n    \"that same audit round were also fixed: AC-003 rewritten to additionally cover the six \"\n    \"CascadeInput literals in crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs (lines 48, 141, 196, \"\n    \"258, 324, 411) alongside cascade.rs's own seven test-module literals -- all thirteen \"\n    \"confirmed to construct no Fixed groups (only Linked/default), so all can take \"\n    \"TagIndex::empty(); a new AC-014 added covering plan_snapshot's newly-introduced ws.tags() \"\n    \"fallibility; a new non_goals item added documenting GroupCheckOutcome.new_members as \"\n    \"intentionally write-only in this spec's wiring.\"\n)\n\n# Fix 3: reasoning -- drop the now-false AC-010c dedup justification paragraph\nd['reasoning'] = d['reasoning'].split(\" For AC-010c's dedup fix,\")[0] + (\n    \" AC-010c's dedup requirement was later retracted in a second audit round after being \"\n    \"traced as not load-bearing for any other criterion in this spec -- see revision_note.\"\n)\n\n# Fix 4: AC-003 -- add cascade_tests.rs's 6 literals, simplify TagIndex::empty() guidance\ncriteria = d['acceptance_criteria']\nby_id = {c['id']: c for c in criteria}\nby_id['AC-003']['criterion'] = (\n    \"crates/callisto-graph builds and its full test suite (including its integration test \"\n    \"binaries) compiles successfully after CascadeInput gains a `tags: &TagIndex` field, with \"\n    \"every CascadeInput construction site updated to supply it: commands/version.rs's \"\n    \"plan_version (line 70), commands/snapshot.rs's plan_snapshot (line 53), the seven \"\n    \"pre-existing CascadeInput literals inside cascade.rs's own #[cfg(test)] mod tests block \"\n    \"(lines 698, 779, 850, 947, 1074, 1157, 1237), and the six pre-existing CascadeInput \"\n    \"literals inside crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs (lines 48, 141, 196, 258, 324, \"\n    \"411). None of these thirteen pre-existing test literals construct a Fixed group (they use \"\n    \"Linked groups or GroupTable::default()), so all thirteen are updated to supply \"\n    \"`tags: &TagIndex::empty()`. `cargo test -p callisto-graph --no-run` (or the workspace \"\n    \"equivalent via `just ci` / `moon run :test`) completes with zero compilation errors across \"\n    \"all of cascade.rs, its test module, cascade_tests.rs, version.rs, and snapshot.rs.\"\n)\n\n# Fix 5: ws.root borrow issue in plan_version api_surface entry\nfor e in d['api_surface']:\n    if 'plan_version' in e['name']:\n        e['description'] = e['description'].replace(\n            \"NapiTargetsIndex::load(&ws.config.groups, ws.root)?\",\n            \"NapiTargetsIndex::load(&ws.config.groups, &ws.root)?\"\n        ).replace(\n            \"crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks(&ws.graph, &ws.config.groups, &base_versions, tags, &napi, ws.root)\",\n            \"crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks(&ws.graph, &ws.config.groups, &base_versions, tags, &napi, &ws.root)\"\n        ).replace(\n            \"sourcing `&ws.graph` for `_graph` and `ws.root` for `root`\",\n            \"sourcing `&ws.graph` for `_graph` and `&ws.root` for `root` (Workspace.root is `pub root: PathBuf`, so it must be borrowed, not moved, from a `&Workspace`)\"\n        )\n\nwith open(path, 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(d, f, indent=2)\n\nprint(\"patched\")\nprint(\"purpose has dedup mention:\", \"deduplicate\" in d['purpose'])\nprint(\"AC-003 mentions cascade_tests.rs:\", \"cascade_tests.rs\" in by_id['AC-003']['criterion'])\nfor e in d['api_surface']:\n    if 'plan_version' in e['name']:\n        print(\"plan_version entry has &ws.root twice:\", e['description'].count('&ws.root'))\nPYEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1578,"cache_read_input_tokens":427950,"output_tokens":2345,"outp