{"parentUuid":"8513bfd1-a155-4c04-a980-4c52568d4181","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8jeu5S9myzWqG7CJfXx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LdCQqoYHzBdTrD16725fkp","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Challenge Track 1 implementation plan","subagent_type":"vector:challenger","prompt":"Adversarially review the plan@1 at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/plan-fixed-group-cascade.json against its source spec at .claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS.json (workspace root /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto, spec_hash sha256:5050ccacc14ab9b144a88e934dbadde003e480251a50227cc011a8b32249306e — verify this hash still matches the spec file on disk, since if it doesn't the plan was built against a stale spec version).\n\nThis spec passed canon-exit-gate only after 4 rounds of adversarial review that caught: a misdiagnosed fix location (a plan that targeted the wrong function would silently fail to fix the actual bug), a borrow-checker error in a call-site sketch, an incomplete enumeration of test files needing updates, and a reference to a nonexistent enum variant. Given that history, be especially rigorous checking whether the plan's 12 tasks (organized in 4 batches: B1/T01-T04 CascadeInput.tags field + 15 call sites, B2/T05 the new Fixed-group convergence block in solve_cascade, B3/T06-T09 pre_mutation_checks wiring into plan_version, B4/T10-T12 GroupTable::resolve conflict detection) correctly implement what the spec's api_surface section actually describes — not a plausible-sounding paraphrase of it. In particular: does T05's Fixed-group convergence block genuinely mirror the Linked-group block's structure (equality-gated insert into out.targets/out.severities, BTreeSet-backed worklist, changed=true signaling) as the spec requires, or does it risk the same \"unreachable for the seed-path scenario\" mistake the first spec draft made? Does B4's conflict detection genuinely check across BOTH fixed_of and linked_of (unified, per AC-010b) rather than being scoped per-kind?\n\nCheck all seven standard dimensions: missing criteria (any of the 16 ACs — AC-001 through AC-013 plus AC-007b, AC-010b, AC-014 — with no covering task), wrong order (a task referencing a symbol/field a later task creates), over-specified (steps too rigid for legitimate implementation-detail flexibility), under-specified (missing test assertions or target files), poor-batching (a task crossing a compilation boundary it shouldn't), missing-error-handling (any of the spec's 5 is_error_case:true criteria — AC-007, AC-007b, AC-010, AC-010b, AC-014 — lacking a real implementation+test step, not just a mention), and orphaned-criteria (an AC ID that appears in no task's covers_criteria). Output the standard JSON with per-issue list and overall pass/fail verdict."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1503,"cache_read_input_tokens":452952,"output_tokens":1368,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":208},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1503,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1368,"cache_read_input_tokens":452952,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1503},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8jegc66Jw6ahDiDAXqE","type":"assistant","uuid":"49091f1a-f02b-4bc5-8996-b8c9cca766d7","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:44:46.707Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d