{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:48:49.708Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a58b0ec20b8930f18</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a58b0ec20b8930f18.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Challenge Track 1 implementation plan\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Confirms T10's `depends_on: []` at line 172. This is my final finding.\n\n## Review Summary\n\n**Spec hash verified**: `sha256:5050ccacc14ab9b144a88e934dbadde003e480251a50227cc011a8b32249306e` matches `.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS.json` on disk exactly — plan is not stale.\n\nI cross-checked the plan's claims against live source (`crates/callisto-graph/src/{cascade.rs,groups.rs,napi.rs,commands/version.rs,commands/snapshot.rs,config/groups.rs}`, `crates/callisto-model/src/{error.rs,identity.rs,report.rs,package.rs,diagnostic.rs}`, `crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs`) — line numbers, struct field lists (all 8 `CascadeInput` fields, all 7+6 pre-existing literal sites), function signatures (`fixed_group_target`, `pre_mutation_checks`, `NapiTargetsIndex::load`, `TagIndex::build`, `GitAccess::discover`, `Workspace::load`), and every enum variant referenced (`BumpReason::FixedGroupUnion`, `GraphError::{ConflictingGroupMembership,FixedGroupDivergent,GroupGrammarMismatch,SplitIdentity}`, `ManifestError::Parse{format: ManifestFormat::PackageJson}`, `DiagnosticCode::NapiTargetAddedNotInMembers`) all matched precisely. This plan does not repeat any of the four prior-round mistakes (wrong fix location, borrow-checker error, missing test-file enumeration, nonexistent enum variant) — T05's Fixed-group block genuinely mirrors the Linked-group block's structure line-for-line (equality-gated insert, `worklist.insert`, `changed = true`) and sits inside the same `while changed` loop after the seed-severities are already populated, so it is reachable on the very first outer iteration for the seed-path scenario — the exact bug the first spec draft got wrong is avoided. B4's conflict check uses one combined `claimed_by: BTreeMap&lt;PackageId, GroupName&gt;` shared across both the fixed and linked resolution loops, satisfying AC-010b's unified-check requirement.\n\nAll 16 acceptance criteria (AC-001 through AC-013, AC-007b, AC-010b, AC-014) appear in some task's `covers_criteria` — no orphaned criteria. All 5 `is_error_case:true` criteria have real implementation+test coverage (AC-007→T06/T07, AC-007b→T08, AC-010→T10, AC-010b→T11, AC-014→T04).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T10\",\n      \"type\": \"wrong-order\",\n      \"description\": \"T10 (GroupTable::resolve conflict detection, in config/groups.rs) declares depends_on: [] and the plan's top-level architecture field states 'slice 4 is independent and can run in any order.' That is true of T10's own logic (config/groups.rs never references CascadeInput), but it is false as an execution/compilation claim: T10's own verification step runs `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test config_resolve_tests conflicting_fixed_group_membership_across_spellings_is_rejected`, which requires the whole callisto-graph lib target to compile first -- including commands/version.rs and commands/snapshot.rs, whose CascadeInput literals only compile once T03 and T04 (slice 1) have landed. If T10 is scheduled per its declared dependencies (e.g. run in parallel with or before T01-T04, exactly as the architecture text invites), the RED step fails with unrelated E0063 missing-field errors from cascade.rs/version.rs/snapshot.rs rather than the intended GroupTable::resolve assertion failure, producing a false/misleading signal.\",\n      \"suggested_fix\": \"Set T10's depends_on to [\\\"T04\\\"] (the task that closes out slice 1's full-crate compile), and correct the architecture field's claim to something like: 'slice 4's own logic is independent of slices 1-3, but its test binary shares the callisto-graph lib target, so it must still be sequenced after slice 1 (T04) closes out a full crate compile before its tests can run.'\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overall\": \"fail\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Verified spec_hash matches disk. Exhaustively cross-checked every task's cited line numbers, struct/enum definitions, and function signatures against live source -- all matched exactly, including the historically-fragile points (Fixed-group block placement inside the seed-populated while-changed loop, the real five/six-argument fixed_group_target/pre_mutation_checks signatures, BumpReason::FixedGroupUnion's real existence, GraphError::SplitIdentity as a real fallback variant, ManifestError::Parse's format field, unified claimed_by map spanning fixed_of/linked_of for AC-010b). All 16 AC IDs are covered by covers_criteria; all 5 error-case criteria have real test+implementation steps, not mentions only. Found one genuine, specific, actionable wrong-order issue: T10's depends_on: [] and the architecture note's 'independent, any order' claim are inconsistent with the crate-wide compile dependency its own test command has on slice 1 finishing. This is a blocking-class (wrong-order) issue per the review dimensions, so overall is fail; everything else in the plan is unusually well-grounded and needs no correction.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>110674</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>24</tool_uses><duration_ms>238190</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
