"reasoning\": \"AC-003 (crate compiles) is also covered by this task per the plan's covers_criteria list, satisfied by the compile-GREEN step; no dedicated test needed since it's a compile-level property, so it's omitted from criteria_evidence proper (no single test/impl line pair proves a whole-crate compile) but the full-suite run and clean clippy/fmt confirm it. AC-005's implementation_line points to PlannedBump.to (line 96); BumpRecord.to is at line 106, both proven by the same test.\"\n}\n```\n\nFiles touched:\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs` (only file modified — `tags` wiring at lines 38/63, new test module at lines 155–334)\n\nCommit: `bf2bde7` — \"fix(graph): wire tags into plan_snapshot's CascadeInput and pin AC-005/AC-006/AC-014\"\n\nOne deviation worth flagging: the plan's literal AC-006 test body was self-referential (checking the whole file's source via `include_str!` for a string that necessarily appears in the test's own name/comments), which would have made it fail unconditionally. I fixed this by scoping the substring check to only the code above the `#[cfg(test)]` boundary, preserving the test's intent and assertion message.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>70078</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>30</tool_uses><duration_ms>1628640</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
