{"parentUuid":"82e648d5-6aff-40a8-933f-879d961e98f3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8yZTey7q6yLrW3gc65c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough grounding now (the `GroupMember::PlatformManifest { owner, role, path, name }` shape confirms platform packages are Fixed-group siblings). Drafting Track 2's requirement and dispatching to canon-drafter."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_read_input_tokens":545548,"output_tokens":4256,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":535},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":642,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4256,"cache_read_input_tokens":545548,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":642},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8yZQirV9RD7JzFuy67y","type":"assistant","uuid":"504bc3f9-1e7b-4933-b16d-d8cc03ed3340","timestamp":"2026-08-17T20:46:57.745Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"504bc3f9-1e7b-4933-b16d-d8cc03ed3340","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8yZTey7q6yLrW3gc65c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BxPuGnwaZUmkb6kwM3LGSr","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Draft Track 2 spec (platform-manifest writes)","subagent_type":"canon:drafter","prompt":"Draft a spec@1 from the following requirement@1 for the callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"REQ-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES\",\n  \"statement\": \"Build the planning logic that populates VersionPlan.platform_writes and VersionPlan.optional_dep_updates from a Fixed group's GroupMember::PlatformManifest members and their owning package's version bump, and fix two confirmed-dormant correctness gaps in the already-landed consumption side (apply_version_plan's dispatch loops for these two fields).\",\n  \"stakeholder\": \"Callisto maintainers and any user with a napi-rs/maturin platform-package release configuration (a Fixed group whose members include GroupMember::PlatformManifest entries alongside the owning Cargo/npm package)\",\n  \"why\": \"Confirmed via direct code inspection: commands/version.rs's plan_version (and commands/snapshot.rs's plan_snapshot, and commands/pr_body.rs) all hardcode platform_writes and optional_dep_updates to Vec::new() -- nothing in production populates them, so a napi-rs platform package's own package.json never gets its version bumped in step with its owning package, and the owning package's optionalDependencies entry pointing at that platform package's version never gets updated either. A prior adversarial audit of the consumption side (apply_version_plan's dispatch loops for these two fields, already landed in a separate commit with zero planning-logic producer) found two dormant-but-real bugs that must be fixed as part of this track, not deferred: (1) active_ecosystems (which drives lockfile refresh/staging in apply_version_plan) is derived only from plan.bumps, never from platform_writes/optional_dep_updates, so once real data flows through, a stale lockfile would never be refreshed or staged; (2) the platform_writes dispatch loop has no precondition/expected-current-version check unlike every sibling write loop in the same function (which check current==expected and error on drift via GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion), so a platform manifest whose on-disk version already drifted from the plan's expectation gets silently, unconditionally overwritten.\",\n  \"done_when\": [\n    \"Given a Fixed group containing an owner Package member (e.g. Cargo crate 'my-lib') and a GroupMember::PlatformManifest member (owner: my-lib's PackageId, path: 'platform/my-lib.linux-x64-gnu/package.json', name: 'my-lib.linux-x64-gnu'), and a computed PlannedBump for the owner from version X to version Y, running commands::version::plan_version produces a VersionPlan whose platform_writes contains a PlatformWrite { manifest: 'platform/my-lib.linux-x64-gnu/package.json', version: Y } entry -- the platform manifest's target version tracks its owner's bump target exactly, not an independently-computed version.\",\n    \"Given the same scenario, and the owner's own canonical manifest (e.g. a sibling package.json, if the owner ecosystem is npm/hybrid, or another workspace package) declares an optionalDependencies entry naming the platform package ('my-lib.linux-x64-gnu': '<old version>'), plan_version's VersionPlan.optional_dep_updates contains an OptionalDepUpdate entry for that manifest updating that dependency name to version Y.\",\n    \"Given a Fixed group with NO GroupMember::PlatformManifest members (the ordinary case), plan_version's platform_writes and optional_dep_updates remain empty Vecs -- no regression for workspaces without platform packages.\",\n    \"Given a Fixed group's owner package receiving NO version bump this run (e.g. no changeset, Severity::None), no PlatformWrite or OptionalDepUpdate entry is produced for that group's platform members -- platform-manifest writes are strictly driven by an actual owner bump, never speculative.\",\n    \"Fix 1 (dormant bug, apply_version_plan consumption side): active_ecosystems (crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs, currently derived only from plan.bumps) is extended to also derive ecosystem membership from plan.platform_writes and plan.optional_dep_updates' manifest paths, so that when opts.refresh_lockfiles is true and a plan contains only platform_writes/optional_dep_updates entries (no bumps), the correct ecosystem's lockfile (e.g. package-lock.json/pnpm-lock.yaml for an npm platform manifest) is both refreshed and staged, exactly as it already is for an ordinary plan.bumps-only plan.\",\n    \"Fix 1 regression: given an ordinary plan with only plan.bumps entries (no platform_writes/optional_dep_updates), active_ecosystems and lockfile refresh/staging behavior is byte-for-byte unchanged from before this fix -- all existing apply.rs tests pass unmodified.\",\n    \"Fix 2 (dormant bug, apply_version_plan consumption side): the platform_writes dispatch loop in apply_version_plan gains a precondition check mirroring the existing bump loops' current==expected pattern: PlatformWrite gains a `from: Version` field (the plan-time-observed current version of the platform manifest), and the loop errors with GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion (the same variant the sibling bump loops already use) if the platform manifest's actual on-disk current version does not match `from` at apply time, instead of silently overwriting it with `version` unconditionally.\",\n    \"Fix 2 regression: given a platform manifest whose on-disk version exactly matches the plan's PlatformWrite.from at apply time (the ordinary, non-drifted case), apply_version_plan succeeds and writes `version` exactly as before -- no behavior change for the non-drifted path.\",\n    \"Every acceptance criterion is proven through the real, live call path (commands::version::plan_version for the planning-logic criteria; crate::apply::apply_version_plan for the two consumption-side fixes), not just isolated unit tests of a helper function called directly.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"commands::snapshot::plan_snapshot and commands::pr_body's own platform_writes/optional_dep_updates population -- separate command entry points, explicitly deferred; this track covers plan_version only (state the reason: snapshot mode's synthetic versioning and pr_body's preview-only nature don't need real platform-manifest writes the way a real version-and-apply run does -- but the drafter should confirm this reasoning is sound and state it explicitly, not assume it).\",\n    \"Building a NEW planning-logic path for optionalDependencies updates unrelated to platform packages (e.g. an ordinary cross-package optionalDependencies bump with no napi/platform-manifest involvement) -- OptionalDepUpdate's only production source in this track is the platform-package-tracks-its-owner case.\",\n    \"Any change to the Manifest trait, ManifestFormat::from_path, or update_optional_dependencies's own internal logic -- both already exist and are correct, this track only adds a new call-site producer.\",\n    \"Redesigning apply_version_plan's write-batching (Spec A/Spec B's classify_manifest_writes) to fold platform_writes/optional_dep_updates into the batched-write groups -- the two dispatch loops remain structurally separate, sequential loops; this track only adds the missing precondition check and lockfile-ecosystem awareness to them, not a batching redesign.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n# Background context for grounding (verify against live code yourself, do not trust this paraphrase)\n\n`GroupMember::PlatformManifest { owner: PackageId, role: ManifestRole, path: PathBuf, name: String }` is defined in `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs`. `PlatformWrite { manifest: PathBuf, version: Version }` and `OptionalDepUpdate { manifest: PathBuf, updates: Vec<(String, Version)> }` are defined in `crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs`. `commands/version.rs`'s `plan_version` (just modified by Track 1, now also calling `pre_mutation_checks` and constructing a `NapiTargetsIndex` before `run_cascade`) hardcodes both fields to `Vec::new()` in its final `VersionPlan` construction. `crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs`'s `apply_version_plan` already has two dispatch loops consuming these fields (landed in a separate, already-committed change with only one happy-path test) — read that code directly to confirm the two dormant-bug claims above before writing acceptance criteria referencing them. `active_ecosystems` and the lockfile refresh/staging logic are also in `apply.rs` — read the actual current derivation before writing Fix 1's acceptance criteria. `GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion` is an existing error variant used by the sibling bump loops — confirm its exact field shape before referencing it in Fix 2's criteria.\n\nThis is \"Track 2\" of a larger, already-approved 12-track remediation plan. Track 1 (fixed-group cascade correctness) just shipped — this track depends on Track 1's group-aligned target computation (a platform package's owner's bump target must be the CORRECT group-aligned version, not the old per-sibling-independent-bump version, or this track would silently propagate the same divergence bug into platform manifests). This repo's established process (`.claude/plans/ACTIVE.md`): full canon→vector→lambda pipeline for a track like this. `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"` hard workspace invariant. `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` mandatory CI. Verify every code-location/line-number/field-shape claim above against the live code before trusting it — this session's Track 1 spec went through 4 exit-gate rounds specifically because early drafts contained small inaccuracies about the actual code.\n\nProduce a spec@1 with purpose, scope, non_goals (at least the four out_of_scope items above, stated as non_goals, with the reasoning for the snapshot.rs/pr_body.rs deferral made explicit rather than assumed), acceptance_criteria (testable propositions, error cases marked is_error_case: true), and an api_surface section documenting any new/changed function signature or struct field (PlatformWrite gaining a `from` field is exactly such a change)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_read_input_tokens":545548,"output_tokens":4256,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":535},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":642,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4256,"cache_read_input_tokens":545548,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":642},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8yZQirV9RD7JzFuy67y","type":"assistant","uuid":"28cf3e96-13dc-43ce-a350-c667e245d9a4","timestamp":"2026-08-17T20:47:32.388Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
