{"parentUuid":"570ed955-c80f-438b-a81b-e598b6758c9a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8za5tfWaafpn4hKy5Ni","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013Fp24m6zPscyEFU5dyu7GC","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Exit-gate Track 2 spec","subagent_type":"canon:exit-gate","prompt":"Issue a binding pass/fail verdict on the spec@1 at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track2-draft.json (id SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES, callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto). This is retry_count 1 (first exit-gate pass). Read the full spec fresh from disk — do not trust this summary.\n\nHistory: canon-verifier found 10/14 original criteria directly grounded in the requirement, 4 (AC-002, AC-004, AC-007, AC-008) drafter-added without direct citation but plausible completeness additions. canon-auditor then independently found: (1) AC-002's derivation mechanism for PlatformWrite.from was genuinely ambiguous with two different-behavior implementations possible (GroupMember::PlatformManifest's own `role` field vs. hardcoded ManifestRole::Canonical) — a Cargo-format platform manifest would crash under one reading; fixed by specifying ManifestRole::Canonical unconditionally, matching apply.rs's own existing convention at lines 247/257. (2) AC-012 (Fix 2's precondition check) omitted the idempotent-retry branch — a crash-retry where the platform manifest was already written to its target version would incorrectly throw UnexpectedManifestVersion; fixed by narrowing AC-012 to exclude that case and adding new AC-012b covering it as success. (3) AC-007 (multi-platform-target-per-owner) left optional_dep_updates's shape unspecified for that scenario, with a real runtime consequence (duplicate un-batched opens/persists of the same manifest file); fixed by adding AC-007b requiring merged updates in one OptionalDepUpdate entry. (4) AC-014 was a testing-process rule, not an observable-behavior criterion; moved out of acceptance_criteria into non_goals. All four fixes applied directly. I additionally found and fixed several stale AC-ID cross-references in the api_surface section left over from before these criteria were renumbered/added (e.g. \"AC-005, AC-006\" for lockfile logic corrected to \"AC-009, AC-010, AC-011\"; \"AC-011\" for the malformed-manifest error path corrected to \"AC-008\"; \"AC-007, AC-008\" for the precondition check corrected to \"AC-012, AC-012b, AC-013\") — verify these corrections actually landed and are now internally consistent, don't just trust that they did.\n\nRead the current code at crates/callisto-graph/src/{plan.rs,apply.rs,commands/version.rs,config/groups.rs,groups.rs} and crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs yourself to independently re-verify every api_surface/acceptance-criteria claim — especially the ManifestRole::Canonical claim (does apply.rs really already use ManifestRole::Canonical at both the platform_writes and optional_dep_updates dispatch sites, and does ManifestDecl::new really reject a Platform-role+CargoToml-format combination as the auditor claimed?) and the idempotent-retry claim (do the sibling PlannedBump-driven write loops in apply.rs really have a three-way current==target/current==from/else branch, confirming AC-012b's proposed behavior genuinely mirrors an established pattern rather than inventing new semantics?).\n\nApply your standard adversarial pass/fail standard: every acceptance criterion testable, no vague language, no TBDs, error cases covered with is_error_case: true, scope narrow enough for one planning cycle. Default disposition is fail. Output a verdict@1 with artifact_type \"spec@1\" and retry_count 1."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2452,"cache_read_input_tokens":577171,"output_tokens":1415,"output_token