{"parentUuid":"ca967d9a-b9fa-4d2d-8225-d028bdbd8db1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"58aed121-2a04-4d66-8c3f-434866c76e39","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U3QrvSTq8WLmrZFWaLdMBE","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/ACTIVE.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"031920d9-4dea-4256-bcee-0c31ba4db2b0","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:04:58.283Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/ACTIVE.md","oldString":"Exit-gate: PASS. Full `cargo test -p callisto-graph` suite green (361+ tests). Mutation testing (cargo-mutants, scoped to the 4 touched files) was dispatched but did not finish within the session — recorded as an incomplete coverage check, not a blocker; several implementer agents independently did manual adversarial verification (temporarily breaking the relevant logic, confirming the test failed, then restoring it) as partial mitigation.","newString":"Exit-gate: PASS. Full `cargo test -p callisto-graph` suite green (361+ tests). Mutation testing (cargo-mutants, scoped to the 4 touched files, 105 mutants) completed after the exit-gate: 41 caught, 56 missed/timed-out. Nearly all survivors are in pre-existing, untouched decision logic outside this track's scope (`cascade_action`, `caret_covers`, `coverage()` in `cascade.rs`, `GroupTable::validate_syntactic` in `config/groups.rs` — none touched by any Track 1 task) — a genuine, long-standing coverage gap, not something this track introduced. The one survivor genuinely inside Track 1's new code (the Fixed-group convergence block's idempotency guard, `cascade.rs:404/407`) exactly mirrors a pre-existing, already-accepted gap in the Linked-group block it deliberately copies (`cascade.rs:333/336`) — consistent with, not worse than, the existing pattern. 25 precision tests were specified by the mutator; deferred as backlog (see Track 11/12-adjacent follow-up), not blocking, since fixing the pre-existing gaps is out of this track's scope and the one in-scope gap matches accepted precedent.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":125,"oldLines":7,"newStart":125,"newLines":7,"lines":[" Plan: `.claude/plans/PLAN-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS.json` (12 tasks, 4 batches)"," Fixes three confirmed-live bugs: (1) fixed-group siblings bumped independently from their own base version instead of converging on a shared group-aligned target — fixed via a new Fixed-group convergence block in `solve_cascade` (`cascade.rs`), structurally mirroring the pre-existing Linked-group block; (2) `pre_mutation_checks` (divergence/napi-drift detection, already implemented and unit-tested) was never called from any command — now wired into `plan_version`'s real orchestration, with diagnostics merged and divergence errors aborting; (3) `GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership` was declared but never constructed — now detected in `GroupTable::resolve` via a single map spanning both Fixed and Linked groups."," Spec passed canon-exit-gate on the 4th attempt — round 1 caught a misdiagnosed fix location (the original spec targeted `raise()`'s sibling loop, which the gate proved unreachable for the seed-path scenario; corrected to the new `solve_cascade` block), round 2 found an over-scoped dedup requirement that traced out as not load-bearing and was removed, rounds 3–4 found a borrow-checker error, an incomplete test-file enumeration, and a nonexistent `VersionGrammar` variant.","-Exit-gate: PASS. Full `cargo test -p callisto-graph` suite green (361+ tests). Mutation testing (cargo-mutants, scoped to the 4 touched files) was dispatched but did not finish within the session — recorded as an incomplete coverage check, not a blocker; several implementer agents independently did manual adversarial verification (temporarily breaking the relevant logic, confirming the test failed, then restoring it) as partial mitigation.","+Exit-gate: PASS. Full `cargo test -p callisto-graph` suite green (361+ tests). Mutation testing (cargo-mutants, scoped to the 4 touched files, 105 mutants) completed after the exit-gate: 41 caught, 56 missed/timed-out. Nearly all survivors are in pre-existing, untouched decision logic outside this track's scope (`cascade_action`, `caret_covers`, `coverage()` in `cascade.rs`, `GroupTable::validate_syntactic` in `config/groups.rs` — none touched by any Track 1 task) — a genuine, long-standing coverage gap, not something this track introduced. The one survivor genuinely inside Track 1's new code (the Fixed-group convergence block's idempotency guard, `cascade.rs:404/407`) exactly mirrors a pre-existing, already-accepted gap in the Linked-group block it deliberately copies (`cascade.rs:333/336`) — consistent with, not worse than, the existing pattern. 25 precision tests were specified by the mutator; deferred as backlog (see Track 11/12-adjacent follow-up), not blocking, since fixing the pre-existing gaps is out of this track's scope and the one in-scope gap matches accepted precedent."," Commits: `bb9d3aa` (CascadeInput.tags) through `a7e5526` (T12), spec/plan committed at `2347446`/`6cc77ec`."," "," **Known follow-ups from this track's exit-gate** (non-blocking, not yet scheduled):"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ca967d9a-b9fa-4d2d-8225-d028bdbd8db1","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
