{"parentUuid":"e44ea125-f3c9-45a8-bae4-eff49b29034a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce91D4262CQPHJT5CowyB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All grounding confirmed. Applying all four fixes."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1269,"cache_read_input_tokens":604692,"output_tokens":3121,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":295},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1269,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3121,"cache_read_input_tokens":604692,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1269,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1269},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce91CzDPeUZpZgZ5pqgo6","type":"assistant","uuid":"ff069fc6-cd1b-4ae3-8510-bdaf90ce61b5","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:08:30.677Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"ff069fc6-cd1b-4ae3-8510-bdaf90ce61b5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce91D4262CQPHJT5CowyB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UzCDiyUz84kcJbqm3ybiRQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\npython3 << 'PYEOF'\nimport json\n\npath = '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track2-draft.json'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    d = json.load(f)\n\ncriteria = d['acceptance_criteria']\nby_id = {c['id']: c for c in criteria}\n\n# Fix 1 (Blocker 2): AC-002 -- name open() not just ManifestDecl::new, pin OpenContext derivation\nby_id['AC-002']['criterion'] = (\n    \"In the AC-001 scenario, PlatformWrite.from equals the version string currently declared \"\n    \"in the platform manifest file at path P on disk at plan time. plan_version reads P via \"\n    \"ManifestFormat::from_path(P) to detect format, constructs ManifestDecl::new(P, \"\n    \"ManifestRole::Canonical, format) -- ManifestRole::Canonical is used unconditionally \"\n    \"regardless of the owning GroupMember::PlatformManifest's own `role` field, so that a \"\n    \"Cargo/TOML-formatted platform manifest (e.g. a maturin platform crate) does not trip \"\n    \"ManifestDecl::new's Platform-role-vs-CargoToml-format rejection (crates/callisto-model/\"\n    \"src/package.rs:104-106) -- then opens it via callisto_manifests::open(&decl, &ctx) and \"\n    \"calls .current_version() on the resulting handle. The OpenContext `ctx` is derived by \"\n    \"plan_version using the exact same pattern apply_version_plan already uses (crates/\"\n    \"callisto-graph/src/apply.rs:118-130): cargo_workspace via \"\n    \"WorkspaceCargoResolver::load(root.join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\")).inheritance(), and \"\n    \"npm_workspace_kind via callisto_manifests::detect_npm_workspace_kind(root) -- both \"\n    \"derived from the real workspace root, not passed as None. This mirrors the \"\n    \"ManifestRole::Canonical construction already used by apply_version_plan's platform_writes \"\n    \"and optional_dep_updates dispatch loops (crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs:247,257), so \"\n    \"plan-time and apply-time reads of a given platform manifest use the same role and the \"\n    \"same context derivation and cannot diverge.\"\n)\nac002b = {\n    \"id\": \"AC-002b\",\n    \"criterion\": (\n        \"Given the AC-001 scenario where the platform manifest at path P is a Cargo.toml with \"\n        \"`version.workspace = true` (a maturin platform crate inheriting its version from the \"\n        \"workspace root, per crates/callisto-graph/src/cargo.rs:47-52's inherited_version \"\n        \"flag), and the workspace's root Cargo.toml successfully resolves a workspace-level \"\n        \"version via WorkspaceCargoResolver, plan_version's OpenContext derivation (per AC-002) \"\n        \"successfully resolves the inherited version and current_version() returns Ok(..) with \"\n        \"that resolved version, rather than Err(ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited) -- \"\n        \"confirming the AC-002 context derivation actually makes this real, common maturin \"\n        \"layout work end-to-end, not just avoid the format/role rejection.\"\n    ),\n    \"is_error_case\": False,\n}\nidx002 = criteria.index(by_id['AC-002'])\ncriteria.insert(idx002 + 1, ac002b)\n\n# Fix 2 (Blocker 3): AC-005 -- scope to workspace, not group (VersionPlan has no per-group partition)\nby_id = {c['id']: c for c in criteria}\nby_id['AC-005']['criterion'] = (\n    \"Given a workspace where no Fixed group anywhere has any GroupMember::PlatformManifest \"\n    \"members (only Package members across every group), plan_version's VersionPlan.\"\n    \"platform_writes and VersionPlan.optional_dep_updates are both empty Vecs -- no regression \"\n    \"for workspaces without platform packages. (VersionPlan carries no per-group partition, so \"\n    \"this is necessarily a workspace-wide assertion, not a per-group one.)\"\n)\n\n# Fix 3 (Blocker 1): AC-009/AC-010 -- split staging from refresh; npm has no refresh subprocess\nby_id = {c['id']: c for c in criteria}\nby_id['AC-009']['criterion'] = (\n    \"Fix 1 (apply.rs active_ecosystems): given a VersionPlan whose plan.bumps is empty but \"\n    \"plan.platform_writes contains one entry pointing at an npm-ecosystem manifest path (e.g. \"\n    \"'platform/my-lib.linux-x64-gnu/package.json'), ApplyOptions.refresh_lockfiles == true, \"\n    \"and opts.transient == false, calling apply_version_plan causes the npm lockfile \"\n    \"(package-lock.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, yarn.lock, or bun.lockb -- whichever exists on disk \"\n    \"at the workspace root) to be included in ApplyOutcome.staged. apply_version_plan's \"\n    \"lockfile_ecosystems staging table (crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs:411-421) is not \"\n    \"filtered by npm workspace kind, so any of the four npm lockfile filenames present on disk \"\n    \"is staged, not specifically the one matching the detected workspace kind. Note: \"\n    \"apply_version_plan has no npm lockfile REFRESH subprocess at all (only Cargo via `cargo \"\n    \"update` and Pypi via `uv lock`/`poetry lock` at apply.rs:353-407) -- this is true for \"\n    \"every plan, before and after this fix, npm-touching or not. This criterion asserts \"\n    \"staging only; ApplyOutcome.lockfile_refresh_results contains no npm entry, matching the \"\n    \"pre-existing, unchanged behavior for an ordinary plan.bumps-only plan touching an npm \"\n    \"manifest.\"\n)\nby_id['AC-010']['criterion'] = (\n    \"Fix 1 (apply.rs active_ecosystems): given the AC-009 scenario but using \"\n    \"plan.optional_dep_updates instead of plan.platform_writes (plan.bumps empty, one \"\n    \"OptionalDepUpdate entry pointing at an npm-ecosystem manifest path, refresh_lockfiles == \"\n    \"true, transient == false), calling apply_version_plan causes the same npm-lockfile \"\n    \"staging-only behavior described in AC-009 -- the npm lockfile present on disk is included \"\n    \"in ApplyOutcome.staged, and no npm entry appears in ApplyOutcome.lockfile_refresh_results.\"\n)\n\n# Fix 4 (Blocker 4): AC-011 -- assert on observable ApplyOutcome fields, not private active_ecosystems\nby_id = {c['id']: c for c in criteria}\nby_id['AC-011']['criterion'] = (\n    \"Fix 1 regression: given an ordinary VersionPlan with only plan.bumps entries populated \"\n    \"(plan.platform_writes and plan.optional_dep_updates both empty, as in every plan before \"\n    \"this track), calling apply_version_plan with refresh_lockfiles == true produces \"\n    \"byte-for-byte the same ApplyOutcome.lockfile_refresh_results and the same \"\n    \"ApplyOutcome.staged as before this track's change -- confirmed by all pre-existing \"\n    \"apply.rs tests passing unmodified. (active_ecosystems itself is a function-local binding \"\n    \"with no external visibility; this criterion is expressed against ApplyOutcome's public \"\n    \"fields, which are what a test can actually observe.)\"\n)\n\nwith open(path, 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(d, f, indent=2)\n\nprint(\"patched. criteria count:\", len(criteria), [c['id'] for c in criteria])\nPYEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1269,"cache_read_input_tokens":604692,"output_tokens":3121,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":295},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1269,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3121,"cache_read_input_tokens":604692,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1269,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1269},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce91CzDPeUZpZgZ5pqgo6","type":"assistant","uuid":"d746dc8c-79b3-42df-97d3-669bc42212e1","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:08:53.885Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
