{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:39:15.301Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a26bad1b7285f989a</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a26bad1b7285f989a.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Challenge Track 2 implementation plan\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>```json\n{\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"TASK-2\",\n      \"type\": \"under-specified\",\n      \"description\": \"Implementation step 2 says 'for each owner with an entry in bump_by_pkg' as though bump_by_pkg already exists in commands/version.rs. Grepping the file confirms it does not — the only owner-lookup structure present is `pkg_map: HashMap&lt;&amp;PackageId, &amp;Package&gt;` built at line ~100, which maps packages to their Package definition, not to their PlannedBump. There is also no step anywhere in TASK-2 that constructs a PackageId-&gt;PlannedBump lookup from the `bumps: Vec&lt;PlannedBump&gt;` computed earlier at line 95-136. An implementer following the steps literally has no defined `bump_by_pkg` to reference.\",\n      \"suggested_fix\": \"Add an explicit sub-step to TASK-2, before the platform-manifest loop: 'Build `let bump_by_pkg: std::collections::BTreeMap&lt;PackageId, &amp;PlannedBump&gt; = bumps.iter().map(|b| (b.package.clone(), b)).collect();` from the `bumps` Vec already computed earlier in plan_version.' Then reference `bump_by_pkg.get(owner)` in the loop step.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"TASK-5\",\n      \"type\": \"under-specified\",\n      \"description\": \"Step 3 says 'open the owner's canonical manifest' but does not specify the resolution mechanism from `owner: PackageId` (the field on GroupMember::PlatformManifest) to an actual manifest path. `Package::canonical_manifests()` (crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs:24-28) returns an ITERATOR, not a single manifest — the codebase explicitly supports dual-published packages via `is_dual_published()` (package.rs:68-75), which can have two canonical manifests (e.g. npm + Cargo). The step neither says to use the existing `pkg_map: HashMap&lt;&amp;PackageId, &amp;Package&gt;` (already built at commands/version.rs:100) to resolve owner-&gt;Package, nor states which canonical manifest to use if `canonical_manifests()` yields more than one. This directly affects AC-003/AC-004/AC-007b correctness for any owner package that happens to be dual-published.\",\n      \"suggested_fix\": \"Add to TASK-5 step 3: 'Resolve `owner: PackageId` to its Package via the existing `pkg_map` (commands/version.rs:100). Call `.canonical_manifests()` on that Package; if it yields more than one entry, [pick a defined rule — e.g. use the first, or skip optional-dep detection for dual-published owners since Fixed-group owners with platform siblings are expected to be single-ecosystem] — state the rule explicitly rather than leaving \\\"the owner's canonical manifest\\\" ambiguous.'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"TASK-4\",\n      \"type\": \"missing-error-handling\",\n      \"description\": \"AC-008 is disjunctive: 'the platform manifest file declared in group config does not exist on disk, OR exists but cannot be parsed as valid content for its ecosystem (malformed JSON/TOML)'. TASK-4 only writes and covers the first disjunct (file deleted from disk before plan_version runs, single test `plan_version_returns_err_when_platform_manifest_missing_from_disk_at_plan_time`). The second disjunct — a platform manifest that exists but contains malformed/unparseable JSON or TOML — has no corresponding test anywhere in TASK-4 (or elsewhere in the plan). Although the `?`-based propagation TASK-2 relies on will likely handle both cases identically at the code level, the spec explicitly calls out both failure modes as part of one is_error_case:true criterion, and only one is proven.\",\n      \"suggested_fix\": \"Add a fourth test to TASK-4: write syntactically invalid content (e.g. truncated/unbalanced JSON) into the platform manifest file on disk instead of deleting it, then call plan_version and assert Err(GraphError) is returned with no partial VersionPlan — covering AC-008's 'malformed JSON/TOML' disjunct, not just the missing-file disjunct.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overall\": \"fail\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Verified spec_hash matches file on disk. Read plan.rs, apply.rs (lines 100-430, 2230-2270), commands/version.rs (full), config/groups.rs (full) against the plan's 8 tasks and 16 spec ACs. The two areas the caller specifically flagged for scrutiny (TASK-2 OpenContext derivation, TASK-8 three-way precondition branch) both genuinely match the spec's mandated pattern -- verified by reading the exact cited line ranges. AC-007b merge logic (TASK-5/6) correctly produces one OptionalDepUpdate per manifest path via BTreeMap keying, not per platform member. All 16 AC IDs are covered in criteria_coverage_check with no orphans. However, three concrete gaps survive: TASK-2 references an undefined 'bump_by_pkg' lookup with no construction step (blocking -- implementer must invent the map's type/construction, risking divergence from the bumps Vec's actual shape); TASK-5's 'open the owner's canonical manifest' elides both the owner-&gt;manifest path resolution mechanism and the dual-published-package ambiguity that the codebase's own Package::canonical_manifests()/is_dual_published() API demonstrates is a real case; and TASK-4 leaves AC-008's second disjunct (malformed manifest content, as opposed to missing file) completely untested despite AC-008 being one of only two is_error_case:true criteria in this spec and the task instructions explicitly calling out error-case rigor. These are blocking under the missing-error-handling and under-specified dimensions.\"\n}\n```\n\nRelevant files reviewed:\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/PLAN-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs` (lines 100-430, 2230-2270)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs`</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>88052</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>21</tool_uses><duration_ms>231257</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
