t's WIP causing a full-suite test failure there.\"\n}\n```\n\n**Summary**\n\nImplemented TASK-8 (apply.rs Fix 2) via TDD in `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs`. Added a three-way precondition check to the `platform_writes` dispatch loop (lines 244-262): `current == pw.version` → idempotent no-op but still staged (AC-012b); `current == pw.from` → normal write (AC-013, proven by the pre-existing unmodified regression test); else → `Err(GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion { path, expected_from, expected_to, found })` with the manifest left untouched (AC-012).\n\nTwo new tests added at apply.rs:2332 and apply.rs:2384. Confirmed genuine RED for the drift case before implementing. All 30 apply.rs tests pass, fmt/clippy clean, committed as `4726863`.\n\nOne note: the full crate test suite has one unrelated failing test (`commands::version::tests::probe_cargo_platform_sibling_discovery`) caused by uncommitted WIP debug code in `commands/version.rs` belonging to the concurrently-running TASK-3 agent — that file was explicitly out of scope for this task, so it was left untouched. `apply.rs`'s own test module is fully green.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>70939</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>21</tool_uses><duration_ms>289149</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
