{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:59:01.578Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aec2c6020ccb56559</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Sc9yCXGVoYracJ5unYVTbH</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/aec2c6020ccb56559.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement TASK-3 (workspace-inherited version + multi-sibling)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I found a genuine, empirically-verified contradiction between AC-002b and the actual system behavior, and stopped before writing any implementation or committing. Here's what happened.\n\n**Investigation**: I read TASK-3 from the plan and AC-002b/AC-007 directly from the spec file. TASK-2's landed code (`crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:264-302`) already loops over every `GroupMember::PlatformManifest` and derives `cargo_workspace` inheritance into `OpenContext`, confirming AC-007 (multi-sibling npm platform writes) is fully supported with zero new implementation.\n\nFor AC-002b (a maturin-style Cargo.toml platform manifest with `version.workspace = true`, discovered as a `GroupMember::PlatformManifest` through the real `Workspace::load` pipeline, per the spec's explicit \"AC-001 scenario\" wording), I traced the actual discovery code:\n\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:196-217` — the only code that registers a manifest into `IdentityIndex.platform` (which is what makes `groups.rs::resolve()` classify a config member as `GroupMember::PlatformManifest` rather than `GroupMember::Package`) is gated by `if *eco == Ecosystem::Npm`. There is no equivalent branch for `Ecosystem::Cargo`.\n- I verified this empirically with a throwaway probe test (written, run, then fully reverted via `git checkout --`) that constructed a real workspace with a separate `crates/plat/Cargo.toml` (`version.workspace = true`, own package name `owner-darwin-arm64`) referenced in a `[[fixed-group]] members` list alongside the owner. Through the real `Workspace::load` → `plan_version` pipeline, it resolved as an ordinary `GroupMember::Package`, got its own independent `PlannedBump` writing to its own Cargo.toml, and `platform_writes` came back empty — never a `PlatformWrite`.\n\nSo there is currently no real-discovery code path that can produce a Cargo-format `GroupMember::PlatformManifest`, which AC-002b requires end-to-end. Per the spec's own non-goal #6 (\"Validating that a GroupMember::PlatformManifest's owner resolves... this track assumes group config already passed that validation\"), AC-002b's premise depends on discovery working for Cargo manifests — and it doesn't. Faking this via a hand-constructed `GroupTable` (bypassing real discovery) would contradict the task's own explicit instruction that these scenarios must be proven through `plan_version`'s real return value, not isolated calls — so I stopped rather than build a test/implementation that hides this gap behind a green checkmark.\n\nI made no code changes (the probe was fully reverted; `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs` is clean at HEAD `4726863`) and did not commit.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"TASK-3\",\n  \"status\": \"spec_contradiction\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"Read TASK-3 from plan file\",\n    \"Read AC-002b and AC-007 text directly from spec file\",\n    \"Read TASK-2's landed platform_writes loop and existing Case-D hybrid-root test fixtures in commands/version.rs for convention consistency\",\n    \"Traced walk.rs platform-manifest discovery (index.platform registration) and confirmed it is gated to Ecosystem::Npm only, with no Cargo equivalent\",\n    \"Empirically probed the real Workspace::load -&gt; plan_version pipeline with a maturin-style Cargo.toml platform sibling fixture; confirmed it resolves as GroupMember::Package, not GroupMember::PlatformManifest, and platform_writes remains empty\",\n    \"Reverted the probe test; verified working tree is clean at HEAD\",\n    \"Did not write AC-007 test or commit, since TASK-3 bundles both criteria into a single commit unit\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"fail\",\n  \"commit_sha\": null,\n  \"concerns\": \"AC-007 is fully valid and unaffected by this contradiction -- a two npm-platform-sibling scenario following the same real Case-D discovery pattern as AC-001 would pass today with zero further implementation changes, per TASK-2's existing loop. Recommend routing AC-002b back through canon (correction mode) to either (a) revise AC-002b to describe the actual supported mechanism, or (b) split platform-manifest discovery for Cargo/maturin into its own spec/track that extends walk.rs's Ecosystem::Npm-gated platform detection to Ecosystem::Cargo, then re-plan TASK-3 to cover AC-007 alone (or AC-007 plus a corrected AC-002b) in the interim.\",\n  \"contradiction\": {\n    \"criterion_id\": \"AC-002b\",\n    \"spec_claim\": \"A maturin-style platform manifest -- a Cargo.toml with `version.workspace = true` -- can be declared as a GroupMember::PlatformManifest sibling of a Fixed-group owner (the same real-workspace-discovery pattern as AC-001's Case D npm hybrid-root), such that calling plan_version through its real, disk-discovered call path (not a direct current_version() call) resolves the workspace-inherited version and emits a PlatformWrite with `from` equal to that resolved version.\",\n    \"observed_behavior\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:196-217 (the only site that registers a manifest into IdentityIndex.platform, which is what causes crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs::resolve() to classify a config member as GroupMember::PlatformManifest rather than GroupMember::Package) is gated by `if *eco == Ecosystem::Npm` with no equivalent branch for Ecosystem::Cargo. Empirically verified: a fixture with a real workspace (root Cargo.toml declaring [workspace.package] version = \\\"3.2.1\\\"), an owner crate, and a separate crates/plat/Cargo.toml (name \\\"owner-darwin-arm64\\\", version.workspace = true) referenced in [[fixed-group]] members alongside the owner -- run through the real Workspace::load -&gt; plan_version pipeline -- resolved \\\"owner-darwin-arm64\\\" as an ordinary GroupMember::Package (via index.resolve_human, since it has its own valid Cargo package name), producing its own independent PlannedBump that writes to its own Cargo.toml directly, with plan.platform_writes remaining empty. No Cargo-format manifest can currently become a GroupMember::PlatformManifest through the real discovery pipeline, so AC-002b's scenario cannot be constructed end-to-end as the criterion (and this task's explicit instruction to prove it via plan_version's real return value) requires.\"\n  },\n  \"reasoning\": \"AC-007 is provably satisfiable with existing TASK-2 code (verified by reading the loop). AC-002b's premise fails at the discovery layer (walk.rs), several layers before plan_version even runs, and the spec's own non_goals explicitly assumes group-membership validity/discovery is out of this track's scope and already correct -- but it isn't, for the Cargo ecosystem. Hand-constructing a GroupTable to bypass real discovery would satisfy neither the criterion's intent nor this task's explicit 'not a direct call in isolation' instruction, so I stopped rather than fake it. Did not commit anything since TASK-3's single commit message covers both criteria as one unit and only one could be honestly completed.\"\n}\n```\n\nRelevant paths:\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs` (unchanged, clean at HEAD `4726863`)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:196-217` (the Npm-only platform-registration gate)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs:161-165,202-206` (index.platform lookup that produces `GroupMember::PlatformManifest`)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json` (AC-002b, AC-007, non_goals #6)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/PLAN-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json` (TASK-3)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>89030</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>30</tool_uses><duration_ms>350155</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
