{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:02:53.019Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a62326ed4b363d714</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Ssk455DhhEJx6nchcAJHAG</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a62326ed4b363d714.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Correct Track 2 spec AC-002b contradiction (retry)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>The correction is complete. The spec file at `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json` has been revised in place. Summary of what changed and why:\n\n**Decision: option (a)** — narrowed AC-002b rather than converting it to a non-goal, because the OpenContext/workspace-inheritance resolution logic (AC-002's format-agnostic machinery) is real work this track owns and can prove today; discarding the whole criterion to a non-goal would have thrown away a legitimate, currently-provable guarantee along with the genuinely out-of-scope discovery gap.\n\n**Changes made:**\n1. **AC-002b** rewritten to explicitly state that real, disk-discovered Cargo platform-manifest classification does not work today (citing walk.rs:199's `Ecosystem::Npm`-only gate), and to scope the criterion to a fixture-constructed `GroupMember::PlatformManifest` fed directly into `plan_version` — proving the OpenContext resolution logic is format-agnostic without depending on discovery that doesn't exist yet.\n2. **New non_goals entry added** explicitly naming \"extending walk.rs's Ecosystem::Npm gate to Ecosystem::Cargo\" as deferred, out-of-scope future work, clarifying that this track's machinery will work once that