{"parentUuid":"19a49539-774d-483a-8b0b-38e9efc7a875","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce95NjHhofmjW6qbx8SFD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014i1ozCyS3GkmrNtyD8UAAQ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Exit-gate corrected Track 2 spec","subagent_type":"canon:exit-gate","prompt":"Issue a binding pass/fail verdict on the corrected spec@1 at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json (id SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES). This spec previously passed exit-gate (3 rounds) and began implementation. A lambda-implementer working TASK-3 then found and reported a genuine contradiction: AC-002b required a real, disk-discovered Cargo-format platform manifest to become a GroupMember::PlatformManifest, but walk.rs:199's platform-manifest discovery is gated to `if *eco == Ecosystem::Npm` with no Cargo branch — confirmed independently by two readers (the implementer and the orchestrating process) that this scenario is unreachable through the real pipeline today.\n\nA canon-drafter correction (canon/correct mode) was just applied: AC-002b was narrowed (option a, not converted to a non_goal) to instead verify the OpenContext/workspace-inheritance resolution logic directly, using a test-constructed GroupMember::PlatformManifest fixture (bypassing walk.rs discovery) rather than requiring the full real-discovery pipeline to already support Cargo. A new non_goals entry was added explicitly deferring the walk.rs Ecosystem::Npm-to-Cargo discovery extension as separate, out-of-scope future work. This is documented in the spec's revision_note field.\n\nRead the full spec fresh from disk — do not trust this summary. Verify: (1) AC-002b's new text is internally consistent and genuinely testable (does it now describe a scenario a competent implementer can actually build and run, without requiring walk.rs discovery to work?), (2) the new non_goals entry accurately