nt (`ManifestFormat::from_path`, `ManifestDecl::new`, `open`, `current_version`) and confirmed both tests genuinely fail (red), then restored the real implementation byte-for-byte and confirmed green again.\n- `cargo fmt -p callisto-graph`, `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n- Full suite: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib` → 371 passed, 0 failed.\n- Committed as `b5a9123`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"TASK-4\",\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"confirmed clean tree at TASK-2 HEAD (431feb9) via git log/status\",\n    \"read AC-008 acceptance criterion text directly from spec file on disk\",\n    \"reviewed TASK-2's landed Case D hybrid-root fixture convention for consistency\",\n    \"wrote plan_version_returns_err_when_platform_manifest_missing_from_disk_at_plan_time\",\n    \"wrote plan_version_returns_err_when_platform_manifest_content_is_malformed (per review-extended test.description)\",\n    \"verified red: temporarily swallowed each ?-propagation site, confirmed both tests fail\",\n    \"restored real implementation byte-for-byte, confirmed both tests green\",\n    \"ran cargo fmt -p callisto-graph\",\n    \"ran cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings (clean)\",\n    \"ran full cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib (371 passed, 0 failed)\",\n    \"committed\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"b5a9123\",\n  \"criteria_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-008\",\n      \"test_file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 853,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 291\n    }\n  ],\n  \"concerns\": \"This task adds no new implementation code by design (depends_on TASK-2, which already implements the full ?-based propagation chain). Genuine red/green TDD was demonstrated indirectly: instead of a red phase preceding implementation, I temporarily broke each error-propagation site to confirm the new tests would fail if the propagation regressed, then restored the shipped implementation unchanged. This matches the plan's own expected_failure note for this task.\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Verified via manual mutation that both tests are non-vacuous: swallowing the error at from_path/ManifestDecl::new/open/current_version caused both new tests to fail with the plan's Ok(VersionPlan{...platform_writes: []...}) printed, proving the tests genuinely exercise the ? propagation and not some unrelated early return.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>76383</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>297437</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"669c1a16-65d8-45df-8d11-04d6b9477627","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:05:14.121Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
