" end-to-end, contradicting the new non_goals entry. Fixed: purpose now explicitly says this is delivered end-to-end for npm only, with Cargo/maturin handled by the same format-agnostic machinery but not yet reachable through real discovery, cross-referencing non_goals.\n\nRead the full spec fresh from disk -- do not trust this summary, verify these three fixes actually landed and are internally consistent. Independently re-verify against live code: crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:213-216 (confirm ManifestRole::Platform is really what gets stored for a real npm platform manifest), crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs:104-106 (confirm the Platform-role-vs-CargoToml-format rejection you cited last round), and re-check that AC-002b's fixture-construction approach (Workspace::load + pushing a member into ws.config.groups.fixed) is genuinely buildable as you confirmed in retry 1 -- this shouldn't have changed, but verify it wasn't broken by the edit.\n\nThis is the second gate of this correction cycle. Per the standard protocol, if this fails, escalation happens above retry_count 3 for this correction cycle (same threshold as any other exit-gate cycle) -- give this the same thoroughness as retry 1. Apply your standard adversarial pass/fail standard: every acceptance criterion testable, no vague language, no TBDs, error cases covered, scope narrow enough for one planning cycle. Default disposition is fail. Output a verdict@1 with artifact_type \"spec@1\" and retry_count 2."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2098,"cache_read_input_tokens":727489,"output_tokens":1313,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2098,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_t