{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:13:43.239Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3297f61b0a204f27</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a3297f61b0a204f27.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Exit-gate corrected Track 2 spec (retry 2)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result># VERDICT: PASS (unconditional)\n\nVerdict file: `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/verdict-spec-track2-retry2.json`\n\n```json\n{ \"verdict\": \"pass\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"artifact_type\": \"spec@1\", \"retry_count\": 2 }\n```\n\nSpec read fresh from `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json`. I did not trust the summary — all three fixes verified in the file text, then re-grounded against live code.\n\n## The three retry-1 blockers\n\n**1. AC-002b vacuity — closed.** The criterion now carries the owner-bump precondition verbatim and asserts `platform_writes` contains **EXACTLY ONE** entry with `manifest == P`, `from == \"3.2.1\"`, `version == Y`. A test finding zero entries now fails on cardinality. Cross-checked against the landed producer at `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:283-300`: the loop `continue`s when the owner has no entry in `bump_by_pkg`, so the precondition is load-bearing, and AC-006 states the same contract consistently.\n\n**2. Unfalsifiable Canonical-role clause — closed, and correctly grounded.**\n- `walk.rs:199` is `if *eco == Ecosystem::Npm` — the gate is real.\n- `walk.rs:213-216` inserts `(primary_id, manifest_rel, role)` *inside* the `if let ManifestRole::Platform { .. } = role` guard at line 201, so the stored role is guaranteed Platform. The spec's \"mirroring exactly\" claim is accurate.\n- Extra link the spec implies but doesn't cite, which I confirmed: `config/groups.rs:161-167` forwards `role: role.clone()` straight into `GroupMember::PlatformManifest` — so the fixture mirrors reality, not an unreachable state.\n- `package.rs:104-106` is exactly `matches!(role, ManifestRole::Platform { .. }) &amp;&amp; format == ManifestFormat::CargoToml → Err(...)`. The falsification path is real, and the landed code survives it (it destructures `{ owner, path, .. }`, discarding role).\n\n**3. `purpose` contradiction — closed.** Now scopes end-to-end delivery to npm and cross-references the non_goals entry. No residual conflict.\n\n## Fixture buildability re-verified (not assumed unchanged)\n\nThe critical question was whether a post-`load` mutation is even observed. It is: `lib.rs:109` assigns `config.groups` inside `Workspace::load`, and `version.rs:283` reads `ws.config.groups.fixed` at plan time. All needed fields are public (`Workspace.config`, `GroupTable.fixed`, `GroupDef.members`, the `GroupMember` variant fields), with in-tree precedent at `aggregate.rs:1184-1193`.\n\nThe Cargo inheritance chain also holds end to end — `cargo.rs:47-52` (detect) → `CargoToml::open`'s `inheritance: ctx.cargo_workspace.clone()` → `cargo.rs:178-189` (`Ok(inherited)` when Some, `Err(WorkspaceInherited)` when None) → `cargo.rs:579-587`. So `from == \"3.2.1\"` is the correct discriminator between a working and a broken `OpenContext` derivation.\n\n## Full-spec sweep\n\nAll 15 criteria assert on observable values; no vague language. Only `TBD` hit in the file is the meta-phrase \"No TBDs remain\" in the private `reasoning` scratchpad. Error cases carry `is_error_case: true` (AC-008, AC-012), with AC-012/AC-012b partitioned so they cannot claim the same input. Scope is three files behind six explicit non_goals — one planning cycle, no split warranted.\n\nTwo cosmetic inaccuracies exist and are **not** blockers, require no fix, and this pass is not conditioned on them: AC-002b's parenthetical credits `lib.rs` with a \"documented test-construction pattern\" that lives in `aggregate.rs` instead, and \"pushing the member into `ws.config.groups.fixed`\" is loose for a `BTreeMap`. Neither creates an implementer judgment call about what correct means — the criterion states the full construction independently. Failing on citation polish would be gate theater in the opposite direction.\n\nCleared for vector. Escalation threshold (&gt;3) not reached.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>72200</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>243603</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
