mt -p callisto-graph`: clean.\n- `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib`: 376 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo test -p callisto-graph` (full crate, all binaries/integration tests/doctests): all green, exit code 0.\n- Commit `ef1c6334` — `test(graph): pin AC-007b merged optional_dep_updates for two platform siblings` — was created (140 insertions only, matching the intended test-only diff).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"TASK-6\",\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"verified_clean_tree_and_prereq_commits\",\n    \"read_AC-007b_from_spec_file\",\n    \"wrote_failing-capable_test_following_TASK-3_fixture_pattern\",\n    \"confirmed_test_detects_regression_via_temporary_sabotage_of_merge_key\",\n    \"reverted_sabotage_restoring_TASK-5_implementation_unchanged\",\n    \"cargo_fmt\",\n    \"cargo_clippy_-D_warnings_clean\",\n    \"cargo_test_lib_376_passed\",\n    \"cargo_test_full_crate_all_green\",\n    \"committed\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"ef1c6334\",\n  \"criteria_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-007b\",\n      \"test_file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 1108,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 322\n    }\n  ],\n  \"concerns\": null,\n  \"reasoning\": \"TASK-5 already shipped the BTreeMap&lt;PathBuf, Vec&lt;(String, Version)&gt;&gt;::entry(...).or_default().push(...) keying (version.rs:322-326) that merges by owner canonical manifest path. This task's own definition states no new implementation is expected. Since there was no true pre-implementation red state available, I verified test validity by deliberately breaking the merge key (appending the platform name to the path) and confirming the test failed with the exact 2-vs-1 divergence AC-007b targets, then reverted to TASK-5's real code untouched. Full crate test suite and clippy are clean; commit landed via the environment's checkpoint auto-commit exactly matching the intended diff (140 insertions, test-only).\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>69528</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>41</tool_uses><duration_ms>617287</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
