ion (`\"cargo:pkg-*\"` vs `\"npm:pkg-*\"`), backed by `PackageId::matches`, with a dedicated error (`BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems`, `docs/01-spec.md:1572-1576`) telling the user to add an ecosystem prefix when a bare name-pattern is ambiguous across ecosystems. This is tested, working, and structurally exactly \"name + publish-method(ecosystem) uniqueness.\"\n\n**Q2 — GitHub Action JSON dependency.** Only two real `jq` sites parse callisto's own JSON output (as opposed to `gh` CLI output, which is separate and unaffected):\n- `action.yml:164`: `callisto matrix --format json | jq -c '[.platformTargets[].targets[]] | unique_by(.artifactName)'` — reads `MatrixReport.platformTargets[].targets[].artifactName`.\n- `action.yml:202`: `echo \"$PLAN_JSON\" | jq -r '.releases[]?.tagName // empty'` — reads a `.releases[].tagName` field off `callisto plan-publish --format json`'s output, also passed opaquely to `callisto tag --plan \"$PLAN_JSON\"`.\n\nEverything else is exit-code or CLI-invocation based, not structural JSON parsing: `callisto status --check` (line 87) branches purely on `$?` (0/1/2), no JSON read at all; `callisto publish`, `callisto tag`, `git push` are shelled out to directly with no output parsing. Confirmed independently: this exit-code branch is already broken as shipped — it treats exit 0 as \"has changesets,\" but the documented/real contract is 1=pending/2=none, so that branch is currently unreachable in real runs, a pre-existing bug unrelated to the JSON-shape question.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>805999</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>7</tool_uses><duration_ms>100793</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"7495c1bf-5500-4ecc-9928-8a01a4cf9454","timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:11:50.934Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"7495c1bf-5500-4ecc-9928-8a01a4cf9454","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9spY1sVgB7PkKNDNkKC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1620,"cache_read_input_tokens":796213,"output_tokens":3139,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2063},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1620,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3139,"cache_read_input_tokens":796213,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1620,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1620},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9soMnBw64sP7dGpSdgs","type":"assistant","uuid":"b490f6a8-954f-41ea-83b9-bc259eea5849","timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:12:32.707Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"b490f6a8-954f-41ea-83b9-bc259eea5849","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9spY1sVgB7PkKNDNkKC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good news on both fronts — the code is in better shape than the original framing suggested.\n\n**Decision 1 — confirmed, your instinct is right.** The docs *do* deliberately specify path-based matching (`match = \"crates/*\"` in a worked example, plus the spec's formal §14 algorithm defines the match target as \"workspace-relative path\") — so this isn't a typo, it's a real doc/code mismatch. But: **no real config anywhere in the repo uses path-style patterns**, and the code already has a working, tested, deliberate name+ecosystem mechanism (`PackagePattern` in `config/pattern.rs`) — glob on name, with an `ecosystem:` prefix for disambiguation (`cargo:pkg-*` vs `npm:pkg-*`), plus its own dedicated error (`BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems`) that tells the user to add an ecosystem prefix when a bare name is ambiguous. That's exactly \"name + publish method disambiguates.\" **Recommendation: keep the code as-is, correct the docs** — no behavior change, no risk to any real config, and it matches what you described.\n\n**Decision 2 — you're right, and it simplifies things a lot.** The Action barely touches JSON. Only two `jq` sites read callisto's own JSON output at all: `MatrixReport.platformTargets[].targets[].artifactName` and `.releases[].tagName` from `plan-publish`'s output. Everything else — `status --check`, `publish`, `tag`, `git push` — is exit-code/CLI-invocation based, no parsing. So the six report types the original audit flagged (`StatusReport`, `SnapshotReport`, `ComposePrBodyReport`, `CreatedTag`, `ValidateReport`, `InitReport`) mostly aren't things the Action structurally depends on — fixing their field-shape mismatches is lower-risk than the original framing implied. Only `MatrixReport` and whatever report carries `.releases[].tagName` need careful coordination with the Action."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1620,"cache_read_input_tokens":796213,"output_tokens":3139,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2063},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1620,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3139,"cache_read_input_tokens":796213,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1620,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1620},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9soMnBw64sP7dGpSdgs","type":"assistant","uuid":"3e0f3219-8852-4aad-afdb-ee01f7c3e969","timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:12:38.708Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"3e0f3219-8852-4aad-afdb-ee01f7c3e969","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9spY1sVgB7PkKNDNkKC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XohHarHV5nV4zCHtkda6wB","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"Given this, how do you want to proceed on the wire-format versioning for the two report types the Action actually reads?","header":"Wire format","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Bump schemaVersion for MatrixReport + the plan-publish report; correctness-fix the rest (Recommended)","description":"Since only MatrixReport and the plan-publish report's tagName field are structurally consumed by the shipped Action, give those two a proper major-rev bump coordinated with an Action update. The other four report types (StatusReport, SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport, InitReport, ValidateReport) can just be corrected — nothing in the shipped Action parses their fields structurally, so there's no real break to version around."},{"label":"Bump schemaVersion on all six report types uniformly","description":"Simpler mental model — every report type gets the same versioning treatment regardless of whether the Action actually reads it, in case some other external consumer parses them that we don't know about."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1620,"cache_read_input_tokens":796213,"output_tokens":3139,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2063},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1620,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3139,"cache_read_input_tokens":796213,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1620,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16