{"parentUuid":"3251e3de-f945-4887-b525-29069d99051a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9suHSffWjnQXMK7Yg8m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Hxw6D5VemN1D2aooVjVhjD","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/00-design.md","offset":1300,"limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1666,"cache_read_input_tokens":801117,"output_tokens":590,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":473},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1666,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":590,"cache_read_input_tokens":801117,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1666,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1666},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9su3DQSqgnMpFJZu46c","type":"assistant","uuid":"ea5ed8ed-653a-4049-b38d-abf54ef6d568","timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:13:19.759Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"ea5ed8ed-653a-4049-b38d-abf54ef6d568","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3f6d3ffe-8d7a-40a5-97d2-978434159727","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hxw6D5VemN1D2aooVjVhjD","type":"tool_result","content":"1300\t    tool's steady-state behavior, not v0.1's — P5 (§6.3).\n1301\t20. Platform manifests never receive an independent git tag; only the napi main package (and\n1302\t    the crate, if separately published) are tag-bearing release points — P5 (§7.5, §9.2).\n1303\t21. Fixed-group `members` config is authoritative; `napi.targets` is read every run purely as\n1304\t    a non-authoritative cross-check and never auto-mutates `callisto.toml` — membership\n1305\t    changes are only ever written via an explicit, reviewable `init`/sync flow — P2, P5\n1306\t    (§5.3, §7.5).\n1307\t22. A fixed-group member with no prior release tag is exempt from the pre-mutation\n1308\t    divergence check and is unconditionally force-set to the group's target version on its\n1309\t    first inclusion — P3, P5 (§7.5, §7.6).\n1310\t23. **`compose-pr-body` must run before `version`** in any orchestration flow, because\n1311\t    `version` deletes the changeset files `compose-pr-body` reads — P5 (§12.2).\n1312\t24. **Git tags are never created at `version` time**; a tag is only ever created after the\n1313\t    publish it represents has actually succeeded, and only pushed by the calling workflow,\n1314\t    never by callisto — creating a tag before a publish succeeds would let P2's stateless\n1315\t    detection mistake a partial failure for a completed release — P2, P3 (§9.1).\n1316\t25. **`PackageId` → tag-name resolution is exactly one function** in `callisto-model`, used\n1317\t    identically by fixed-group forcing (§7.5), `plan-publish`'s `releases[].tagName` (§9.2),\n1318\t    and `last_tag_for`'s glob-and-extract search (§9.1) — two independently-evolved\n1319\t    resolution paths for the same concept is precisely the failure class documented in\n1320\t    release-please's `#2207` — P5 (§9.1).\n1321\t26. The coordination core (`callisto-format`, `callisto-model`, `callisto-graph`,\n1322\t    `callisto-manifests`, `callisto-conventional`, `callisto-changelog`) has zero moon in\n1323\t    its dependency tree, and passes its fixture suite under `wasmtime` with only the\n1324\t    workspace root preopened — both CI-enforced from v0.1, before `callisto-moon` exists —\n1325\t    P5, P7 (§0.1).\n1326\t27. `callisto-cli/src` contains no graph-construction or cascade code — CI-enforced — the\n1327\t    automated version of \"don't become knope\" (§0.1's decision doc) — P5, P6.\n1328\t28. Every default that fires and could defensibly have gone the other way names its\n1329\t    governing config key in human-readable output; the corresponding plan/report value type\n1330\t    carries an optional attribution field (`.bumps[].governedBy`, §12.5) — a config key\n1331\t    discoverable only by reading the docs is a design defect, not a docs gap — P5, P7\n1332\t    (§18 Q5.4).\n1333\t\n1334\t---\n1335\t\n1336\t## 14. Config format\n1337\t\n1338\tHybrid: workspace-level `callisto.toml` for cross-package concerns, per-project `moon.yml`\n1339\textension block for package-scoped overrides.\n1340\t\n1341\t```toml\n1342\t# callisto.toml\n1343\t[changesets]\n1344\tdir = \".changeset\"\n1345\t\n1346\t[cascade]\n1347\tmode = \"out-of-range\"   # out-of-range | always — §7.4's cascade-trigger axis: WHEN to\n1348\t                         # cascade a dependent at all (default: only when its declared spec\n1349\t                         # no longer covers the new version)\n1350\tbump-severity = \"patch\"   # patch | minor — §7.4's cascade-severity axis: HOW HARD to bump a\n1351\t                           # dependent once cascade fires (a distinct axis from `mode` above;\n1352\t                           # earlier drafts conflated these into one four-value key)\n1353\tpeer-escalation = true   # peer-dep out-of-range non-patch escalates to major (§13 inv. 9);\n1354\t                          # true by default, opt-out not opt-in — set false to disable\n1355\tpreserve-npm-ranges = true   # §7.3/§13 inv. 15 — if a bump can't be confidently\n1356\t                              # round-tripped, leave the original range string untouched and\n1357\t                              # warn rather than overwriting it; this key gates whether\n1358\t                              # range-preserving rewrite is attempted at all (true is the\n1359\t                              # only sane default — false would mean always overwriting to"}]},"uuid":"f4cfd471-43c4-4e75-a3eb-4e25d8c03988","timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:13:19.826Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/00-design.md","content":"    tool's steady-state behavior, not v0.1's — P5 (§6.3).\n20. Platform manifests never receive an independent git tag; only the napi main package (and\n    the crate, if separately published) are tag-bearing release points — P5 (§7.5, §9.2).\n21. Fixed-group `members` config is authoritative; `napi.targets` is read every run purely as\n    a non-authoritative cross-check and never auto-mutates `callisto.toml` — membership\n    changes are only ever written via an explicit, reviewable `init`/sync flow — P2, P5\n    (§5.3, §7.5).\n22. A fixed-group member with no prior release tag is exempt from the pre-mutation\n    divergence check and is unconditionally force-set to the group's target version on its\n    first inclusion — P3, P5 (§7.5, §7.6).\n23. **`compose-pr-body` must run before `version`** in any orchestration flow, because\n    `version` deletes the changeset files `compose-pr-body` reads — P5 (§12.2).\n24. **Git tags are never created at `version` time**; a tag is only ever created after the\n    publish it represents has actually succeeded, and only pushed by the calling workflow,\n    never by callisto — creating a tag before a publish succeeds would let P2's stateless\n    detection mistake a partial failure for a completed release — P2, P3 (§9.1).\n25. **`PackageId` → tag-name resolution is exactly one function** in `callisto-model`, used\n    identically by fixed-group forcing (§7.5), `plan-publish`'s `releases[].tagName` (§9.2),\n    and `last_tag_for`'s glob-and-extract search (§9.1) — two independently-evolved\n    resolution paths for the same concept is precisely the failure class documented in\n    release-please's `#2207` — P5 (§9.1).\n26. The coordination core (`callisto-format`, `callisto-model`, `callisto-graph`,\n    `callisto-manifests`, `callisto-conventional`, `callisto-changelog`) has zero moon in\n    its dependency tree, and passes its fixture suite under `wasmtime` with only the\n    workspace root preopened — both CI-enforced from v0.1, before `callisto-moon` exists —\n    P5, P7 (§0.1).\n27. `callisto-cli/src` contains no graph-construction or cascade code — CI-enforced — the\n    automated version of \"don't become knope\" (§0.1's decision doc) — P5, P6.\n28. Every default that fires and could defensibly have gone the other way names its\n    governing config key in human-readable output; the corresponding plan/report value type\n    carries an optional attribution field (`.bumps[].governedBy`, §12.5) — a config key\n    discoverable only by reading the docs is a design defect, not a docs gap — P5, P7\n    (§18 Q5.4).\n\n---\n\n## 14. Config format\n\nHybrid: workspace-level `callisto.toml` for cross-package concerns, per-project `moon.yml`\nextension block for package-scoped overrides.\n\n```toml\n# callisto.toml\n[changesets]\ndir = \".changeset\"\n\n[cascade]\nmode = \"out-of-range\"   # out-of-range | always — §7.4's cascade-trigger axis: WHEN to\n                         # cascade a dependent at all (default: only when its declared spec\n                         # no longer covers the new version)\nbump-severity = \"patch\"   # patch | minor — §7.4's cascade-severity axis: HOW HARD to bump a\n                           # dependent once cascade fires (a distinct axis from `mode` above;\n                           # earlier drafts conflated these into one four-value key)\npeer-escalation = true   # peer-dep out-of-range non-patch escalates to major (§13 inv. 9);\n                          # true by default, opt-out not opt-in — set false to disable\npreserve-npm-ranges = true   # §7.3/§13 inv. 15 — if a bump can't be confidently\n                              # round-tripped, leave the original range string untouched and\n                              # warn rather than overwriting it; this key gates whether\n                              # range-preserving rewrite is attempted at all (true is the\n                              # only sane default — false would mean always overwriting to","numLines":60,"startLine":1300,"totalLines":2185}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ea5ed8ed-653a-4049-b38d-abf54ef6d568","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
