{"parentUuid":"48492412-6f98-4a96-b1f9-6b767881641b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9sv6WsQ4TSadPRzuhLj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012L6iEGEje4MUUnVkoUK7xW","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/00-design.md","offset":1393,"limit":45},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2226,"cache_read_input_tokens":802783,"output_tokens":210,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":93},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2226,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":210,"cache_read_input_tokens":802783,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2226},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9suunhSt6ZG6N5SgABj","type":"assistant","uuid":"3fe26b72-f8ff-4d63-85bf-7cf440822605","timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:13:27.319Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"3fe26b72-f8ff-4d63-85bf-7cf440822605","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3f6d3ffe-8d7a-40a5-97d2-978434159727","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012L6iEGEje4MUUnVkoUK7xW","type":"tool_result","content":"1393\tname = \"foo-and-its-cli-docs\"\n1394\tmembers = [\"foo\", \"foo-docs\"]   # share a version only when jointly touched (§7.5) —\n1395\t                                 # previously defined in §7.5 as a first-class peer of\n1396\t                                 # fixed-group but never given a config block\n1397\t\n1398\t[registries.cratesIo]\n1399\ttype = \"cargo\"\n1400\t[registries.npm]\n1401\ttype = \"npm\"\n1402\t```\n1403\t\n1404\t**Path-like values (`[changesets].dir`, `[[package]]`/`[[package-set]] changelog`) always use\n1405\tforward slashes (`/`), never backslashes, regardless of the OS the value was authored or is\n1406\tread on.** `callisto.toml` is checked into version control and read by developers and CI on\n1407\twhatever platform they're on; the parsed value goes through the same `workspace_relative`\n1408\tnormalization used for real filesystem-discovered paths (`callisto-model`'s `workspace_relative`), which only *converts* a\n1409\tnative separator to `/` on the platform that's actually running — on POSIX, `\\` is a legal\n1410\tfilename character, not a separator, so a Windows-authored `dir = \"custom\\\\subdir\"` value\n1411\twould be read back as one oddly-named directory (`custom\\subdir`, one component) rather than\n1412\ttwo nested ones the moment the same file is read on macOS or Linux CI. Writing `dir =\n1413\t\"custom/subdir\"` is portable on every platform this tool runs on, including Windows.\n1414\t\n1415\t```yaml\n1416\t# packages/foo/moon.yml\n1417\textensions:\n1418\t  callisto:\n1419\t    package-name: foo\n1420\t    release-trigger: changeset\n1421\t    publish-to: [cratesIo, npm]\n1422\t    tag-template: \"foo@{version}\"\n1423\t```\n1424\t\n1425\tDiscovery walks the workspace (moon's project graph when available for authoritative\n1426\tproject roots, `ignore`-crate walk otherwise — `ProjectLocator`, §0.1/§15); `package-set`\n1427\tmatches expand to concrete packages; explicit `[[package]]` entries always win over set\n1428\tmatches. A set matching nothing, or two sets claiming the same package, is a hard config\n1429\terror. **Group membership validation, at parse time (P5), not at mutation time**: a package\n1430\tmust belong to at most one `[[fixed-group]]` and at most one `[[linked-group]]`, and the\n1431\tfixed and linked member sets must be disjoint — reject with a clear error listing the\n1432\tconflicting groups, rather than letting an ambiguous membership surface as a confusing\n1433\tmutation-time alignment failure.\n1434\t\n1435\t---\n1436\t\n1437\t## 15. Architecture"}]},"uuid":"7005d347-caf8-4db4-abc5-b68346c80e69","timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:13:27.385Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/00-design.md","content":"name = \"foo-and-its-cli-docs\"\nmembers = [\"foo\", \"foo-docs\"]   # share a version only when jointly touched (§7.5) —\n                                 # previously defined in §7.5 as a first-class peer of\n                                 # fixed-group but never given a config block\n\n[registries.cratesIo]\ntype = \"cargo\"\n[registries.npm]\ntype = \"npm\"\n```\n\n**Path-like values (`[changesets].dir`, `[[package]]`/`[[package-set]] changelog`) always use\nforward slashes (`/`), never backslashes, regardless of the OS the value was authored or is\nread on.** `callisto.toml` is checked into version control and read by developers and CI on\nwhatever platform they're on; the parsed value goes through the same `workspace_relative`\nnormalization used for real filesystem-discovered paths (`callisto-model`'s `workspace_relative`), which only *converts* a\nnative separator to `/` on the platform that's actually running — on POSIX, `\\` is a legal\nfilename character, not a separator, so a Windows-authored `dir = \"custom\\\\subdir\"` value\nwould be read back as one oddly-named directory (`custom\\subdir`, one component) rather than\ntwo nested ones the moment the same file is read on macOS or Linux CI. Writing `dir =\n\"custom/subdir\"` is portable on every platform this tool runs on, including Windows.\n\n```yaml\n# packages/foo/moon.yml\nextensions:\n  callisto:\n    package-name: foo\n    release-trigger: changeset\n    publish-to: [cratesIo, npm]\n    tag-template: \"foo@{version}\"\n```\n\nDiscovery walks the workspace (moon's project graph when available for authoritative\nproject roots, `ignore`-crate walk otherwise — `ProjectLocator`, §0.1/§15); `package-set`\nmatches expand to concrete packages; explicit `[[package]]` entries always win over set\nmatches. A set matching nothing, or two sets claiming the same package, is a hard config\nerror. **Group membership validation, at parse time (P5), not at mutation time**: a package\nmust belong to at most one `[[fixed-group]]` and at most one `[[linked-group]]`, and the\nfixed and linked member sets must be disjoint — reject with a clear error listing the\nconflicting groups, rather than letting an ambiguous membership surface as a confusing\nmutation-time alignment failure.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Architecture","numLines":45,"startLine":1393,"totalLines":2185}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3fe26b72-f8ff-4d63-85bf-7cf440822605","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
