{"parentUuid":"4b26715f-43dd-4db3-bbea-42b038772f39","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9syDhYscdMri7e3aoRu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014QSP1QoXu7AQ3XrK6XRTRw","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","offset":6310,"limit":40},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1258,"cache_read_input_tokens":807394,"output_tokens":267,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":121},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1258,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":267,"cache_read_input_tokens":807394,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1258,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1258},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9sy2RdwrxLwfGzTWrXj","type":"assistant","uuid":"51f00f1c-b3a2-4102-8115-699cac62d9de","timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:14:09.737Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"51f00f1c-b3a2-4102-8115-699cac62d9de","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3f6d3ffe-8d7a-40a5-97d2-978434159727","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014QSP1QoXu7AQ3XrK6XRTRw","type":"tool_result","content":"6310\t   (`[changesets]`, `[cascade]`, `[validation]`, `[registries.*]`).\n6311\t\n6312\tAnything unset falls back to a built-in default, and `ResolvedConfig` records *which* of those\n6313\ttwo happened per key (§G.5.4's provenance), because §18 Q5.2's `init` rule (\"write a key only\n6314\twhen the workspace's answer differs from callisto's built-in default\") and §13 invariant 28's\n6315\t`(default)` marker (§CLI.5.3) both need exactly that fact.\n6316\t\n6317\t```rust\n6318\t/// Read `callisto.toml` (absent is legal — every key has a default, §18 Q5.5's L1 workspace).\n6319\t/// Per-project `moon.yml` blocks are merged later, during graph construction (§G.4.1 step 4),\n6320\t/// since they are keyed by project root and the project set does not exist yet here.\n6321\tpub fn load(root: &Path) -> Result<ResolvedConfig, ConfigError>;\n6322\t```\n6323\t\n6324\t**Per-package resolution, in full.** Run during graph construction, once the project set is\n6325\tknown:\n6326\t\n6327\t```\n6328\tfor each discovered package P (by project root path, workspace-relative):\n6329\t    layers ← []\n6330\t    if moon.yml block exists at P's root              → layers.push(MoonYml, block)\n6331\t    if an explicit [[package]] whose `match` == P     → layers.push(CallistoToml, entry)\n6332\t    if P's [[fixed-group]] sets any per-package key   → layers.push(CallistoToml, group)\n6333\t    if P's [[linked-group]] sets any per-package key  → layers.push(CallistoToml, group)\n6334\t    for each [[package-set]] whose `match` glob ⊇ P   → collect\n6335\t        if more than one matches P                    → ConfigError::OverlappingPackageSets\n6336\t        else                                          → layers.push(CallistoToml, set)\n6337\t    layers.push(Default, derive_from_manifests(P))    # §18 Q5.2's derivation rules\n6338\t    resolve field-by-field, first layer that specifies the field wins;\n6339\t    record ConfigProvenance from the winning layer.\n6340\t\n6341\tafter all packages:\n6342\t    for each [[package-set]] that matched nothing     → ConfigError::PackageSetMatchedNothing\n6343\t    for each [[package]] that matched nothing         → ConfigError::PackageMatchedNothing\n6344\t```\n6345\t\n6346\t§14's \"two sets claiming the same package is a hard config error\" is `OverlappingPackageSets`;\n6347\tan explicit `[[package]]` overlapping a set is **not** an error — §14 says explicit entries\n6348\t\"always win over set matches,\" which presupposes the overlap.\n6349\t"}]},"uuid":"53207d20-0981-4dca-9339-fdd0bf49a65a","timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:14:09.801Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","content":"   (`[changesets]`, `[cascade]`, `[validation]`, `[registries.*]`).\n\nAnything unset falls back to a built-in default, and `ResolvedConfig` records *which* of those\ntwo happened per key (§G.5.4's provenance), because §18 Q5.2's `init` rule (\"write a key only\nwhen the workspace's answer differs from callisto's built-in default\") and §13 invariant 28's\n`(default)` marker (§CLI.5.3) both need exactly that fact.\n\n```rust\n/// Read `callisto.toml` (absent is legal — every key has a default, §18 Q5.5's L1 workspace).\n/// Per-project `moon.yml` blocks are merged later, during graph construction (§G.4.1 step 4),\n/// since they are keyed by project root and the project set does not exist yet here.\npub fn load(root: &Path) -> Result<ResolvedConfig, ConfigError>;\n```\n\n**Per-package resolution, in full.** Run during graph construction, once the project set is\nknown:\n\n```\nfor each discovered package P (by project root path, workspace-relative):\n    layers ← []\n    if moon.yml block exists at P's root              → layers.push(MoonYml, block)\n    if an explicit [[package]] whose `match` == P     → layers.push(CallistoToml, entry)\n    if P's [[fixed-group]] sets any per-package key   → layers.push(CallistoToml, group)\n    if P's [[linked-group]] sets any per-package key  → layers.push(CallistoToml, group)\n    for each [[package-set]] whose `match` glob ⊇ P   → collect\n        if more than one matches P                    → ConfigError::OverlappingPackageSets\n        else                                          → layers.push(CallistoToml, set)\n    layers.push(Default, derive_from_manifests(P))    # §18 Q5.2's derivation rules\n    resolve field-by-field, first layer that specifies the field wins;\n    record ConfigProvenance from the winning layer.\n\nafter all packages:\n    for each [[package-set]] that matched nothing     → ConfigError::PackageSetMatchedNothing\n    for each [[package]] that matched nothing         → ConfigError::PackageMatchedNothing\n```\n\n§14's \"two sets claiming the same package is a hard config error\" is `OverlappingPackageSets`;\nan explicit `[[package]]` overlapping a set is **not** an error — §14 says explicit entries\n\"always win over set matches,\" which presupposes the overlap.\n","numLines":40,"startLine":6310,"totalLines":11427}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"51f00f1c-b3a2-4102-8115-699cac62d9de","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
