{"parentUuid":"678ebe6c-f7f0-4526-aa37-32533ccf104d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9tCVBafbqf4VUJs4ps1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JhuWDBcpya14gLgpacHPDx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\ngit add docs/00-design.md docs/01-spec.md\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\ndocs: correct [[package]]/[[package-set]] match semantics to name-glob, not path\n\nBoth docs deliberately specified path-based match patterns (match =\n\"crates/*\", the spec's §14 algorithm defining P as a workspace-relative\npath). The shipped implementation (PackagePattern, config/pattern.rs)\nmatches the package's NAME instead, with an optional ecosystem: prefix\nto disambiguate a bare name-glob spanning ecosystems.\n\nConfirmed no real config anywhere in the repo uses path-style patterns,\nand the name+ecosystem mechanism is deliberate and already tested\n(BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems). Corrected the docs to describe the\nactual mechanism rather than rewriting the code -- this is Track 3a from\nthe remediation plan, resolved as a doc-only fix per the decision that\nname+ecosystem is the intended design going forward.\n\nAlso fixed BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems's own doc comment, which\nused a slash (cargo/name) instead of the real colon syntax (cargo:name).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HxMVynBHufrDkmRHgmKgcH\nEOF\n)\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2458,"cache_read_input_tokens":813111,"output_tokens":531,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2458,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":531,"cache_read_input_to