{"parentUuid":"a382eac1-02c0-435b-ae44-9f7af9546262","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"85d31ba4-6f8f-48e6-988f-afee4a454cec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CYhjZ2wFACA3RXikVo7naj","type":"tool_result","content":"1174-- `version --refresh-lockfiles` → `.bumps[]{package,from,to,severity}` (mandatory),\n1175-  `.bumps[].governedBy` (optional — the config key responsible for a non-default-path\n1176:  decision, e.g. `\"cascade.peer-escalation\"`; absent when the bump followed no named\n1177-  default, §13 invariant 28), `.lockfileRefreshResults[]{filename,refreshCommand,success,\n1178-  exitCode}` (optional — absent when `--refresh-lockfiles` wasn't passed)\n1179-- `plan-publish` → the shape in §9.2; `.rustCrates`/`.npmPlatformPackages`/\n1180-  `.npmMainPackages`/`.releases` mandatory as arrays (possibly empty), absence of the key\n1181-  entirely is a hard schema failure\n1182-- `snapshot` → `.version` (mandatory), `.packages[]{name, ecosystem}` (mandatory, possibly\n1183-  empty) — no `published`/`publishedPackages` fields; snapshot computes and writes a\n1184-  transient version (§8), it does not publish, so there is nothing \"published\" for this\n--\n1276-   never reorderable via config — P5.\n1277-9. Peer-dep out-of-range non-patch escalates to major on the dependent by default,\n1278:   opt-out not opt-in (`[cascade].peer-escalation`, §14) — P5.\n1279-10. Dev-dep out-of-range is `Severity::None` — spec rewrite only, no version bump — P5.\n1280-11. `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer detection is case-sensitive (uppercase only), matching the\n1281-    Conventional Commits spec exactly — P5.\n1282-12. Rerun-safety check at mutation time: re-read on-disk version, compare to the value\n1283-    captured at aggregation time (§7.6 step 1) — not the plan, which is written later, at\n1284-    step 10, after mutation — hard-error on drift — P3, P5.\n1285-13. Fixed-group alignment verified before any mutation, not during — P5.\n1286-14. Schema version is a first-class, versioned contract for every `--format json` output;\n--\n1351-                           # dependent once cascade fires (a distinct axis from `mode` above;\n1352-                           # earlier drafts conflated these into one four-value key)\n1353:peer-escalation = true   # peer-dep out-of-range non-patch escalates to major (§13 inv. 9);\n1354-                          # true by default, opt-out not opt-in — set false to disable\n1355-preserve-npm-ranges = true   # §7.3/§13 inv. 15 — if a bump can't be confidently\n1356-                              # round-tripped, leave the original range string untouched and\n1357-                              # warn rather than overwriting it; this key gates whether\n1358-                              # range-preserving rewrite is attempted at all (true is the\n1359-                              # only sane default — false would mean always overwriting to\n1360-                              # an exact version, knope-style, which this design rejects)\n1361-\n--\n1619-- **v0.1 — Rust + npm core.** `callisto-format` (byte-compat fixtures), `callisto-model` +\n1620-  `callisto-graph` (§7's full dependency graph and cascade table, §7.4 — all six\n1621:  edge-kind/coverage rows, including peer-escalation and dev-none, ship here since neither\n1622-  is napi-specific; a prior draft deferred them to v0.3 alongside groups, which was wrong —\n1623-  groups are napi-specific, the cascade table isn't), `callisto-manifests` (Cargo.toml +\n1624-  package.json, range preservation, `WorkspaceCargoResolver` for `[workspace.dependencies]`\n1625-  inheritance — committed here, not merely \"must be handled from v0.1\" in an open-questions\n1626-  aside), `callisto-changelog` (changelog generation — §7.6 step 7 is a mutation step of\n1627-  `version`, which ships here; previously unscheduled in any milestone despite this\n1628-  dependency), `callisto-cli` with `add`/`status`/`version`/`init`. Stateless `last_tag_for`\n1629-  primitive (§9.1's glob-and-extract resolution) built and used by `status` even before\n--\n1785-| `[[fixed-group]]` / `[[linked-group]]` | `fixed` / `linked` | No |\n1786-| `[[package-set]]` / `[[package]]` | `ignore`, plus per-package `access` | Partly — glob-set matching is new, the intent isn't |\n1787:| `[cascade].peer-escalation` | none (behavior is hardcoded) | Yes |\n1788-| `[cascade].preserve-npm-ranges` | none (always on, not configurable) | Yes, as an off-switch §14 already declines to recommend |\n1789-| `[validation].allow-empty-changesets` | none (§6.3's check doesn't exist there) | Yes |\n1790-| `release-trigger` (`Auto`) | none | Yes — v0.2 |\n1791-| `pre-major-inference` | none (release-please's `bumpMinorPreMajor`) | Yes — v0.2 |\n1792-| `tag-template` | none (tag shape is fixed) | Yes — but §9.1's default *is* changesets' shape |\n1793-| `publish-to` / `[registries.*]` | `access` + `.npmrc` | Roughly |\n1794-| `ManifestRole::Platform` / napi coordination | none | **Yes — this is the wedge (§2.1 cases E/F)** |\n1795-\n--","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a337e177-01cf-4c9c-84a7-a24d2fc643c2","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:06:08.930Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1174-- `version --refresh-lockfiles` → `.bumps[]{package,from,to,severity}` (mandatory),\n1175-  `.bumps[].governedBy` (optional — the config key responsible for a non-default-path\n1176:  decision, e.g. `\"cascade.peer-escalation\"`; absent when the bump followed no named\n1177-  default, §13 invariant 28), `.lockfileRefreshResults[]{filename,refreshCommand,success,\n1178-  exitCode}` (optional — absent when `--refresh-lockfiles` wasn't passed)\n1179-- `plan-publish` → the shape in §9.2; `.rustCrates`/`.npmPlatformPackages`/\n1180-  `.npmMainPackages`/`.releases` mandatory as arrays (possibly empty), absence of the key\n1181-  entirely is a hard schema failure\n1182-- `snapshot` → `.version` (mandatory), `.packages[]{name, ecosystem}` (mandatory, possibly\n1183-  empty) — no `published`/`publishedPackages` fields; snapshot computes and writes a\n1184-  transient version (§8), it does not publish, so there is nothing \"published\" for this\n--\n1276-   never reorderable via config — P5.\n1277-9. Peer-dep out-of-range non-patch escalates to major on the dependent by default,\n1278:   opt-out not opt-in (`[cascade].peer-escalation`, §14) — P5.\n1279-10. Dev-dep out-of-range is `Severity::None` — spec rewrite only, no version bump — P5.\n1280-11. `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer detection is case-sensitive (uppercase only), matching the\n1281-    Conventional Commits spec exactly — P5.\n1282-12. Rerun-safety check at mutation time: re-read on-disk version, compare to the value\n1283-    captured at aggregation time (§7.6 step 1) — not the plan, which is written later, at\n1284-    step 10, after mutation — hard-error on drift — P3, P5.\n1285-13. Fixed-group alignment verified before any mutation, not during — P5.\n1286-14. Schema version is a first-class, versioned contract for every `--format json` output;\n--\n1351-                           # dependent once cascade fires (a distinct axis from `mode` above;\n1352-                           # earlier drafts conflated these into one four-value key)\n1353:peer-escalation = true   # peer-dep out-of-range non-patch escalates to major (§13 inv. 9);\n1354-                          # true by default, opt-out not opt-in — set false to disable\n1355-preserve-npm-ranges = true   # §7.3/§13 inv. 15 — if a bump can't be confidently\n1356-                              # round-tripped, leave the original range string untouched and\n1357-                              # warn rather than overwriting it; this key gates whether\n1358-                              # range-preserving rewrite is attempted at all (true is the\n1359-                              # only sane default — false would mean always overwriting to\n1360-                              # an exact version, knope-style, which this design rejects)\n1361-\n--\n1619-