{"parentUuid":"6f09d524-0fcc-46c2-ab2c-aed6ac9d358b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9xLSMrWzw8GpqSHGcDV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019C1Jr4r13G8Zn36vPwxeZG","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review peer-escalation severity fix","subagent_type":"bug-hunter","prompt":"Read-only review of an uncommitted change in the callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Run `git diff crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs` to see the change — do NOT run `git stash`, `git checkout`, `git reset`, or `git clean`, this is read-only review of live uncommitted work.\n\nContext: `cascade_action`'s peer-dependency escalation had a confirmed-live bug — its `source: Severity` parameter (previously named `_source`, unused) was ignored, so every out-of-range peer dependency edge escalated to `Severity::Major` regardless of whether the real upstream change was Patch, Minor, or Major severity. Per this repo's own spec (docs/01-spec.md §7.4/§13 invariant 9), escalation to Major should only fire when the source severity is non-patch (Minor or Major); a patch-severity source should fall through to the ordinary `cfg.bump_severity` row instead. The fix adds `&& matches!(source, Severity::Minor | Severity::Major)` to the escalation guard's existing condition, and renames the parameter from `_source` to `source`.\n\nReview this change for: (1) scope adherence — does it do exactly this fix and nothing more, (2) correctness — does the guard condition genuinely match the spec's row 4/row 5 table (`docs/01-spec.md` lines ~7186-7202, read it directly to confirm) for ALL severity levels (None, Patch, Minor, Major) not just the three tested, (3) sibling gaps — is `cascade_action` called from anywhere else in the codebase that might depend on the old (buggy) always-Major behavior in a way this fix could break, and is there any OTHER place in the codebase that independently reimplements or duplicates this same peer-escalation logic that should have gotten the same fix but didn't, (4) test quality — does the new test `cascade_action_peer_escalation_only_fires_for_non_patch_source` genuinely exercise the fixed code path (not just check governed_by/escalated flags without pinning severity), and does it cover enough of the four severity levels to be confident the guard is right, not just the three that happen to compile.\n\nAlso check: `Severity::None` as a peer source — is there a real scenario where `cascade_action(Peer, DoesNotCover, Severity::None, cfg)` could be called, and if so, does the current match arm order handle it correctly (falls through to row 4, same as Patch)?\n\nReport findings via the standard categorized output: scope adherence, non-negotiable violations (this repo has `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"` as a hard invariant — confirm none introduced), sibling gaps, test quality. Do not modify any files."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":571,"cache_read_input_tokens":854953,"output_tokens":1143,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":98},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":571,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1143,"cache_read_input_tokens":854953,"cache_creation_input_tokens":571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":571},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9xLFSXcVHZ4oAVEADqo","type":"assistant","uuid":"70fedea0-c7f4-4136-b0c2-33fd42bd5a5b","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:11:34.008Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","v