{"parentUuid":"aacfbed5-e12b-4da7-81ad-46106874e76b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9xknnr27HkLwboY8Kk7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`IdentityIndex` already derives `Clone`. I have everything needed. Drafting the requirement and dispatching canon-drafter."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":969,"cache_read_input_tokens":864961,"output_tokens":3180,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":969,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3180,"cache_read_input_tokens":864961,"cache_creation_input_tokens":969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":969},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9xkfvMSLFBnSFwaTuaC","type":"assistant","uuid":"90dbdc78-36aa-4bca-84bc-04057225dbcc","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:16:54.084Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"90dbdc78-36aa-4bca-84bc-04057225dbcc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9xknnr27HkLwboY8Kk7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FYMEAco6JrpxzW5Yr2bLNo","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Draft Track 9 spec (cascade correctness)","subagent_type":"canon:drafter","prompt":"Draft a spec@1 from the following requirement@1 for the callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Produce the actual spec@1 JSON object as your final output — do not describe a plan to draft it, do the drafting work yourself in this invocation.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"REQ-TRACK9-CASCADE-REWRITE-KEY-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"statement\": \"Fix a confirmed-live bug: crate::cascade::solve_cascade builds dependency-spec rewrite keys from PackageId::name() instead of the target manifest's ecosystem-native name, so a cross-ecosystem rewrite onto a dual-identity (napi-style) package targets the wrong manifest key and fails with Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound), aborting apply_version_plan for that package.\",\n  \"stakeholder\": \"Callisto maintainers and any user with a dual-identity package (a Cargo crate and an npm package co-located or otherwise identity-linked, e.g. a napi-rs native module) that has a dependent whose spec needs rewriting across ecosystems during a cascade\",\n  \"why\": \"Confirmed live via direct code trace: crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs's solve_cascade (around line 271) constructs RewriteKey { name: edge.to.name().to_string(), .. } -- edge.to's own PackageId name, not the name registered in the TARGET manifest's ecosystem. crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs:493 already implements the correct lookup, IdentityIndex::native_name(&self, id: &PackageId, eco: Ecosystem) -> Option<&str>, but solve_cascade has no access to an IdentityIndex today -- CascadeInput (which already carries a tags: &TagIndex field from a prior track) has no identity field, and IdentityIndex (defined in callisto-graph, a Layer 2 crate per this repo's CLAUDE.md layer-isolation invariant) cannot be exposed through the generic DependencyResolver trait (defined in callisto-model, Layer 1) without violating that invariant. The wrong key flows into callisto-manifests's update_dependency_spec (crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs, confirmed at lines 300/308/341/349/697), which returns Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound) when the key doesn't match a real manifest entry -- a hard failure that propagates via ? through apply_version_plan, aborting the apply for that package on an ordinary, real Cargo+npm co-located package with a cross-ecosystem dependent.\",\n  \"done_when\": [\n    \"Given a dual-identity package D (registered in IdentityIndex.native for both Cargo and Npm ecosystems under potentially different native names, e.g. Cargo name 'my-native-lib' and npm name '@scope/my-native-lib') and a dependent package whose manifest (in a DIFFERENT ecosystem than one of D's registrations) has an out-of-range dependency spec on D that solve_cascade decides to rewrite, the resulting RewriteKey.name equals D's native name AS REGISTERED for the dependent manifest's own ecosystem (looked up via IdentityIndex::native_name(&D's PackageId, dependent_manifest_ecosystem)), not D's PackageId::name().\",\n    \"This holds through the real, live call path: crate::cascade::run_cascade / solve_cascade, not just an isolated call to IdentityIndex::native_name directly.\",\n    \"Given a target package for which IdentityIndex::native_name(id, eco) returns None for the dependent manifest's ecosystem (no cross-ecosystem identity was ever registered for that pairing -- the common, non-dual-identity case), the rewrite key falls back to PackageId::name() exactly as today -- this must be a pure, zero-regression fallback for every existing non-dual-identity workspace.\",\n    \"CascadeInput gains an `identity: &IdentityIndex` field. Both real construction sites are updated to supply it: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs and crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs.\",\n    \"Workspace (crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs) gains an `identity: IdentityIndex` field, populated at Workspace::load time from the already-computed graph.identity() (IdentityIndex already derives Clone) -- Workspace::load is not generic over D (it always concretely produces a ManifestWalkResolver-backed Workspace), so graph.identity() is callable there today without any trait-bound change.\",\n    \"Given an ordinary, real dependency-spec rewrite scenario with no dual-identity package involved anywhere in the workspace (the common case, exercised by this repo's existing cascade/rewrite test suite), the rewrite key, the resulting manifest write, and every existing test's assertions are byte-for-byte unchanged from before this fix -- a genuine, verified regression-proof, not an assumption.\",\n    \"The specific failing scenario named in the bug report -- a real Cargo+npm co-located dual-identity package with a cross-ecosystem dependent whose spec needs rewriting -- is proven, end-to-end through apply_version_plan (not just solve_cascade in isolation), to succeed (no Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound)) and to write the CORRECT manifest key after this fix, where it previously failed.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"Track 1 (fixed-group cascade correctness, already shipped) and any change to the Fixed-group convergence block or GroupTable::resolve's conflict detection -- unrelated code paths in the same file.\",\n    \"Track 2 (platform-manifest writes, already shipped) and any change to plan_version's platform_writes/optional_dep_updates producer logic -- unrelated.\",\n    \"cascade_action's peer-escalation severity fix -- a separate, narrower Track 9 sub-bug, already fixed and committed independently as a lighter-loop change in this same session; this spec covers ONLY the rewrite-key bug.\",\n    \"Redesigning IdentityIndex's own internal structure, native_name's signature, or the Layer 1/Layer 2 boundary itself -- this track threads existing, correct, already-implemented identity data through to where it's needed; it does not change how identity resolution works.\",\n    \"Any change to update_dependency_spec or other callisto-manifests write logic -- that crate already correctly errors on an unmatched key; this track fixes what key gets constructed, not how a key is consumed.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n# Background context for grounding (verify against live code yourself, do not trust this paraphrase)\n\nThis is a sub-bug of \"Track 9\" from a larger, already-approved 12-track remediation plan; its sibling bug (cascade_action's peer-escalation severity) was already fixed and committed this session as a narrow, single-function lighter-loop change (not part of this spec). This rewrite-key bug was investigated and found to require CascadeInput-threading work comparable in scope to a prior track (Track 1, SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS.json) that added a `tags: &TagIndex` field to CascadeInput and touched ~15 call sites -- this bug's fix is expected to touch roughly 16 call sites too (2 real construction sites for CascadeInput in commands/version.rs and commands/snapshot.rs, plus ~14 test-only construction sites across cascade.rs's own test module and crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs). Read Track 1's spec and its api_surface section for the established pattern/precedent this spec should follow for threading a new field through CascadeInput and its construction sites -- reuse that exact approach (e.g. how Track 1 handled the same class of problem for `tags`).\n\nThis repo's established process (`.claude/plans/ACTIVE.md`): full canon→vector→lambda pipeline for architecturally significant changes like this one. `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"` hard workspace invariant. `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` mandatory CI. Verify every code-location/line-number/field-shape claim above against the live code before trusting it -- Track 1's and Track 2's specs each needed multiple exit-gate rounds specifically because early drafts contained small inaccuracies about the actual code; expect the same rigor to be needed here.\n\nProduce a spec@1 with purpose, scope, non_goals (at least the five out_of_scope items above, stated as non_goals), acceptance_criteria (testable propositions, error cases marked is_error_case: true — note the regression-proof criterion and the fallback criterion are both important and easy to under-specify), and an api_surface section documenting the CascadeInput.identity field, the Workspace.identity field, and the exact rewrite-key construction code change (with the correct fallback expression using .unwrap_or_else())."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":969,"cache_read_input_tokens":864961,"output_tokens":3180,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":969,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3180,"cache_read_input_tokens":864961,"cache_creation_input_tokens":969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":969},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9xkfvMSLFBnSFwaTuaC","type":"assistant","uuid":"7c121a8f-598a-4b66-b3e8-9c7de7f2158b","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:17:25.311Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"7c121a8f-598a-4b66-b3e8-9c7de7f2158b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d1296045-3415-4a80-87fb-118208e02a8f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FYMEAco6JrpxzW5Yr2bLNo","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a9ea16adccde28549 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a9ea16adccde28549', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a9ea16adccde28549.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"dd96c5ac-fafa-430e-b10a-2d47cc112fb0","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:17:31.749Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a9ea16adccde28549","description":"Draft Track 9 spec (cascade correctness)","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt":"Draft a spec@1 from the following requirement@1 for the callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Produce the actual spec@1 JSON object as your final output — do not describe a plan to draft it, do the drafting work yourself in this invocation.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"REQ-TRACK9-CASCADE-REWRITE-KEY-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"statement\": \"Fix a confirmed-live bug: crate::cascade::solve_cascade builds dependency-spec rewrite keys from PackageId::name() instead of the target manifest's ecosystem-native name, so a cross-ecosystem rewrite onto a dual-identity (napi-style) package targets the wrong manifest key and fails with Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound), aborting apply_version_plan for that package.\",\n  \"stakeholder\": \"Callisto maintainers and any user with a dual-identity package (a Cargo crate and an npm package co-located or otherwise identity-linked, e.g. a napi-rs native module) that has a dependent whose spec needs rewriting across ecosystems during a cascade\",\n  \"why\": \"Confirmed live via direct code trace: crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs's solve_cascade (around line 271) constructs RewriteKey { name: edge.to.name().to_string(), .. } -- edge.to's own PackageId name, not the name registered in the TARGET manifest's ecosystem. crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs:493 already implements the correct lookup, IdentityIndex::native_name(&self, id: &PackageId, eco: Ecosystem) -> Option<&str>, but solve_cascade has no access to an IdentityIndex today -- CascadeInput (which already carries a tags: &TagIndex field from a prior track) has no identity field, and IdentityIndex (defined in callisto-graph, a Layer 2 crate per this repo's CLAUDE.md layer-isolation invariant) cannot be exposed through the generic DependencyResolver trait (defined in callisto-model, Layer 1) without violating that invariant. The wrong key flows into callisto-manifests's update_dependency_spec (crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs, confirmed at lines 300/308/341/349/697), which returns Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound) when the key doesn't match a real manifest entry -- a hard failure that propagates via ? through apply_version_plan, aborting the apply for that package on an ordinary, real Cargo+npm co-located package with a cross-ecosystem dependent.\",\n  \"done_when\": [\n    \"Given a dual-identity package D (registered in IdentityIndex.native for both Cargo and Npm ecosystems under potentially different native names, e.g. Cargo name 'my-native-lib' and npm name '@scope/my-native-lib') and a dependent package whose manifest (in a DIFFERENT ecosystem than one of D's registrations) has an out-of-range dependency spec on D that solve_cascade decides to rewrite, the resulting RewriteKey.name equals D's native name AS REGISTERED for the dependent manifest's own ecosystem (looked up via IdentityIndex::native_name(&D's PackageId, dependent_manifest_ecosystem)), not D's PackageId::name().\",\n    \"This holds through the real, live call path: crate::cascade::run_cascade / solve_cascade, not just an isolated call to IdentityIndex::native_name directly.\",\n    \"Given a target package for which IdentityIndex::native_name(id, eco) returns None for the dependent manifest's ecosystem (no cross-ecosystem identity was ever registered for that pairing -- the common, non-dual-identity case), the rewrite key falls back to PackageId::name() exactly as today -- this must be a pure, zero-regression fallback for every existing non-dual-identity workspace.\",\n    \"CascadeInput gains an `identity: &IdentityIndex` field. Both real construction sites are updated to supply it: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs and crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs.\",\n    \"Workspace (crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs) gains an `identity: IdentityIndex` field, populated at Workspace::load time from the already-computed graph.identity() (IdentityIndex already derives Clone) -- Workspace::load is not generic over D (it always concretely produces a ManifestWalkResolver-backed Workspace), so graph.identity() is callable there today without any trait-bound change.\",\n    \"Given an ordinary, real dependency-spec rewrite scenario with no dual-identity package involved anywhere in the workspace (the common case, exercised by this repo's existing cascade/rewrite test suite), the rewrite key, the resulting manifest write, and every existing test's assertions are byte-for-byte unchanged from before this fix -- a genuine, verified regression-proof, not an assumption.\",\n    \"The specific failing scenario named in the bug report -- a real Cargo+npm co-located dual-identity package with a cross-ecosystem dependent whose spec needs rewriting -- is proven, end-to-end through apply_version_plan (not just solve_cascade in isolation), to succeed (no Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound)) and to write the CORRECT manifest key after this fix, where it previously failed.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"Track 1 (fixed-group cascade correctness, already shipped) and any change to the Fixed-group convergence block or GroupTable::resolve's conflict detection -- unrelated code paths in the same file.\",\n    \"Track 2 (platform-manifest writes, already shipped) and any change to plan_version's platform_writes/optional_dep_updates producer logic -- unrelated.\",\n    \"cascade_action's peer-escalation severity fix -- a separate, narrower Track 9 sub-bug, already fixed and committed independently as a lighter-loop change in this same session; this spec covers ONLY the rewrite-key bug.\",\n    \"Redesigning IdentityIndex's own internal structure, native_name's signature, or the Layer 1/Layer 2 boundary itself -- this track threads existing, correct, already-implemented identity data through to where it's needed; it does not change how identity resolution works.\",\n    \"Any change to update_dependency_spec or other callisto-manifests write logic -- that crate already correctly errors on an unmatched key; this track fixes what key gets constructed, not how a key is consumed.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n# Background context for grounding (verify against live code yourself, do not trust this paraphrase)\n\nThis is a sub-bug of \"Track 9\" from a larger, already-approved 12-track remediation plan; its sibling bug (cascade_action's peer-escalation severity) was already fixed and committed this session as a narrow, single-function lighter-loop change (not part of this spec). This rewrite-key bug was investigated and found to require CascadeInput-threading work comparable in scope to a prior track (Track 1, SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS.json) that added a `tags: &TagIndex` field to CascadeInput and touched ~15 call sites -- this bug's fix is expected to touch roughly 16 call sites too (2 real construction sites for CascadeInput in commands/version.rs and commands/snapshot.rs, plus ~14 test-only construction sites across cascade.rs's own test module and crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs). Read Track 1's spec and its api_surface section for the established pattern/precedent this spec should follow for threading a new field through CascadeInput and its construction sites -- reuse that exact approach (e.g. how Track 1 handled the same class of problem for `tags`).\n\nThis repo's established process (`.claude/plans/ACTIVE.md`): full canon→vector→lambda pipeline for architecturally significant changes like this one. `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"` hard workspace invariant. `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` mandatory CI. Verify every code-location/line-number/field-shape claim above against the live code before trusting it -- Track 1's and Track 2's specs each needed multiple exit-gate rounds specifically because early drafts contained small inaccuracies about the actual code; expect the same rigor to be needed here.\n\nProduce a spec@1 with purpose, scope, non_goals (at least the five out_of_scope items above, stated as non_goals), acceptance_criteria (testable propositions, error cases marked is_error_case: true — note the regression-proof criterion and the fallback criterion are both important and easy to under-specify), and an api_surface section documenting the CascadeInput.identity field, the Workspace.identity field, and the exact rewrite-key construction code change (with the correct fallback expression using .unwrap_or_else()).","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a9ea16adccde28549.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7c121a8f-598a-4b66-b3e8-9c7de7f2158b","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
