{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:20:44.553Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a8be2735fd51ae217</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_019C1Jr4r13G8Zn36vPwxeZG</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a8be2735fd51ae217.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review peer-escalation severity fix\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Review: `crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs` peer-escalation source-severity fix\n\nRead `.agents/subagents/bug-hunter.md`, `.agents/skills/bug-hunter/SKILL.md`, and `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto-findings/FINDINGS.md` in full first, per instructions. This finding is not previously logged in the ledger. This is a read-only review — no files were modified; only `git diff`, `cargo test`, `cargo clippy`, and `cargo fmt --check` were run.\n\n### Scope adherence — clean\n`git diff crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs` shows exactly one production-code change: the parameter rename `_source` → `source`, and one added guard clause `&amp;&amp; matches!(source, Severity::Minor | Severity::Major)` on the pre-existing peer-escalation match arm (`crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:53`). The rest of the diff is the new test. Nothing else in the function, file, or workspace was touched — `git status`/`git diff --stat` at review time confirms only `cascade.rs` is dirty (the other files from the session-start snapshot — `snapshot.rs`, `version.rs`, `apply.rs`, `graph_tests.rs` — had already been committed before this review began). No incidental refactors, no unrelated formatting churn beyond what rustfmt required for the now-multi-line guard (`cargo fmt -p callisto-graph -- --check` is clean).\n\n### Correctness against spec — confirmed correct\nRead `docs/01-spec.md:7186-7209` directly. Row 5's condition is literally \"peer, genuinely out of range, non-patch source → MAJOR,\" row 4 is \"peer, out of range, patch source (or escalation opted out).\" `Severity` (`crates/callisto-model/src/severity.rs:14-19`) has exactly 4 variants: `None, Patch, Minor, Major`. The new guard `matches!(source, Severity::Minor | Severity::Major)` correctly implements row 5 for both non-patch severities that matter, and correctly falls through to row 4 for `Patch`. `Severity::None` is the one case not literally spelled \"patch\" in the spec's row-4 comment — see the \"Also check\" section below; it's provably unreachable, and the fallback is correct even if it weren't.\n\n### Sibling gaps — none found\n- `cascade_action` has exactly one production call site in the whole workspace: `crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:237` inside `solve_cascade`/`run_cascade` (confirmed via `grep -rn \"cascade_action\" crates/`). No other crate or command reimplements or duplicates the peer-escalation decision logic — everywhere else (`commands/version.rs:176`, `commands/pr_body.rs:106,197`, `callisto-changelog/src/render.rs:63`) only *consumes* the resulting `BumpReason::PeerEscalation` value, they don't re-derive severity.\n- Traced whether any existing test or code path depended on the old always-Major behavior: only one integration test exercises `DepKind::Peer` end-to-end (`crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs:161` `test_peer_dependency_escalation`), and it seeds `Severity::Major`, so it's unaffected by the fix — confirmed passing (`cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib cascade` and the `cascade_tests.rs` binary both green, 10/10 and prior integration tests all `ok`).\n- Traced `raise()` (`cascade.rs:482-541`): when the guard now correctly declines to escalate a patch-source peer edge, `decision.escalated` is `false`, so `raise` emits `BumpReason::Cascade` instead of `BumpReason::PeerEscalation` — exactly the right downstream behavior for changelog/PR-body rendering, no special-casing needed in those consumers.\n\n### Non-negotiable violations — none\n`unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`: confirmed no `unsafe` introduced (`grep -n \"unsafe\" crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs` → no matches). `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --lib --tests -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n### Test quality — good, one minor gap\n`cascade_action_peer_escalation_only_fires_for_non_patch_source` (`cascade.rs:616-663`) calls `cascade_action` directly and pins `severity`, `escalated`, and `governed_by` for all three cases — this is a genuine assertion, not a shape-only check: the Patch case asserts `severity == Severity::Patch` (row 4's actual computed value, `cfg.bump_severity.as_severity()` with `CascadeBumpSeverity::Patch` — verified this mapping at `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs:106-118`), so if the new guard were absent or wrong, this assertion would see `Severity::Major` instead and fail. Minor/Major cases are pinned too. It covers 3 of the 4 `Severity` variants directly at the unit level — `Severity::None` is not exercised by this test.\n\n**Gap on `Severity::None`, and answer to the \"Also check\" question**: traced every insertion path into `out.severities`/`input.seed` (the only source of `src_sev` passed to `cascade_action` at `cascade.rs:225,237`):\n- `aggregate.rs:226` (inference) and `:298` (explicit changeset) both gate insertion behind `if outcome.severity &gt; cur_sev` / `if entry.severity &gt; cur_sev` where `cur_sev` defaults to `Severity::None` — so any severity that actually gets inserted is provably `&gt; None`.\n- `raise()` (`cascade.rs:494-499`) and its fixed-sibling loop (`:524-538`) gate on `if sev &gt; cur_sev` the same way.\n- The linked-group (`:339-345`) and fixed-group (`:410-416`) convergence blocks both gate on `max_sev &gt; Severity::None` before inserting.\n\nEvery single write site to the severities map enforces \"never insert `Severity::None`,\" so `cascade_action(Peer, DoesNotCover, Severity::None, cfg)` cannot occur through `run_cascade`/`solve_cascade` today — it's unreachable, not just untested. If that invariant were ever broken by a future call site, the current match-arm order already handles it correctly: `Severity::None` doesn't match `Severity::Minor | Severity::Major`, so it falls through to row 4 exactly like `Patch`, which is the safe/conservative outcome either way.\n\n**Recommendation (not a defect, just a completeness note)**: since `cascade_action` is a `pub fn` tested directly (not just through the one production call site), a fourth assertion for `Severity::None` in the same test would make the unit test exhaustive over the enum rather than relying on an untested cross-function invariant to justify the omission — cheap to add, would fully close the loop for anyone reading the test in isolation without redoing this trace.\n\n**Files referenced** (all read-only): `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/severity.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/dependency.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md` (lines 1848-1851, 4997-5003, 7186-7256), `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/00-design.md` (line 1277, invariant 9's literal text; lines 1925-1929).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>75414</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>47</tool_uses><duration_ms>514833</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
