{"parentUuid":"c1f864a3-79f1-46dd-b6e4-b928775d9a20","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9ycbwNnhEFcsAtTwf5A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012ecZ4DxE3ocF9NF3hCxAdD","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Verify Track 9 spec grounding","subagent_type":"canon:verifier","prompt":"Verify the draft spec@1 at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track9-draft.json (id SPEC-TRACK9-CASCADE-REWRITE-KEY-CORRECTNESS, for the callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto) against its source requirement@1 below. For each of the spec's 7 acceptance criteria, classify as supported, unsupported, or overfitted.\n\nSource requirement@1:\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"REQ-TRACK9-CASCADE-REWRITE-KEY-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"statement\": \"Fix a confirmed-live bug: crate::cascade::solve_cascade builds dependency-spec rewrite keys from PackageId::name() instead of the target manifest's ecosystem-native name, so a cross-ecosystem rewrite onto a dual-identity (napi-style) package targets the wrong manifest key and fails with Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound), aborting apply_version_plan for that package.\",\n  \"why\": \"Confirmed live via direct code trace: cascade.rs's solve_cascade constructs RewriteKey { name: edge.to.name().to_string(), .. } -- edge.to's own PackageId name, not the name registered in the TARGET manifest's ecosystem. IdentityIndex::native_name already implements the correct lookup, but solve_cascade has no access to an IdentityIndex today. The wrong key flows into callisto-manifests's update_dependency_spec, which returns Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound) when the key doesn't match a real manifest entry.\",\n  \"done_when\": [\n    \"Given a dual-identity package D and a dependent package whose manifest is in a DIFFERENT ecosystem than one of D's registrations, declaring an out-of-range dependency spec on D that solve_cascade decides to rewrite, the resulting RewriteKey.name equals D's native name AS REGISTERED for the dependent manifest's own ecosystem (looked up via IdentityIndex::native_name), not D's PackageId::name().\",\n    \"This holds through the real, live call path: crate::cascade::run_cascade / solve_cascade, not just an isolated call to IdentityIndex::native_name directly.\",\n    \"Given a target package for which IdentityIndex::native_name(id, eco) returns None for the dependent manifest's ecosystem (the common, non-dual-identity case), the rewrite key falls back to PackageId::name() exactly as today -- this must be a pure, zero-regression fallback for every existing non-dual-identity workspace.\",\n    \"CascadeInput gains an `identity: &IdentityIndex` field. Both real construction sites are updated to supply it: commands/version.rs and commands/snapshot.rs.\",\n    \"Workspace gains an `identity: IdentityIndex` field, populated at Workspace::load time from the already-computed graph.identity() -- Workspace::load is not generic over D, so graph.identity() is callable there today without any trait-bound change.\",\n    \"Given an ordinary, real dependency-spec rewrite scenario with no dual-identity package involved anywhere in the workspace (the common case, exercised by this repo's existing cascade/rewrite test suite), the rewrite key, the resulting manifest write, and every existing test's assertions are byte-for-byte unchanged from before this fix -- a genuine, verified regression-proof, not an assumption.\",\n    \"The specific failing scenario named in the bug report -- a real Cargo+npm co-located dual-identity package with a cross-ecosystem dependent whose spec needs rewriting -- is proven, end-to-end through apply_version_plan (not just solve_cascade in isolation), to succeed (no Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound)) and to write the CORRECT manifest key after this fix, where it previously failed.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"Track 1 and Track 2 (already shipped) -- unrelated code paths.\",\n    \"cascade_action's peer-escalation severity fix -- a separate sub-bug, already fixed and committed independently.\",\n    \"Redesigning IdentityIndex's own internal structure, native_name's signature, or the Layer 1/Layer 2 boundary itself.\",\n    \"Any change to update_dependency_spec or other callisto-manifests write logic.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nNote the spec's own `reasoning` field documents a deliberate, evidence-based deviation from the requirement's done_when item about a \"new Workspace.identity field\": the drafter found ManifestWalkResolver already exposes a public `identity() -> &IdentityIndex` accessor and Workspace::load already calls it, so the spec uses `ws.graph.identity()` directly at both CascadeInput construction sites instead of adding a duplicate field to Workspace. Assess whether this deviation is a legitimate, well-evidenced correction (verify it yourself against crates/callisto-graph/src/resolver.rs and crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs) or whether it under-delivers on what the requirement actually needs -- and whether the spec's acceptance criteria (particularly AC-005) still correctly test the OBSERVABLE outcome the requirement cares about despite the internal-mechanism change.\n\nRead the full spec@1 JSON from disk for complete acceptance criteria text. Output a structured evidence report with supported, unsupported, and overfitted arrays plus a reasoning scratchpad."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1035,"cache_read_input_tokens":894754,"output_tokens":2043,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1035,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2043,"cache_read_input_tokens":894754,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1035},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9ycQHeYbRiMmBfJgoiM","type":"assistant","uuid":"0f60c42d-97f8-483f-ad9e-822c2a6a1801","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:28:26.260Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
