dentity: &IdentityIndex` field. Both real construction sites are updated to supply it: commands/version.rs and commands/snapshot.rs.\",\n    \"Workspace gains an `identity: IdentityIndex` field, populated at Workspace::load time from the already-computed graph.identity() -- Workspace::load is not generic over D, so graph.identity() is callable there today without any trait-bound change.\",\n    \"Given an ordinary, real dependency-spec rewrite scenario with no dual-identity package involved anywhere in the workspace (the common case, exercised by this repo's existing cascade/rewrite test suite), the rewrite key, the resulting manifest write, and every existing test's assertions are byte-for-byte unchanged from before this fix -- a genuine, verified regression-proof, not an assumption.\",\n    \"The specific failing scenario named in the bug report -- a real Cargo+npm co-located dual-identity package with a cross-ecosystem dependent whose spec needs rewriting -- is proven, end-to-end through apply_version_plan (not just solve_cascade in isolation), to succeed (no Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound)) and to write the CORRECT manifest key after this fix, where it previously failed.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"Track 1 and Track 2 (already shipped) -- unrelated code paths.\",\n    \"cascade_action's peer-escalation severity fix -- a separate sub-bug, already fixed and committed independently.\",\n    \"Redesigning IdentityIndex's own internal structure, native_name's signature, or the Layer 1/Layer 2 boundary itself.\",\n    \"Any change to update_dependency_spec or other callisto-manifests write logic.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nNote the spec's own `reasoning` field documents a deliberate, evidence-based deviation from the requirement's done_when item about a \"new Workspace.identity field\": the drafter found ManifestWalkResolver already exposes a public `identity() -> &IdentityIndex` accessor and Workspace::load already calls it, so the spec uses `ws.graph.identit