{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:33:34.096Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4272885cd24cf6f4</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a4272885cd24cf6f4.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit Track 9 spec quality\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>```json\n{\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-005\",\n      \"type\": \"untestable\",\n      \"description\": \"The api_surface's 'Workspace.identity (via ManifestWalkResolver::identity, no new struct field required)' entry, and AC-005's claim that version.rs:73 and snapshot.rs:54 can supply `identity: ws.graph.identity()`, do not compile. plan_version&lt;R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver, I: SeverityInference&gt; (version.rs:24) and plan_snapshot&lt;R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver&gt; (snapshot.rs:9) are both generic over D. ManifestWalkResolver::identity() (resolver.rs:41) is an inherent method on the concrete struct; DependencyResolver (callisto-model/src/discovery.rs:36-43) has no identity() method and per the spec's own non_goals must never gain one (layer isolation). Rust type-checks a generic function body against its declared trait bounds only -- it does not know, inside the body, that every real caller happens to pass ManifestWalkResolver. The spec's justification ('both call sites are monomorphized through Workspace::load's concrete ManifestWalkResolver in every real call path') conflates monomorphization at a generic function's call sites with method resolution inside that function's own body -- these are different compiler phases, and the latter does not benefit from the former. The reasoning that correctly justifies `graph.identity()` inside Workspace::load (verified live: that impl block is `impl&lt;'a, R: CommandRunner&gt; Workspace&lt;'a, R, ManifestWalkResolver&gt;`, not generic over D) was silently and incorrectly extended to plan_version/plan_snapshot, which ARE generic over D. As written, AC-005's compile-success claim is false for the specified fix.\",\n      \"suggested_fix\": \"Add `pub identity: IdentityIndex` as an actual new field on `Workspace&lt;'a, R, D&gt;` (crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs, alongside `root`, `config`, `graph`; IdentityIndex derives Clone so an owned field avoids adding a new lifetime bound to Workspace). Populate it only inside the existing `impl&lt;'a, R: CommandRunner&gt; Workspace&lt;'a, R, ManifestWalkResolver&gt;` block -- the same place Workspace::load already computes `graph.identity()` today for GroupTable::resolve and promoted_siblings, where D is concretely ManifestWalkResolver and the call is legal. Then version.rs:73 and snapshot.rs:54 supply `identity: &amp;ws.identity` -- a plain struct-field read with no bound on D, so both generic plan_version&lt;R,D,I&gt; and plan_snapshot&lt;R,D&gt; compile unconditionally regardless of what D is instantiated with. Revise api_surface entry 'Workspace.identity' and the spec's reasoning field to state this: the field-based design the original requirement proposed is not merely a matter of taste here, it is required for plan_version/plan_snapshot to compile at all, because they are generic over D and identity() is not part of the DependencyResolver trait bound.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-007\",\n      \"type\": \"untestable\",\n      \"description\": \"AC-007 asserts 'a PackageId::Bare target never causes a panic, unwrap failure, or a different code path than the None-registration case.' Verified against live code: native_name (identity.rs:493-499) is a plain BTreeMap iteration with equality comparison -- no unwrap/expect/index/panic branch exists for any PackageId variant. PackageId::name() (callisto-model/src/identity.rs:102-107) and ecosystem() (:94-99) are total matches over Bare/Prefixed with no panic path either. Panic-freedom therefore holds unconditionally for ANY correct-or-incorrect implementation of this fix -- an implementer cannot make this criterion fail while writing the specified one-line replacement, so it has zero discriminating power as a regression check. Separately, 'a different code path than the None-registration case' requires knowing internal control flow to evaluate ('is this the same code path as that other case?') rather than observable input/output behavior -- this fails the semantic-model auditability test (two independent testers with no implementation knowledge cannot evaluate 'same code path' from outside).\",\n      \"suggested_fix\": \"Replace AC-007 with a concrete, externally-observable input/output criterion that keeps the Bare case as a named regression fixture (this is a legitimate completeness addition -- native_name's real signature takes any PackageId including Bare, so the case is worth pinning -- but it should assert an outcome, not an absence of panic that is already structurally guaranteed): 'Given a rewrite target `PackageId::Bare(\\\"foo\\\".to_string())` with no IdentityIndex.native registration under the dependent's ecosystem, `input.identity.native_name(&amp;edge.to, eco)` returns None and the constructed RewriteKey.name equals \\\"foo\\\" (edge.to.name()) -- exercised through the same crate::cascade::run_cascade call path as AC-002, confirming the Bare variant is handled identically to the Prefixed None-registration case in AC-003.'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-001\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguous\",\n      \"description\": \"The api_surface entry for CascadeInput.identity says test fixtures needing native_name to resolve should use 'a populated IdentityIndex built via its existing test-construction helpers' -- no such named helper (e.g. IdentityIndex::with_native(...)) exists anywhere in the codebase. Verified by grepping every IdentityIndex construction site in the workspace (identity.rs:236,253,271,295,324; walk.rs:109; ecosystem_bugs_test.rs:272,310): every one constructs via `IdentityIndex::default()` followed by direct insertion into the (confirmed pub, not pub(crate)) `native: BTreeMap&lt;(Ecosystem, String), PackageId&gt;` field. Given this session's established pattern of underspecified fixture-construction mechanisms causing exit-gate failures on Track 1 and Track 2, two implementers reading 'existing test-construction helpers' could reasonably go looking for a nonexistent builder function rather than using the direct-field-insert pattern that is actually the only one in use.\",\n      \"suggested_fix\": \"In the CascadeInput.identity api_surface entry, replace 'a populated IdentityIndex built via its existing test-construction helpers for tests that need native_name to resolve' with: 'a populated IdentityIndex constructed via direct insertion into its public `native` field (crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs:342), the same mechanism used throughout the codebase's existing tests (e.g. identity.rs:236-324, ecosystem_bugs_test.rs:272,310) -- there is no dedicated builder function. For AC-001: `let mut idx = IdentityIndex::default(); idx.native.insert((Ecosystem::Cargo, \\\"my-native-lib\\\".to_string()), d_id.clone()); idx.native.insert((Ecosystem::Npm, \\\"@scope/my-native-lib\\\".to_string()), d_id.clone());`.'\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overall\": \"fail\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Confirmed clean: no scope overlap with SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS -- Track 1's `tags` field (already shipped) and Track 9's `identity` field are additive, sequential, non-conflicting threads onto CascadeInput; live-code CascadeInput has exactly 9 fields including tags (cascade.rs:141-151), and the 8+6=14 test-literal-site count in cascade.rs and cascade_tests.rs was confirmed by direct grep, matching the spec's own count exactly. Track 1's Fixed-group convergence block and Track 9's RewriteKey-construction site are genuinely different code regions in the same file with no interaction. `.map(str::to_string)` in the api_surface fix line was compiled directly and is correct for Option&lt;&amp;str&gt; -&gt; Option&lt;String&gt;. IdentityIndex.native was found to be a public field (not pub(crate) as the task briefing assumed), which resolves the mechanism-availability question favorably but the spec still gestures vaguely at nonexistent 'helpers' rather than naming the direct-insertion pattern -- flagged as AC-001 ambiguity. AC-007's no-panic guarantee is a legitimate instinct (matching the missing-error-case dimension, since native_name's real signature does take Bare) but as phrased is structurally untestable/non-discriminating and partly relies on unobservable 'code path' language -- recommend narrowing to a concrete outcome rather than trimming outright. The disqualifying finding is AC-005/api_surface's ws.graph.identity() claim: plan_version and plan_snapshot are generic over D: DependencyResolver, and identity() is an inherent ManifestWalkResolver method absent from the DependencyResolver trait bound, so the specified fix does not compile at either real construction site. This directly contradicts the canon-verifier's confirmation that the accessor-based deviation is 'correct against live code' -- that confirmation appears to have validated the reasoning only where it actually holds (Workspace::load's non-generic impl block) and then let it be silently misapplied to two different, generic functions. Given the instruction not to relitigate the general architectural preference (accessor vs. new field), I want to be precise about what's being reported: this is not a stylistic objection to the deviation, it is a verified compile failure in the deviation's specific application at the two real call sites the spec directs an implementer to edit, discovered by reading the actual generic signatures of plan_version and plan_snapshot. It must be fixed before this spec can pass to planning.\"\n}\n```\n\nKey file paths referenced during this audit (all absolute):\n- `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track9-draft.json` (spec under audit)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs` (IdentityIndex, native_name)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/identity.rs` (PackageId)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/resolver.rs` (ManifestWalkResolver::identity)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/discovery.rs` (DependencyResolver trait)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs`, `snapshot.rs` (plan_version/plan_snapshot generic signatures and CascadeInput construction sites)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs` (CascadeInput struct, rewrite-key site)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS.json` (confirmed no overlap)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>76676</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>21</tool_uses><duration_ms>234930</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
