{"parentUuid":"d40c9b03-b069-45c9-bdb9-7746a89640d3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_019uW2fG8pBsxteiRgU9mFQt","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"callisto\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":45},"type":"attachment","uuid":"233a0feb-6621-4333-8071-8c0b0f3c82d7","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:41:06.862Z","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"233a0feb-6621-4333-8071-8c0b0f3c82d7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track9-draft.json","snippet":"1\t{\n2\t  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK9-CASCADE-REWRITE-KEY-CORRECTNESS\",\n3\t  \"purpose\": \"Fix solve_cascade's dependency-spec rewrite-key construction (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, RewriteKey.name at the site that currently reads `name: edge.to.name().to_string()`, inside the `if d.rewrite { ... }` block around line 269) so that, when the rewrite target is a dual-identity package registered in IdentityIndex under different native names per ecosystem (e.g. a Cargo crate that is also a napi-rs npm package), the key uses the name actually present in the dependent manifest being rewritten -- looked up via IdentityIndex::native_name(&edge.to, eco) where `eco` is the dependent's own already-computed ecosystem -- instead of PackageId::name(), which is the name registered for the dependency's OWN native ecosystem and can differ from what the cross-ecosystem dependent manifest actually wrote. The wrong key is currently passed to callisto-manifests's update_dependency_spec, which returns Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound) when the key does not match a real manifest entry, aborting apply_version_plan for the affected package. This spec threads an `&IdentityIndex` through CascadeInput and Workspace so solve_cascade has the data it needs, following the exact precedent set by Track 1's `tags: &TagIndex` threading (SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS): a new required field on CascadeInput, supplied at both real construction sites, sourced from a new field on Workspace populated once at Workspace::load time from the resolver's already-computed IdentityIndex.\",\n4\t  \"scope\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs (CascadeInput struct, the single RewriteKey-construction site inside solve_cascade's `if d.rewrite` block), crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs (Workspace struct and Workspace::load), crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (plan_version's CascadeInput construction, line 73), crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs (plan_snapshot's CascadeInput construction, line 54), and every test-only CascadeInput struct-literal construction site in crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs's own `#[cfg(test)]` module and crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs (8 + 6 = 14 sites confirmed by direct grep count as of this spec). No change to IdentityIndex's internal structure, native_name's signature, callisto-manifests's update_dependency_spec, or cascade_action.\",\n5\t  \"non_goals\": [\n6\t    \"Track 1 (fixed-group cascade correctness, already shipped) and any change to the Fixed-group convergence block or GroupTable::resolve's conflict detection -- unrelated code paths in the same file, out of scope for this spec.\",\n7\t    \"Track 2 (platform-manifest writes, already shipped) and any change to plan_version's platform_writes/optional_dep_updates producer logic -- unrelated.\",\n8\t    \"cascade_action's peer-escalation severity fix -- a separate, narrower Track 9 sub-bug already fixed and committed independently in this same session as a lighter-loop change; this spec covers ONLY the rewrite-key bug.\",\n9\t    \"Redesigning IdentityIndex's own internal structure, native_name's signature, or the Layer 1 (callisto-model) / Layer 2 (callisto-graph) boundary itself -- this spec threads existing, already-implemented identity data through to where it is needed; it does not change how identity resolution works or weaken the layer-isolation invariant (IdentityIndex remains a callisto-graph type; it is never exposed through the generic, callisto-model-defined DependencyResolver trait).\",\n10\t    \"Any change to update_dependency_spec or other callisto-manifests write logic -- that crate already correctly errors on an unmatched key; this spec fixes what key gets constructed, not how a key is consumed.\",\n11\t    \"Constructing or exposing an IdentityIndex for any DependencyResolver implementation other than ManifestWalkResolver. Workspace::load is defined only in the `impl<'a, R: CommandRunner> Workspace<'a, R, ManifestWalkResolver>` block (crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs), which is not generic over D, so `graph.identity()` -- a method defined on ManifestWalkResolver itself, not on the DependencyResolver trait -- is callable there without any trait-bound change. A test double implementing DependencyResolver with no identity() method is unaffected by this spec; such tests supply CascadeInput.identity directly as a struct-literal field, per AC-005.\",\n12\t    \"Deduplicating or otherwise changing IdentityIndex.native's insertion/lookup semantics when the same (PackageId, Ecosystem) pair is registered more than once -- native_name's existing first-match iteration order (BTreeMap iteration, deterministic) is used as-is.\"\n13\t  ],\n14\t  \"api_surface\": [\n15\t    {\n16\t      \"name\": \"CascadeInput.identity\",\n17\t      \"signature\": \"pub identity: &'a IdentityIndex\",\n18\t      \"description\": \"New required field added to CascadeInput (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs; currently 9 fields: graph, groups, cfg, seed, reasons, named_by, base, pre, tags -- none named identity). IdentityIndex is defined in crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs and already derives Clone. Required so the RewriteKey-construction site inside solve_cascade's `if d.rewrite { ... }` block can call `input.identity.native_name(&edge.to, eco)`. Both real construction sites must supply it: commands/version.rs's plan_version (`identity: &ws.graph.index` is not accessible -- use `identity: ws.graph.identity()` via ManifestWalkResolver's public `identity(&self) -> &IdentityIndex` accessor, since `ws.graph` is a `ManifestWalkResolver` there) and commands/snapshot.rs's plan_snapshot (same accessor, `ws.graph.identity()`). Every test-only CascadeInput struct literal (8 sites in cascade.rs's test module, 6 sites in tests/cascade_tests.rs) must add an `identity: &IdentityIndex` field -- either `&IdentityIndex::default()` for tests with no dual-identity fixture, or a populated `IdentityIndex` built via its existing test-construction helpers for tests that need native_name to resolve.\"\n19\t    },\n20\t    {\n21\t      \"name\": \"Workspace.identity (via ManifestWalkResolver::identity, no new struct field required)\",\n22\t      \"signature\": \"ws.graph.identity() -> &IdentityIndex, called at CascadeInput-construction sites\",\n23\t      \"description\": \"Verified against live code: ManifestWalkResolver already exposes `pub fn identity(&self) -> &IdentityIndex { &self.index }` (crates/callisto-graph/src/resolver.rs). Workspace::load (crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs, the `impl<'a, R: CommandRunner> Workspace<'a, R, ManifestWalkResolver>` block, not generic over D) already computes `graph.identity()` today and uses it inline for `GroupTable::resolve` and `promoted_siblings`. No new field on the Workspace struct itself is required or added by this spec -- plan_version and plan_snapshot each already hold `ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>` with `ws.graph: D`; since both call sites are monomorphized through Workspace::load's concrete ManifestWalkResolver in every real (non-test-double) call path, `ws.graph.identity()` is callable at both sites without a trait-bound change. This corrects the requirement's premise of adding a dedicated `Workspace.identity: IdentityIndex` field: the existing `ManifestWalkResolver::identity()` accessor already provides the same data with no duplication, and duplicating it as a second field would risk drift between `ws.graph`'s live index and a stale copy. The two real construction sites (version.rs:73, snapshot.rs:54) pass `identity: ws.graph.identity()` directly as the CascadeInput.identity field.\"\n24\t    },\n25\t    {\n26\t      \"name\": \"cascade::solve_cascade (RewriteKey.name construction, corrected)\",\n27\t      \"signature\": \"Inside solve_cascade's existing `if d.rewrite { ... }` block (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, `match rewrite_spec(...) { RewriteOutcome::Rewritten(to_spec) => { let key = RewriteKey { ... } ... } }`). solve_cascade's own public signature is unchanged: `pub fn solve_cascade<D: DependencyResolver>(input: CascadeInput<'_, D>) -> Result<CascadeOutcome, GraphError>`.\",\n\n... [43 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b034c129-8c47-4293-8ba5-03aa0b7b34bd","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:41:07.121Z","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
