{"parentUuid":"d2dc5522-86ef-4aca-9eee-ee67abdaf0c3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9zgbHukD3Mx9oKjJqzt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M3C9RwWEKC4waVhR7nGHco","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Exit-gate Track 9 spec","subagent_type":"canon:exit-gate","prompt":"Issue a binding pass/fail verdict on the spec@1 at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track9-draft.json (id SPEC-TRACK9-CASCADE-REWRITE-KEY-CORRECTNESS, callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto). This is retry_count 1 (first exit-gate pass). Read the full spec fresh from disk — do not trust this summary.\n\nHistory: canon-verifier found 6/7 criteria directly grounded in the requirement (AC-007 flagged as a reasonable but not literally-cited defensive addition). canon-auditor then found a CRITICAL defect: the spec's original design (found by a prior drafting pass, not present in the requirement) used `ws.graph.identity()` directly at plan_version/plan_snapshot's CascadeInput construction sites instead of adding a new Workspace.identity field -- but plan_version<R, D, I> and plan_snapshot<R, D> are BOTH generic over D: DependencyResolver, and ManifestWalkResolver::identity() is an inherent method absent from the DependencyResolver trait bound (which cannot reference IdentityIndex, a Layer 2 type, from callisto-model's Layer 1, per this repo's CLAUDE.md layer-isolation invariant) -- so `ws.graph.identity()` genuinely does NOT compile inside either generic function body. This was a real, confirmed compile-error-causing defect, not a stylistic preference. Fixed: reverted to the requirement's original design -- Workspace<'a, R, D> gains an actual owned `identity: IdentityIndex` field, populated once inside Workspace::load's existing non-generic-over-D impl block (where `graph.identity()` genuinely IS callable, confirmed), and both real call sites read it as a plain struct field (`&ws.identity`, no D bound, compiles unconditionally). The audit also found AC-007's original \"no panic\" framing was structurally unfalsifiable (native_name/PackageId::name()/ecosystem() have no panic path for ANY input, so no implementation could fail this check) and partly relied on unobservable \"same code path\" language; fixed by replacing it with a concrete, observable outcome (Bare target -> native_name returns None -> RewriteKey.name falls back to edge.to.name(), exercised through the real run_cascade call path). Also fixed: the CascadeInput.identity api_surface entry vaguely referenced nonexistent \"test-construction helpers\" for populating IdentityIndex in tests; replaced with the concrete, only-actually-used-anywhere pattern (direct insertion into IdentityIndex's public `native` field).\n\nRead the full spec fresh from disk — verify all three fixes actually landed and are internally consistent (check for any remaining stale references to `ws.graph.identity()` being directly callable at plan_version/plan_snapshot -- there should be none; every remaining mention of that phrase should be framed as \"does not compile\" or \"was attempted then corrected\", not as a working approach). Independently re-verify against live code in crates/callisto-graph/src/{lib.rs,cascade.rs,resolver.rs,identity.rs,commands/version.rs,commands/snapshot.rs} and crates/callisto-model/src/discovery.rs -- especially confirm plan_version and plan_snapshot's exact generic signatures, and that Workspace::load's impl block is genuinely non-generic over D so populating the new Workspace.identity field there is legal.\n\nApply your standard adversarial pass/fail standard: every acceptance criterion testable, no vague language, no TBDs, error cases covered with is_error_case: true, scope narrow enough for one planning cycle. Default disposition is fail. Output a verdict@1 with artifact_type \"spec@1\" and retry_count 1."},"caller":{"type":"dire