e.identity field, AC-007's observable-outcome rewrite, CascadeInput.identity's concrete construction pattern) all landed correctly, then found 2 new blockers, both just fixed:\n\n1. `scope` never mentioned 18 hand-constructed Workspace struct literals outside Workspace::load that would ALSO stop compiling once Workspace.identity is added (Workspace derives no Default, uses no `..` rest pattern in these literals). Fixed: scope now enumerates all 18 sites by file and line number across 6 test files (validate_command_tests.rs:112,180; snapshot_tests.rs:70,132,183,255; matrix_tests.rs:63,101; graph_tests.rs:35; tags_tests.rs:62,172,333,494; publish_tests.rs:167,679,742,974,1342), with the correct fill value (`identity: IdentityIndex::default()`) for each.\n2. AC-004's exception clause was exclusive (\"unmodified except for... CascadeInput struct literal\" only) and therefore unsatisfiable/contradicted AC-005, since the crate cannot compile without also editing the 18 Workspace literals. Fixed: AC-004's exception clause now names both required mechanical edits (CascadeInput literals AND the 18 Workspace literals), while the byte-for-byte invariance assertion itself is unchanged.\n\nRead the full spec fresh from disk -- do not trust this summary, verify both fixes landed and are internally consistent, and independently re-confirm the 18 file/line citations are accurate by reading the actual test files yourself (crates/callisto-graph/tests/{validate_command_tests,snapshot_tests,matrix_tests,graph_tests,tags_tests,publish_tests}.rs) -- do not just trust that the line numbers are right, this session has repeatedly found off-by-a-few citation errors in prior specs.\n\nApply your standard adversarial pass/fail standard: every acceptance criterion testable, no vague language, no TBDs, error cases covered with is_error_case: true, scope narrow enough for one planning cycle. Default disposition is fail. Output a verdict@1 with artifact_type \"spec@1\" and retry_count 2.","outputF