{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:56:17.358Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a94742edd4d2b5032</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a94742edd4d2b5032.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Exit-gate Track 9 spec (retry 2)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Verdict: PASS (confidence high, retry_count 2)\n\nWritten to `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/verdict-track9-retry2.json`\n\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"pass\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"artifact_type\": \"spec@1\", \"retry_count\": 2, \"blockers\": []}\n```\n\n### Both retry-1 blockers verified resolved\n\n**Blocker 1 (scope omitted the Workspace literals).** I re-derived the site list myself rather than checking the spec's numbers one at a time. `grep -rn \"Workspace {\" --include=\"*.rs\" crates/` returns exactly 19 hits workspace-wide: the 18 test-file literals, plus `Ok(Workspace {` at `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs:131` (Workspace::load itself, correctly excluded). **All 18 line numbers are exact — no drift.** Per-file counts (2, 4, 2, 1, 4, 5) sum to 18, and the list is exhaustive, not just accurate: I also searched turbofish and line-broken construction forms and found zero additional sites. The compile-break premise holds — `pub struct Workspace&lt;'a, R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver = ManifestWalkResolver&gt;` at lib.rs:53 carries no derive attribute at all, and load's own literal lists all 7 fields with no `..` rest pattern.\n\nOne note for the implementer: `graph_tests.rs` is dirty in the working tree, and line 35 is correct against current working-tree content — the state they'll actually edit.\n\n**Blocker 2 (AC-004's exclusive exception).** Now inclusive, naming both CascadeInput literals and the 18 Workspace literals, with an explicit \"both are required for the crate to compile at all, per AC-005\" back-reference. The contradiction with AC-005 is gone and the byte-for-byte invariance assertion is intact and undiluted.\n\n### The three retry-0 fixes independently re-confirmed\n\nThe `Workspace.identity` compile-necessity argument is sound, not hand-waved: `DependencyResolver` (`callisto-model/src/discovery.rs:36`) declares only `packages`/`dependencies_of`/`dependents_of`/`diagnostics` — no `identity()` — while `identity()` is inherent on `ManifestWalkResolver` at `resolver.rs:41`. So `ws.graph.identity()` genuinely cannot compile inside the generic `plan_version`/`plan_snapshot` bodies, and the new field is required rather than redundant.\n\nEvery other citation checked out exact: CascadeInput's 9 fields at cascade.rs:141 (none named identity), 8+6=14 test literals with all 8 in cascade.rs falling after `#[cfg(test)]` at line 602, version.rs:73 / snapshot.rs:54, `native_name` at identity.rs:493, `graph.identity()` at lib.rs:109 and 116, and the bug site itself — `if d.rewrite {` at cascade.rs:259 with `name: edge.to.name().to_string(),` verbatim and the `eco` binding computed exactly as described. AC-006's path is constructible, not aspirational: `apply_version_plan` at apply.rs:108, `VersionPlan.rewrites` at plan.rs:16, `update_dependency_spec` called at apply.rs:166 and 227.\n\n### Two things I considered and deliberately did not block on\n\nRecording these so a future gate doesn't re-litigate them:\n\n1. AC-004 names \"the cascade/rewrite test suite\" while its exception clause (b) covers files outside that suite — a category imprecision, but the clause is permissive rather than restrictive and every required edit is enumerated exactly.\n2. No AC asserts the other six suites still *pass* (AC-005 only asserts they compile). I traced this rather than assuming: the sole reader of `Workspace.identity` is the CascadeInput construction, and an empty `IdentityIndex::default()` makes `native_name` return `None`, falling through to the byte-identical pre-fix expression. Behavior in those suites provably cannot change.\n\nNeither would force a drafter to ask a clarifying question or an implementer to guess at intent. Failing on them would be gate theater. No condition was relaxed to reach this pass — the spec is cleared for planning.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>65823</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>19</tool_uses><duration_ms>434891</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
