ot delegate to another agent.\n\nThis spec passed canon-exit-gate on its 3rd attempt after unusually heavy adversarial review — trust its api_surface section's mechanism descriptions as precisely accurate (exact line numbers, exact 18-site enumeration for Workspace struct literals, exact reasoning for why a real Workspace.identity field is required rather than a direct ws.graph.identity() call), but still verify each claim against the live code yourself before writing each task's failing test, since code can drift even between a passing gate and planning.\n\nKey implementation shape from the spec's api_surface (for your own orientation): (1) CascadeInput (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs) gains an `identity: &'a IdentityIndex` field; (2) Workspace<'a, R, D> (crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs) gains an owned `identity: IdentityIndex` field, populated inside Workspace::load's existing non-generic-over-D impl block via `graph.identity().clone()`; (3) solve_cascade's RewriteKey construction (cascade.rs, inside the `if d.rewrite` block) changes `name: edge.to.name().to_string()` to `name: input.identity.native_name(&edge.to, eco).map(str::to_string).unwrap_or_else(|| edge.to.name().to_string())`; (4) both real CascadeInput construction sites (commands/version.rs, commands/snapshot.rs) supply `identity: &ws.identity`; (5) 14 test-only CascadeInput literals (8 in cascade.rs's own test module, 6 in tests/cascade_tests.rs) need an `identity` field added; (6) 18 hand-constructed Workspace struct literals across 6 test files (validate_command_tests.rs, snapshot_tests.rs, matrix_tests.rs, graph_tests.rs, tags_tests.rs, publish_tests.rs — exact line numbers are in the spec's scope field) need an `identity` field added.\n\nSequence tasks by dependency: the Workspace.identity field addition (and its 18 test-site fixups) is independent of the CascadeInput.identity field addition (and its 14 test-site fixups) by file, but the RewriteKey-construction fix and the two real CascadeInput construction sites both depend on BOTH fields existing (Workspace.identity to read from, CascadeInput.identity to write into). No task should exceed 15 minutes — this likely means: one task for Workspace.identity + its 18 test-site fixups (mechanical, same pattern repeated), one task for CascadeInput.identity + its 14 test-site fixups (mechanical, same pattern), one task for the two real construction sites + the RewriteKey fix itself (these are tightly coupled — the fix is meaningless without both fields wired in), then separate tasks proving AC-001/AC-002 (dual-identity cross-ecosystem rewrite), AC-003 (None-fallback), AC-004 (regression-proof), AC-006 (end-to-end apply_version_plan success), AC-007 (Bare-target fallback). Every acceptance criterion (AC-001 through AC-007) must appear in at least one task's covers_criteria.\n\nOutput the plan@1 object directly in your response (the calling process will persist it to .claude/plans/ and pass it through vector-challenger before implementation begins).","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/ae76f80186b6c8c09.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bb7ff0c2-38f9-4949-a6d9-67f4f8925b88","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
