{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T10:10:01.579Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae76f80186b6c8c09</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/ae76f80186b6c8c09.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Plan Track 9 rewrite-key implementation\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All 6 confirmed. Here is the complete plan@1.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"goal\": \"Fix solve_cascade's RewriteKey.name construction to use the dependent manifest's own ecosystem-native identity (via a newly threaded IdentityIndex) instead of PackageId::name(), so dual-identity cross-ecosystem rewrite targets resolve to the correct dependency-manifest key and apply_version_plan no longer aborts with DependencyNotFound.\",\n  \"architecture\": \"Thread identity: &amp;'a IdentityIndex through CascadeInput and an owned identity: IdentityIndex through Workspace (populated once in Workspace::load from graph.identity()), following the exact precedent of Track 1's tags: &amp;TagIndex field. Both fields are added as scaffolding first, with mechanical fixups at every existing struct-literal construction site, then solve_cascade's single RewriteKey.name expression is changed to look up input.identity.native_name(&amp;edge.to, eco) with a PackageId::name() fallback when no cross-ecosystem registration exists. Verification proceeds bottom-up: a dual-identity test and a fallback/regression test through the real run_cascade call path, a full-suite regression pass, and a real on-disk end-to-end apply_version_plan test.\",\n  \"tech_stack\": [\"Rust\", \"cargo\", \"callisto-graph crate\", \"callisto-model crate\"],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK9-CASCADE-REWRITE-KEY-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"spec_file_path\": \".claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK9-CASCADE-REWRITE-KEY-CORRECTNESS.json\",\n  \"spec_hash\": \"sha256:d4575f86242b4a8d0b1ffe6529e42a64d171b929c8d776153fbff1c7f4101199\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T1\",\n      \"title\": \"Add Workspace.identity field, populate at load time, fix 18 test-literal sites\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"modify\": [\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs\",\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/ecosystem_bugs_test.rs\",\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/validate_command_tests.rs\",\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/snapshot_tests.rs\",\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/matrix_tests.rs\",\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/graph_tests.rs\",\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tags_tests.rs\",\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\"\n        ],\n        \"test\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/tests/ecosystem_bugs_test.rs\"]\n      },\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"RED: append this new test function to the end of crates/callisto-graph/tests/ecosystem_bugs_test.rs (after the file's final closing brace, currently line 328):\\n```rust\\n#[test]\\nfn workspace_load_populates_identity_field_from_graph_identity() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    git_init(root);\\n\\n    fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"solo-crate\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"0.1.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let runner = NoopRunner;\\n\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &amp;locator, &amp;runner)\\n        .expect(\\\"workspace should load\\\");\\n\\n    use callisto_model::Ecosystem;\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        ws.identity.native.get(&amp;(Ecosystem::Cargo, \\\"solo-crate\\\".to_string())),\\n        Some(&amp;PackageId::parse(\\\"solo-crate\\\").unwrap()),\\n        \\\"Workspace.identity must be populated from graph.identity() at load time\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n```\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test ecosystem_bugs_test workspace_load_populates_identity_field_from_graph_identity`. Expected failure: compile error `error[E0609]: no field \\\\`identity\\\\` on type \\\\`Workspace&lt;'_, NoopRunner&gt;\\\\`` (or similar 'no field identity' error), since Workspace has no identity field yet.\",\n        \"IMPLEMENT: in crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs, add a new field to the Workspace struct immediately after the existing `pub manifest_cache: RefCell&lt;BTreeMap&lt;PathBuf, Arc&lt;dyn Manifest&gt;&gt;&gt;,` field (currently the last field, line 95):\\n```rust\\n    pub identity: IdentityIndex,\\n```\\nIdentityIndex is already in scope in lib.rs via the existing `pub use identity::{IdentityIndex, IdentityResolver};` (line 44).\",\n        \"IMPLEMENT: in the same file's `impl&lt;'a, R: CommandRunner&gt; Workspace&lt;'a, R, ManifestWalkResolver&gt;` block, inside `Workspace::load`'s `Ok(Workspace { ... })` construction (currently lines 131-139), add a new field immediately after the `manifest_cache,` line:\\n```rust\\n            identity: graph.identity().clone(),\\n```\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test ecosystem_bugs_test workspace_load_populates_identity_field_from_graph_identity`. Expected: test compiles and passes (1 passed; 0 failed).\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --no-run` to surface every other site broken by the new required field. Expected failure: multiple `error[E0063]: missing field \\\\`identity\\\\` in initializer of \\\\`Workspace&lt;...&gt;\\\\`` errors, one for each of the 18 hand-constructed Workspace struct literals in: validate_command_tests.rs (lines 112, 180), snapshot_tests.rs (lines 70, 132, 183, 255), matrix_tests.rs (lines 63, 101), graph_tests.rs (line 35), tags_tests.rs (lines 62, 172, 333, 494), publish_tests.rs (lines 167, 679, 742, 974, 1342).\",\n        \"IMPLEMENT: in each of the 18 sites above, every literal ends its field list with a `manifest_cache: Default::default(),` line immediately before the literal's closing brace (confirmed by direct grep at every listed line). Insert a new line directly after that `manifest_cache: Default::default(),` line, in each of the 6 files, at every listed line number:\\n```rust\\n        identity: callisto_graph::IdentityIndex::default(),\\n```\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --no-run`. Expected: all test binaries compile with zero errors.\"\n      ],\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): add Workspace.identity field populated from graph.identity() at load time\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T2\",\n      \"title\": \"Add CascadeInput.identity field, fix 14 test literals, wire both real construction sites\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"modify\": [\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\",\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs\",\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs\"\n        ],\n        \"test\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\"]\n      },\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T1\"],\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"RED: add this new test function to crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` block, immediately after the `caret_covers_excludes_prerelease_versions` test (currently ending at line 709, right before the `struct TwoPackageGraph` declaration at line 711):\\n```rust\\n#[test]\\nfn cascade_input_accepts_identity_field() {\\n    let graph = TwoPackageGraph { packages: vec![] };\\n    let groups = GroupTable::default();\\n    let cfg = CascadeConfig {\\n        mode: CascadeMode::OutOfRange,\\n        bump_severity: CascadeBumpSeverity::Patch,\\n        peer_escalation: true,\\n        preserve_npm_ranges: false,\\n    };\\n    let seed = BTreeMap::new();\\n    let reasons = BTreeMap::new();\\n    let named_by = BTreeMap::new();\\n    let base = BTreeMap::new();\\n    let identity = IdentityIndex::default();\\n\\n    let input = CascadeInput {\\n        graph: &amp;graph,\\n        groups: &amp;groups,\\n        cfg: &amp;cfg,\\n        seed: &amp;seed,\\n        reasons: &amp;reasons,\\n        named_by: &amp;named_by,\\n        base: &amp;base,\\n        pre: None,\\n        tags: &amp;TagIndex::empty(),\\n        identity: &amp;identity,\\n    };\\n\\n    assert!(input.identity.native.is_empty());\\n}\\n```\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib cascade::tests::cascade_input_accepts_identity_field`. Expected failure: compile error `error[E0560]: struct \\\\`CascadeInput\\\\` has no field named \\\\`identity\\\\`` (or `error[E0609]`), since CascadeInput has no identity field yet.\",\n        \"IMPLEMENT: in crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, add `use crate::identity::IdentityIndex;` to the top-of-file imports, immediately after `use crate::error::GraphError;` (line 11).\",\n        \"IMPLEMENT: in the same file's `CascadeInput&lt;'a, D: DependencyResolver&gt;` struct (lines 141-151), add a new field immediately after `pub tags: &amp;'a TagIndex,` (line 150):\\n```rust\\n    pub identity: &amp;'a IdentityIndex,\\n```\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib cascade::tests::cascade_input_accepts_identity_field`. Expected: still fails to compile, now with `error[E0063]: missing field \\\\`identity\\\\`` at every existing CascadeInput struct literal (8 in this file's own test module, plus version.rs:73 and snapshot.rs:54 once the lib target is checked).\",\n        \"IMPLEMENT: in crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs's test module, every one of the 8 existing CascadeInput literals ends its field list with `tags: &amp;TagIndex::empty(),` immediately before the closing brace, at lines 834, 916, 988, 1086, 1214, 1298, 1379, 1533. Insert a new line directly after each `tags: &amp;TagIndex::empty(),` line, at every one of those 8 locations:\\n```rust\\n            identity: &amp;IdentityIndex::default(),\\n```\",\n        \"IMPLEMENT: in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs, in plan_version's CascadeInput construction (lines 73-83), insert a new line immediately after `tags,` (line 82):\\n```rust\\n        identity: &amp;ws.identity,\\n```\",\n        \"IMPLEMENT: in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs, in plan_snapshot's CascadeInput construction (lines 54-64), insert a new line immediately after `tags,` (line 63):\\n```rust\\n        identity: &amp;ws.identity,\\n```\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib cascade::tests::cascade_input_accepts_identity_field`. Expected: compiles and passes (1 passed; 0 failed) -- this also confirms AC-005's compile-based proposition holds for the library target.\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --no-run`. Expected failure: `error[E0063]: missing field \\\\`identity\\\\`` at the 6 CascadeInput struct literals in crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs, lines 49, 143, 199, 262, 329, 417.\",\n        \"IMPLEMENT: in crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs, add `use callisto_graph::IdentityIndex;` to the top-of-file imports, immediately after `use callisto_graph::TagIndex;` (line 6). Then, at each of the 6 literals (every one ends its field list with `tags: &amp;TagIndex::empty(),` at lines 58, 152, 208, 271, 338, 426), insert a new line directly after that line:\\n```rust\\n    identity: &amp;IdentityIndex::default(),\\n```\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --no-run`. Expected: all test binaries compile with zero errors. This confirms AC-005 in full: the crate fails to compile if either real construction site or the Workspace field is missing, and now compiles because all are present.\"\n      ],\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): add CascadeInput.identity field and wire it from Workspace.identity at both real construction sites\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-005\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T3\",\n      \"title\": \"Fix RewriteKey.name to use the dependent's ecosystem-native identity (AC-001, AC-002)\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"modify\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\"],\n        \"test\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\"]\n      },\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T2\"],\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"RED: add this new test function to crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` block, immediately after `bare_package` (currently ending at line 780, right before `test_linked_group_propagates_severity_to_unseeded_member_and_converges` at line 787):\\n```rust\\n/// AC-001/AC-002: a dual-identity rewrite target registered under two\\n/// different native names per ecosystem must produce a RewriteKey whose\\n/// `name` is the name registered for the DEPENDENT's own ecosystem, not\\n/// PackageId::name() (the target's own native-ecosystem registration).\\n/// Exercised through the real run_cascade -&gt; solve_cascade call path, not a\\n/// direct, isolated call to IdentityIndex::native_name.\\n#[test]\\nfn test_dual_identity_rewrite_key_uses_dependents_ecosystem_native_name() {\\n    let dep_target = PackageId::Bare(\\\"my-native-lib\\\".to_string());\\n    let dependent = PackageId::Prefixed {\\n        ecosystem: Ecosystem::Npm,\\n        name: \\\"dep-app\\\".to_string(),\\n    };\\n\\n    let edge = DepEdge {\\n        from: dependent.clone(),\\n        to: dep_target.clone(),\\n        kind: DepKind::Runtime,\\n        spec: DepSpec::Range(\\n            callisto_model::VersionReq::parse(\\\"^1.0.0\\\", Ecosystem::Npm).unwrap(),\\n            \\\"^1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        ),\\n        from_manifest: std::path::PathBuf::from(\\\"dep-app/package.json\\\"),\\n        inherited: false,\\n    };\\n\\n    let graph = TestGraph {\\n        packages: vec![bare_package(&amp;dep_target), bare_package(&amp;dependent)],\\n        edges: vec![edge],\\n    };\\n\\n    let mut base = BTreeMap::new();\\n    base.insert(dep_target.clone(), Version::semver(1, 0, 0));\\n    base.insert(dependent.clone(), Version::semver(1, 0, 0));\\n\\n    let mut seed = BTreeMap::new();\\n    seed.insert(dep_target.clone(), Severity::Major);\\n\\n    let groups = GroupTable::default();\\n    let cfg = CascadeConfig {\\n        mode: CascadeMode::OutOfRange,\\n        bump_severity: CascadeBumpSeverity::Patch,\\n        peer_escalation: true,\\n        preserve_npm_ranges: false,\\n    };\\n    let reasons = BTreeMap::new();\\n    let named_by = BTreeMap::new();\\n\\n    let mut identity = IdentityIndex::default();\\n    identity.native.insert(\\n        (Ecosystem::Cargo, \\\"my-native-lib\\\".to_string()),\\n        dep_target.clone(),\\n    );\\n    identity.native.insert(\\n        (Ecosystem::Npm, \\\"@scope/my-native-lib\\\".to_string()),\\n        dep_target.clone(),\\n    );\\n\\n    let input = CascadeInput {\\n        graph: &amp;graph,\\n        groups: &amp;groups,\\n        cfg: &amp;cfg,\\n        seed: &amp;seed,\\n        reasons: &amp;reasons,\\n        named_by: &amp;named_by,\\n        base: &amp;base,\\n        pre: None,\\n        tags: &amp;TagIndex::empty(),\\n        identity: &amp;identity,\\n    };\\n\\n    let outcome = run_cascade(input).unwrap();\\n\\n    let rewrite = outcome\\n        .rewrites\\n        .values()\\n        .find(|r| r.dependency == dep_target)\\n        .expect(\\\"a rewrite for dep_target must be produced\\\");\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        rewrite.key.name, \\\"@scope/my-native-lib\\\",\\n        \\\"RewriteKey.name must use the Npm-native name registered for the \\\\\\n         dependent's own ecosystem, not PackageId::name() (\\\\\\\"my-native-lib\\\\\\\")\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n```\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib cascade::tests::test_dual_identity_rewrite_key_uses_dependents_ecosystem_native_name`. Expected failure: assertion failure `assertion \\\\`left == right\\\\` failed ... left: \\\"my-native-lib\\\", right: \\\"@scope/my-native-lib\\\"` -- the pre-fix code uses edge.to.name() unconditionally.\",\n        \"IMPLEMENT: in crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, inside solve_cascade's `if d.rewrite { ... }` block, replace the RewriteKey construction's `name` field (line 277) from:\\n```rust\\n                                name: edge.to.name().to_string(),\\n```\\nto:\\n```rust\\n                                name: input\\n                                    .identity\\n                                    .native_name(&amp;edge.to, eco)\\n                                    .map(str::to_string)\\n                                    .unwrap_or_else(|| edge.to.name().to_string()),\\n```\\nreusing the `eco` binding already computed two lines above the `match rewrite_spec(...)` call.\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib cascade::tests::test_dual_identity_rewrite_key_uses_dependents_ecosystem_native_name`. Expected: test passes (1 passed; 0 failed).\"\n      ],\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): use the dependent's ecosystem-native identity for RewriteKey.name in solve_cascade\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-001\", \"AC-002\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T4\",\n      \"title\": \"Prove the None-registration fallback is unchanged for Prefixed and Bare targets (AC-003, AC-007)\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"modify\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\"],\n        \"test\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\"]\n      },\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T3\"],\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"NOTE: this task adds no further implementation change -- the fallback behavior (`unwrap_or_else(|| edge.to.name().to_string())`) was already implemented in T3. To demonstrate genuine RED-before-GREEN for this task's own tests (not merely tests that pass on arrival), temporarily revert T3's fix by replacing the current `name: input.identity.native_name(&amp;edge.to, eco).map(str::to_string).unwrap_or_else(|| edge.to.name().to_string()),` expression back to `name: edge.to.name().to_string(),` in a local, uncommitted working-tree edit before adding the tests below -- this reversion is not itself a real behavior change since both expressions produce the identical result when no native_name registration exists, so it is safe to use purely as a RED-phase probe.\",\n        \"RED (probe): add these two test functions to crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` block, immediately after `test_dual_identity_rewrite_key_uses_dependents_ecosystem_native_name` (added in T3):\\n```rust\\n/// AC-003: when IdentityIndex::native_name(&amp;target, dependent_eco) returns\\n/// None (the common, non-dual-identity case), RewriteKey.name must equal\\n/// PackageId::name() exactly as it did before this fix, for a Prefixed\\n/// target with no registration.\\n#[test]\\nfn test_none_registration_fallback_uses_package_id_name_ac003() {\\n    let dep_target = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-core\\\").unwrap();\\n    let dependent = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-app\\\").unwrap();\\n    let edge = make_dep_edge(&amp;dependent, &amp;dep_target, \\\"^1.0.0\\\", Ecosystem::Cargo);\\n\\n    let graph = TestGraph {\\n        packages: vec![bare_package(&amp;dep_target), bare_package(&amp;dependent)],\\n        edges: vec![edge],\\n    };\\n\\n    let mut base = BTreeMap::new();\\n    base.insert(dep_target.clone(), Version::semver(1, 0, 0));\\n    base.insert(dependent.clone(), Version::semver(1, 0, 0));\\n\\n    let mut seed = BTreeMap::new();\\n    seed.insert(dep_target.clone(), Severity::Major);\\n\\n    let groups = GroupTable::default();\\n    let cfg = CascadeConfig {\\n        mode: CascadeMode::OutOfRange,\\n        bump_severity: CascadeBumpSeverity::Patch,\\n        peer_escalation: true,\\n        preserve_npm_ranges: false,\\n    };\\n    let reasons = BTreeMap::new();\\n    let named_by = BTreeMap::new();\\n    let identity = IdentityIndex::default();\\n\\n    let input = CascadeInput {\\n        graph: &amp;graph,\\n        groups: &amp;groups,\\n        cfg: &amp;cfg,\\n        seed: &amp;seed,\\n        reasons: &amp;reasons,\\n        named_by: &amp;named_by,\\n        base: &amp;base,\\n        pre: None,\\n        tags: &amp;TagIndex::empty(),\\n        identity: &amp;identity,\\n    };\\n\\n    let outcome = run_cascade(input).unwrap();\\n    let rewrite = outcome\\n        .rewrites\\n        .values()\\n        .find(|r| r.dependency == dep_target)\\n        .expect(\\\"rewrite for dep_target must be produced\\\");\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        rewrite.key.name,\\n        dep_target.name(),\\n        \\\"with no IdentityIndex.native registration, RewriteKey.name must fall back to PackageId::name()\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n/// AC-007: same fallback, exercised for a PackageId::Bare target with no\\n/// registration, confirming the Bare variant is handled identically to the\\n/// Prefixed None-registration case in AC-003.\\n#[test]\\nfn test_bare_target_with_no_registration_falls_back_to_name_ac007() {\\n    let dep_target = PackageId::Bare(\\\"foo\\\".to_string());\\n    let dependent = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-app\\\").unwrap();\\n    let edge = make_dep_edge(&amp;dependent, &amp;dep_target, \\\"^1.0.0\\\", Ecosystem::Cargo);\\n\\n    let graph = TestGraph {\\n        packages: vec![bare_package(&amp;dep_target), bare_package(&amp;dependent)],\\n        edges: vec![edge],\\n    };\\n\\n    let mut base = BTreeMap::new();\\n    base.insert(dep_target.clone(), Version::semver(1, 0, 0));\\n    base.insert(dependent.clone(), Version::semver(1, 0, 0));\\n\\n    let mut seed = BTreeMap::new();\\n    seed.insert(dep_target.clone(), Severity::Major);\\n\\n    let groups = GroupTable::default();\\n    let cfg = CascadeConfig {\\n        mode: CascadeMode::OutOfRange,\\n        bump_severity: CascadeBumpSeverity::Patch,\\n        peer_escalation: true,\\n        preserve_npm_ranges: false,\\n    };\\n    let reasons = BTreeMap::new();\\n    let named_by = BTreeMap::new();\\n    let identity = IdentityIndex::default();\\n\\n    let input = CascadeInput {\\n        graph: &amp;graph,\\n        groups: &amp;groups,\\n        cfg: &amp;cfg,\\n        seed: &amp;seed,\\n        reasons: &amp;reasons,\\n        named_by: &amp;named_by,\\n        base: &amp;base,\\n        pre: None,\\n        tags: &amp;TagIndex::empty(),\\n        identity: &amp;identity,\\n    };\\n\\n    let outcome = run_cascade(input).unwrap();\\n    let rewrite = outcome\\n        .rewrites\\n        .values()\\n        .find(|r| r.dependency == dep_target)\\n        .expect(\\\"rewrite for dep_target must be produced\\\");\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        rewrite.key.name, \\\"foo\\\",\\n        \\\"Bare target with no IdentityIndex.native registration must fall back to edge.to.name()\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n```\",\n        \"Run (with the T3 fix still reverted): `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib cascade::tests::test_none_registration_fallback_uses_package_id_name_ac003 cascade::tests::test_bare_target_with_no_registration_falls_back_to_name_ac007`. Expected: both pass even with the fix reverted, confirming these two tests genuinely exercise only the untouched fallback path (this is the expected, documented outcome for a regression-invariance probe, not a false-positive test).\",\n        \"Restore T3's fix: replace the reverted `name: edge.to.name().to_string(),` expression back to the corrected expression from T3:\\n```rust\\n                                name: input\\n                                    .identity\\n                                    .native_name(&amp;edge.to, eco)\\n                                    .map(str::to_string)\\n                                    .unwrap_or_else(|| edge.to.name().to_string()),\\n```\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib cascade::tests::test_none_registration_fallback_uses_package_id_name_ac003 cascade::tests::test_bare_target_with_no_registration_falls_back_to_name_ac007 cascade::tests::test_dual_identity_rewrite_key_uses_dependents_ecosystem_native_name`. Expected: all 3 pass (3 passed; 0 failed).\"\n      ],\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-003/AC-007 RewriteKey None-registration fallback for Prefixed and Bare targets\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-003\", \"AC-007\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T5\",\n      \"title\": \"Confirm full existing cascade/rewrite suite is byte-identical after the mechanical field additions (AC-004)\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"modify\": [],\n        \"test\": [\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\",\n          \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T4\"],\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"NOTE: this task adds no code changes. Its RED phase already occurred historically: before T1 and T2's mechanical fixups, `cargo test -p callisto-graph --no-run` failed to COMPILE across every one of the 18 Workspace and 14 CascadeInput sites (confirmed by the compile-error steps in T1 and T2). This task confirms the transition to GREEN, and confirms zero assertion changes were needed beyond the mechanical `identity` field additions themselves.\",\n        \"Run: `git diff --stat crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs` and manually confirm every changed line in these two files is either (a) an added `identity: &amp;IdentityIndex::default(),` / `identity: &amp;identity,` line from T2/T3/T4, (b) the single RewriteKey.name expression from T3, or (c) a wholly new #[test] function added in T3/T4 -- no existing assertion, existing test body, or existing RewriteKey/SpecRewrite value was altered.\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib cascade::tests`. Expected: every pre-existing test in cascade.rs's test module passes with its original assertions unchanged (e.g. `cascade_action_peer_escalation_only_fires_for_non_patch_source`, `test_linked_group_propagates_severity_to_unseeded_member_and_converges`, `test_fixed_group_seeded_siblings_converge_on_shared_target`, and the CargoWorkspaceDependency/Manifest DepWriteTarget test) -- 0 failed.\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test cascade_tests`. Expected: every pre-existing test in tests/cascade_tests.rs (including `test_blackbox_cascade_propagation` and `test_diamond_cascade_convergence`) passes with its original assertions unchanged -- 0 failed.\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph`. Expected: full crate test suite passes -- 0 failed, confirming no workspace-wide, no-dual-identity fixture anywhere in the crate produced a different RewriteKey, SpecRewrite, or manifest write than before this spec's changes.\"\n      ],\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): confirm AC-004 -- full cascade/rewrite suite is byte-identical after mechanical identity field additions\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-004\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T6\",\n      \"title\": \"Prove the real, on-disk Case D dual-identity scenario succeeds end-to-end through apply_version_plan (AC-006)\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"modify\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/tests/version_tests.rs\"],\n        \"test\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/tests/version_tests.rs\"]\n      },\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T4\"],\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"IMPLEMENT (imports): at the top of crates/callisto-graph/tests/version_tests.rs, change `use callisto_model::{CommandError, CommandOutput, CommandRunner, PackageId, Severity};` to add `ApplyPermit`:\\n```rust\\nuse callisto_model::{ApplyPermit, CommandError, CommandOutput, CommandRunner, PackageId, Severity};\\n```\\nand add a new import line immediately below the existing `use callisto_graph::Workspace;` line:\\n```rust\\nuse callisto_graph::{apply_version_plan, ApplyOptions};\\n```\",\n        \"RED (probe): before adding the test, temporarily revert T3's fix in crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs back to `name: edge.to.name().to_string(),` (uncommitted working-tree edit) to prove this new integration test genuinely fails against the pre-fix behavior described in the spec's AC-006.\",\n        \"RED: append this new test function to the end of crates/callisto-graph/tests/version_tests.rs (after the file's final closing brace, currently line 158):\\n```rust\\n/// AC-006: the real, on-disk Cargo+npm co-located dual-identity scenario\\n/// from the originating bug report -- a Cargo crate that is also its own\\n/// napi-rs npm package (Case D: same directory, two manifests, one owning\\n/// Bare PackageId since there is no naming collision elsewhere) -- must\\n/// proceed through apply_version_plan to a successful completion for a\\n/// cross-ecosystem npm dependent whose spec needs rewriting, with the\\n/// dependent's package.json mutated to keep the correct, already-in-use\\n/// dependency key. Before the fix, this aborts with\\n/// Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound) because solve_cascade constructs\\n/// the wrong key (\\\"my-native-lib\\\", the Cargo-native name) against a\\n/// manifest that only has an \\\"@scope/my-native-lib\\\" entry.\\n#[test]\\nfn apply_version_plan_succeeds_for_dual_identity_cross_ecosystem_rewrite_ac006() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    git_init_with_commit(root);\\n\\n    fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"crates/my-native-lib\\\")).unwrap();\\n    fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"crates/my-native-lib/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"my-native-lib\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\nedition = \\\\\\\"2021\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"crates/my-native-lib/package.json\\\"),\\n        r#\\\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"@scope/my-native-lib\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"1.0.0\\\"}\\\"#,\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"packages/dep-app\\\")).unwrap();\\n    fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"packages/dep-app/package.json\\\"),\\n        r#\\\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"dep-app\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"1.0.0\\\",\\\"dependencies\\\":{\\\"@scope/my-native-lib\\\":\\\"^1.0.0\\\"}}\\\"#,\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\".changeset\\\")).unwrap();\\n    fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\".changeset/breaking-native-api.md\\\"),\\n        \\\"---\\\\n\\\\\\\"my-native-lib\\\\\\\": major\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nBreaking native API change.\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let runner = NoopRunner;\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &amp;locator, &amp;runner)\\n        .expect(\\\"workspace with Case D dual-identity package should load\\\");\\n\\n    let inference = NoInference;\\n    let opts = VersionOptions {\\n        strict: false,\\n        strict_graph: false,\\n        allow_empty_changesets: true,\\n    };\\n    let plan = plan_version(&amp;ws, &amp;inference, &amp;opts).expect(\\\"plan_version should succeed\\\");\\n\\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\\n    let apply_opts = ApplyOptions::default();\\n    let outcome = apply_version_plan(root, &amp;plan, &amp;runner, &amp;apply_opts, &amp;permit);\\n\\n    assert!(\\n        outcome.is_ok(),\\n        \\\"apply_version_plan must succeed for the dual-identity cross-ecosystem rewrite (AC-006); got: {:?}\\\",\\n        outcome.err()\\n    );\\n\\n    let dep_app_manifest =\\n        fs::read_to_string(root.join(\\\"packages/dep-app/package.json\\\")).unwrap();\\n    assert!(\\n        dep_app_manifest.contains(\\\"\\\\\\\"@scope/my-native-lib\\\\\\\"\\\"),\\n        \\\"dep-app's package.json must retain the ecosystem-native dependency key \\\\\\\"@scope/my-native-lib\\\\\\\"; got:\\\\n{dep_app_manifest}\\\"\\n    );\\n    assert!(\\n        !dep_app_manifest.contains(\\\"\\\\\\\"^1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\"),\\n        \\\"dep-app's dependency spec on my-native-lib must have been rewritten away from the now out-of-range \\\\\\\"^1.0.0\\\\\\\"; got:\\\\n{dep_app_manifest}\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n```\",\n        \"Run (with T3's fix still reverted): `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test version_tests apply_version_plan_succeeds_for_dual_identity_cross_ecosystem_rewrite_ac006`. Expected failure: `apply_version_plan must succeed ... got: Some(ManifestError(DependencyNotFound { ... }))` (or the assertion panics with that error printed), confirming this reproduces the exact originating bug.\",\n        \"Restore T3's fix in crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs (replace the reverted expression back to `name: input.identity.native_name(&amp;edge.to, eco).map(str::to_string).unwrap_or_else(|| edge.to.name().to_string()),`).\",\n        \"Run: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --test version_tests apply_version_plan_succeeds_for_dual_identity_cross_ecosystem_rewrite_ac006`. Expected: test passes (1 passed; 0 failed).\"\n      ],\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): prove AC-006 end-to-end apply_version_plan success for a real on-disk dual-identity Case D rewrite\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-006\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"batches\": [\n    {\n      \"batch_id\": \"B1\",\n      \"title\": \"Scaffolding: field threading and mechanical fixups\",\n      \"target_crate\": \"callisto-graph\",\n      \"task_ids\": [\"T1\", \"T2\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"batch_id\": \"B2\",\n      \"title\": \"The fix and its acceptance-criteria proofs\",\n      \"target_crate\": \"callisto-graph\",\n      \"task_ids\": [\"T3\", \"T4\", \"T5\", \"T6\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nEvery acceptance criterion (AC-001 through AC-007) appears in exactly one task's `covers_criteria` (T2→AC-005, T3→AC-001/AC-002, T4→AC-003/AC-007, T5→AC-004, T6→AC-006). All file paths and line numbers were verified directly against the live repository (not merely trusted from the spec) before being written into task steps: `crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs`, and the six test files listed in the spec's `scope`. The calling process should persist this object to `.claude/plans/` and route it to `vector:challenger` next.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>148995</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>66</tool_uses><duration_ms>757351</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
